SCVMC operates a main campus in San Jose and coordinates a network of Valley Health Centers across the county, ensuring accessible care for all residents. The organization is strongly committed to serving a multilingual and multicultural population, offering extensive language assistance services and resources to help patients navigate financial and social needs. By integrating education, research, and a model of care that addresses the whole person, Santa Clara Valley Medical Center strives to be a trusted partner in the health and well-being of every community member it serves.', '751 S. Bascom Ave., San Jose, CA 95128', 'San Jose', 'CA', '95128', '(408) 885-5000', ARRAY['English', 'Vietnamese', 'Tagalog', 'Simplified Chinese', 'Traditional Chinese', 'Farsi', 'Punjabi', 'Spanish']::text[], 'Hospital', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/santa-clara-valley-medical-center-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/santa-clara-valley-medical-center-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/santa-clara-valley-medical-center-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/santa-clara-valley-medical-center-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/santa-clara-valley-medical-center-google-5.webp", "https://scvmc.scvh.org/favicon.ico"], "rating": 2.9, "reviews": [{"date": "2025-11-17T09:12:03.801411814Z", "text": "Santa Clara Valley Medical Center has been part of our family’s medical journey for years, offering both emergency and general care when it mattered most. One of the Whopper families received urgent treatment here, and while the staff moved quickly and professionally, the wait times and communication gaps were noticeable during peak hours. The general care wings are clean and well-equipped, but the scale of the facility can feel overwhelming without a strong advocate present.\n\nFrom a broader lens, SCVMC could easily anchor a capstone project in public health or healthcare administration. Topics like emergency throughput, patient navigation, or county-level resource allocation would be relevant and timely. The indoor garden area stands out—a rare pocket of calm that reminds you healing isn’t just clinical. For families and students alike, this place reflects both the strengths and limits of public infrastructure in a high-demand region.", "author": "Jonathan Phan", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102451632647716590904/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-01T04:25:17.636455136Z", "text": "This review is for their trauma center, and post trauma medical care.\n\nI should have written a review much sooner. In July 2023 my ex wife became concerned after not hearing from me for an extended period of time. She drove from Aptos to Los Gatos where she found me siezing on the floor, where I probably had been for some time.\n\nI was transported to the trauma center at Santa Clara Valley Medical Center, and arrived in status epilepticus. I remained in ICU for nearly 3 days before being transferred to a room for additional care.\n\nI''m convinced that if not for the well trained team in that ICU I wouldn''t be here to write this today. The care I received after being moved to a room for additional care was also the best of the best.\n\nHopefully you will never need the services of a trauma center. If you do you can find yourself in no better hands than this one.", "author": "Scott Ringgold", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107224675248012860759/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-31T13:04:31.081651994Z", "text": "Go anywhere else! This Hospital is run down, with stained floors and water leak stains on the ceiling.  The staff is sub par.  The Nurses staff blamed each other every time a request was missed.  Went in for acute Bronchitis. Was never given oxygen through a cannula. My dog’s Veterinarian could have given me better care.  Will avoid at all costs in the future.", "author": "A. Kelsey", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115434370475824411929/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-13T06:49:28.023532045Z", "text": "Santa Clara Medical Center “Express Care” is hands down one of the most creatively named places I’ve ever visited, because there is absolutely nothing express about it.\nI spent hours waiting outside, only to finally be escorted into a room where they closed the door behind me and apparently forgot I existed. No updates. No communication. No “we’re running behind.” Nothing. Just silence, fluorescent lighting, and the slow collapse of my patience.\nAt this point I genuinely think the room was not for treatment — it was for storage. I’ve had Amazon packages checked on more frequently than I was here.\nI understand hospitals get busy. What I don’t understand is how basic communication completely disappears. A simple update would’ve gone a long way. Instead, I was left wondering whether I was waiting for medical care or participating in a social experiment about human endurance.\nIf you plan on coming here, make sure to:\neat beforehand\nbring a phone charger\nnotify loved ones\npossibly update your will\nCalling this place “Express Care” feels less like branding and more like satire. The only thing moving quickly here is your descent into frustration.\nOne thing I am certain of is that they will never have to worry about seeing my face here again. I can promise them that much.\nI came in needing medical attention and left with a deeper understanding of eternity.", "author": "Jesse Robledo", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117054753249979456473/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-29T18:11:24.836894648Z", "text": "In 2021, I had surgery at this hospital after breaking my ankle. I was extremely nervous going in, especially after reading some of the reviews, but I remained hopeful. Unfortunately, my experience was very mixed.\n\nDuring surgery, I was told I had complications specifically, an asthma attack. However, this information was never communicated to me directly. My caretaker had to call the hospital after waiting over six hours (the estimated surgery time) to find out what was happening. My surgery ended up taking nearly eight hours. On a positive note, the orthopedic surgeons there were three of them did an excellent job on my ankle itself. Y’all get a 4.5/5.\n\nAfter surgery, I was given a PCA pump attached to my operated leg. When I woke up, a nurse roughly started dressing me before I was fully awake or aware of what was happening. Another nurse had to step in and warn her to be careful with the PCA pump. Unfortunately, the first nurse was so rough that she disconnected it (dummy). When I got home, I realized the medication was leaking out instead of delivering pain relief.\n\nMy caretaker took me back to the hospital, and the experience in the ER was awful. I was in severe pain and very vocal about it, but some of the nurses made fun of me and questioned whether I was “really in that much pain.” I had just undergone an eight-hour surgery and had no effective pain control. Eventually, one kind nurse came to check on me, apologized for her colleagues’ behavior, and gave me something stronger that finally helped.\n\nWhile I was in the ER, I overheard nurses discussing another patient’s private medical information  they loudly stated that the woman next to me had tested positive for COVID. Later, I woke up to a male nurse entering my room with a COVID swab. When I asked if I was being tested, he hesitated and said he was in the “wrong room.” There was no prep table or any indication that a test had been ordered for me, and the situation made me feel very uncomfortable and uneasy.\n\nOverall, while I’m grateful to the orthopedic surgeons and the 1 kind nurse I encountered, my overall experience was extremely disappointing. Communication, professionalism, and patient care were severely lacking in many areas. I would strongly caution others to consider other hospitals if possible.", "author": "Bee Bee", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108368222135476517886/reviews"}], "website": "https://scvmc.scvh.org/home", "location": {"latitude": 37.3139499, "longitude": -121.9340007}, "services": ["Birth Center", "Burn Center", "Emergency Department", "Rehabilitation Center", "Neurosurgery", "Orthopedic Surgery", "Pediatrics", "Sobrato Cancer Center", "Trauma Center", "Women''s Health", "Urgent Care Clinics", "Center for Digestive and Liver Health", "Post Acute Care Transition (PACT) Program"], "insurance": {"notes": "The page mentions ''Help Paying Your Bill'' and ''Financial Help for Healthcare'' programs, and references a ''Price Transparency & Cost Estimator'' page. No specific insurance networks are listed on this page. An Anthem Blue Cross network update is noted on the page.", "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": ["Blue Cross Blue Shield"], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": true}, "highlights": [{"title": "Comprehensive Care", "detail": "Full range of services from primary care to advanced specialties including a Level I Trauma Center, Burn Center, and the Sobrato Cancer Center.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Centers of Excellence", "detail": "Six specialized centers for burn care, digestive and liver health, pediatrics, rehabilitation, cancer, trauma, and women''s health.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Language Assistance", "detail": "Free language assistance services available in multiple languages including Spanish, Tagalog, Vietnamese, Chinese, and more.", "category": "culture"}, {"title": "Financial Help Available", "detail": "Resources and programs to help patients pay their bills and find healthcare coverage, including the Healthcare Access Program (HAP).", "category": "insurance"}, {"title": "Easy Appointment Scheduling", "detail": "Schedule appointments by calling Valley Connection at (888) 334-1000 or through myHealth Online.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Award-Winning Care", "detail": "Recognized with numerous awards and accreditations for outstanding patient care and service.", "category": "reviews"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://scvmc.scvh.org/home", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": null, "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": true, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": true, "scout_query": "Vietnamese speaking hospital in the United States", "search_text": "hospital | english | vietnamese | tiếng việt | người việt | bác sĩ việt | tagalog | simplified chinese | traditional chinese | farsi | punjabi | spanish | birth center | burn center | emergency department | rehabilitation center | neurosurgery | orthopedic surgery | pediatrics | sobrato cancer center | trauma center | women''s health | urgent care clinics | center for digestive and liver health | post acute care transition (pact) program | specialty | emergency | primary care | urgent care | care coordination | blue cross blue shield", "google_types": ["hospital", "medical_lab", "medical_clinic", "doctor", "health", "point_of_interest", "service", "establishment"], "open_weekend": true, "rating_count": 1035, "language_note": "Santa Clara Valley Medical Center provides language assistance services in multiple languages including Spanish, Tagalog, Vietnamese, Farsi, Punjabi, Simplified Chinese, and Traditional Chinese, demonstrating a commitment to serving a diverse, multicultural community in Santa Clara County.", "open_saturday": true, "quality_score": 95, "working_hours": {"friday": "Open 24 hours", "monday": "Open 24 hours", "sunday": "Open 24 hours", "tuesday": "Open 24 hours", "saturday": "Open 24 hours", "thursday": "Open 24 hours", "wednesday": "Open 24 hours"}, "gallery_images": ["https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1341/styles/gallery_1920x640/s3/2024-09/hero-image-004.jpg.webp?VersionId=CH9lZPzpmZK..g9B63xbEU_MDUiTHwpl&itok=1WhrRUts", "https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1341/styles/wide_832/s3/migrated/find-a-provider.jpg.webp?VersionId=ga0fyAlFw5kFzneSIQdbvviNX5Npi0j2&itok=wgq_MGXf", "https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1341/styles/wide_832/s3/2024-11/valley.png.webp?VersionId=1Xs2.wotqhaBh62ZOkVxaftRscmtiobO&itok=qgLUOFpD", "https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1341/styles/wide_850/s3/migrated/Top%20reasons%20to%20choose%20VMC%20750x421.jpg.webp?VersionId=QE0tJYqvBAhAmj6HNjbhYEomGuzPnwL9&itok=nux1MrGD", "https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1341/styles/card_horizontal_816x544/s3/migrated/awards.jpg.webp?VersionId=GFWRD3NeRPnAJnBBB6XcPyKnyQmb33nX&itok=JUMQYPuN", "https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1341/styles/card_horizontal_816x544/s3/2024-11/research.jpg.webp?VersionId=Po50pPsl2JO591LcG.QN38sV956Z2qTj&itok=B9DqdPnU", "https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1341/styles/card_horizontal_816x544/s3/migrated/daisy_awards_main.jpg.webp?VersionId=J_yU9WDBs5qjRuyGVwDEMmS8dmzHn2pt&itok=oMSginrZ", "https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1341/styles/wide_850/s3/migrated/Rehab%20Center%20Care%20Team%20Story-100.jpg.webp?VersionId=nJKjISjc3eWJQ0ZBfsQhUPc.LUUmhJPC&itok=K24pDrJx"], "review_profile": {"rating": 2.9, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Mixed", "summary_quote": "Some reviewers highlight well-trained, professional staff, while others describe subpar and uncommunicative interactions."}, {"theme": "Facility Environment", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Multiple reviews mention run-down conditions, stained floors, and water leak stains on ceilings."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Several patients report significant communication gaps, including lack of updates during long waits and post-surgery information not being shared directly."}, {"theme": "Treatment Outcomes", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Trauma care and surgical outcomes receive high praise, with one reviewer crediting the ICU team for saving their life."}, {"theme": "Wait Times", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Long wait times are a common complaint, with one patient describing the ''Express Care'' as anything but express."}], "summary": "Santa Clara Valley Medical Center receives mixed reviews, with some patients praising the trauma care and surgical expertise, while others criticize long wait times, poor communication, and facility conditions.", "review_count": 1035, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2025-11-17T09:12:03.801411814Z", "text": "Santa Clara Valley Medical Center has been part of our family’s medical journey for years, offering both emergency and general care when it mattered most. One of the Whopper families received urgent treatment here, and while the staff moved quickly and professionally, the wait times and communication gaps were noticeable during peak hours. The general care wings are clean and well-equipped, but the scale of the facility can feel overwhelming without a strong advocate present.\n\nFrom a broader lens, SCVMC could easily anchor a capstone project in public health or healthcare administration. Topics like emergency throughput, patient navigation, or county-level resource allocation would be relevant and timely. The indoor garden area stands out—a rare pocket of calm that reminds you healing isn’t just clinical. For families and students alike, this place reflects both the strengths and limits of public infrastructure in a high-demand region.", "author": "Jonathan Phan", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102451632647716590904/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-01T04:25:17.636455136Z", "text": "This review is for their trauma center, and post trauma medical care.\n\nI should have written a review much sooner. In July 2023 my ex wife became concerned after not hearing from me for an extended period of time. She drove from Aptos to Los Gatos where she found me siezing on the floor, where I probably had been for some time.\n\nI was transported to the trauma center at Santa Clara Valley Medical Center, and arrived in status epilepticus. I remained in ICU for nearly 3 days before being transferred to a room for additional care.\n\nI''m convinced that if not for the well trained team in that ICU I wouldn''t be here to write this today. The care I received after being moved to a room for additional care was also the best of the best.\n\nHopefully you will never need the services of a trauma center. If you do you can find yourself in no better hands than this one.", "author": "Scott Ringgold", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107224675248012860759/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-31T13:04:31.081651994Z", "text": "Go anywhere else! This Hospital is run down, with stained floors and water leak stains on the ceiling.  The staff is sub par.  The Nurses staff blamed each other every time a request was missed.  Went in for acute Bronchitis. Was never given oxygen through a cannula. My dog’s Veterinarian could have given me better care.  Will avoid at all costs in the future.", "author": "A. Kelsey", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115434370475824411929/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-13T06:49:28.023532045Z", "text": "Santa Clara Medical Center “Express Care” is hands down one of the most creatively named places I’ve ever visited, because there is absolutely nothing express about it.\nI spent hours waiting outside, only to finally be escorted into a room where they closed the door behind me and apparently forgot I existed. No updates. No communication. No “we’re running behind.” Nothing. Just silence, fluorescent lighting, and the slow collapse of my patience.\nAt this point I genuinely think the room was not for treatment — it was for storage. I’ve had Amazon packages checked on more frequently than I was here.\nI understand hospitals get busy. What I don’t understand is how basic communication completely disappears. A simple update would’ve gone a long way. Instead, I was left wondering whether I was waiting for medical care or participating in a social experiment about human endurance.\nIf you plan on coming here, make sure to:\neat beforehand\nbring a phone charger\nnotify loved ones\npossibly update your will\nCalling this place “Express Care” feels less like branding and more like satire. The only thing moving quickly here is your descent into frustration.\nOne thing I am certain of is that they will never have to worry about seeing my face here again. I can promise them that much.\nI came in needing medical attention and left with a deeper understanding of eternity.", "author": "Jesse Robledo", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117054753249979456473/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-29T18:11:24.836894648Z", "text": "In 2021, I had surgery at this hospital after breaking my ankle. I was extremely nervous going in, especially after reading some of the reviews, but I remained hopeful. Unfortunately, my experience was very mixed.\n\nDuring surgery, I was told I had complications specifically, an asthma attack. However, this information was never communicated to me directly. My caretaker had to call the hospital after waiting over six hours (the estimated surgery time) to find out what was happening. My surgery ended up taking nearly eight hours. On a positive note, the orthopedic surgeons there were three of them did an excellent job on my ankle itself. Y’all get a 4.5/5.\n\nAfter surgery, I was given a PCA pump attached to my operated leg. When I woke up, a nurse roughly started dressing me before I was fully awake or aware of what was happening. Another nurse had to step in and warn her to be careful with the PCA pump. Unfortunately, the first nurse was so rough that she disconnected it (dummy). When I got home, I realized the medication was leaking out instead of delivering pain relief.\n\nMy caretaker took me back to the hospital, and the experience in the ER was awful. I was in severe pain and very vocal about it, but some of the nurses made fun of me and questioned whether I was “really in that much pain.” I had just undergone an eight-hour surgery and had no effective pain control. Eventually, one kind nurse came to check on me, apologized for her colleagues’ behavior, and gave me something stronger that finally helped.\n\nWhile I was in the ER, I overheard nurses discussing another patient’s private medical information  they loudly stated that the woman next to me had tested positive for COVID. Later, I woke up to a male nurse entering my room with a COVID swab. When I asked if I was being tested, he hesitated and said he was in the “wrong room.” There was no prep table or any indication that a test had been ordered for me, and the situation made me feel very uncomfortable and uneasy.\n\nOverall, while I’m grateful to the orthopedic surgeons and the 1 kind nurse I encountered, my overall experience was extremely disappointing. Communication, professionalism, and patient care were severely lacking in many areas. I would strongly caution others to consider other hospitals if possible.", "author": "Bee Bee", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108368222135476517886/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Santa Clara Valley Medical Center receives mixed reviews, with some patients praising the trauma care and surgical expertise, while others criticize long wait times, poor communication, and facility conditions.", "about_highlight": "Santa Clara Valley Medical Center (SCVMC) is a public, teaching hospital and health system dedicated to serving the diverse community of Santa Clara County. As a cornerstone of Santa Clara Valley Healthcare, it provides a comprehensive range of medical services from primary and urgent care to advanced specialty care in areas such as burn treatment, trauma, cancer, rehabilitation, and women''s health. The medical center is recognized for its commitment to innovative research, community-based care, and clinical excellence, underscored by numerous awards and accreditations. With a focus on compassionate, patient-centered care, SCVMC aims to elevate healthcare by combining cutting-edge treatments with a deep-rooted sense of community responsibility.\n\nSCVMC operates a main campus in San Jose and coordinates a network of Valley Health Centers across the county, ensuring accessible care for all residents. The organization is strongly committed to serving a multilingual and multicultural population, offering extensive language assistance services and resources to help patients navigate financial and social needs. By integrating education, research, and a model of care that addresses the whole person, Santa Clara Valley Medical Center strives to be a trusted partner in the health and well-being of every community member it serves.", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=16193186071065437632&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJ54JcoTHLj4ARwKWou-_AueA", "important_links": [{"url": "https://www.cloudflare.com?utm_source=challenge&utm_campaign=m", "text": "Cloudflare"}, {"url": "https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/", "text": "Privacy"}], "quality_missing": ["team_members", "appointment_url"], "search_keywords": ["hospital", "english", "vietnamese", "tiếng việt", "người việt", "bác sĩ việt", "tagalog", "simplified chinese", "traditional chinese", "farsi", "punjabi", "spanish", "birth center", "burn center", "emergency department", "rehabilitation center", "neurosurgery", "orthopedic surgery", "pediatrics", "sobrato cancer center", "trauma center", "women''s health", "urgent care clinics", "center for digestive and liver health", "post acute care transition (pact) program", "specialty", "emergency", "primary care", "urgent care", "care coordination", "blue cross blue shield"], "cultural_context": "Santa Clara Valley Medical Center provides language assistance services in multiple languages including Spanish, Tagalog, Vietnamese, Farsi, Punjabi, Simplified Chinese, and Traditional Chinese, demonstrating a commitment to serving a diverse, multicultural community in Santa Clara County.", "services_offered": [{"name": "Birth Center", "category": "Women''s Health", "description": "Comprehensive maternity and childbirth services.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Burn Center", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Specialized care for burn injuries, one of six Centers of Excellence.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Emergency Department", "category": "Emergency", "description": "24/7 emergency medical services for urgent and life-threatening conditions.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Rehabilitation Center", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Physical and occupational therapy and rehabilitation services.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Neurosurgery", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Advanced surgical care for conditions affecting the brain and nervous system.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Orthopedic Surgery", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Surgical and non-surgical treatment for musculoskeletal issues.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Pediatrics", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Comprehensive healthcare for infants, children, and adolescents.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Sobrato Cancer Center", "category": "Specialty", "description": "A full-service cancer treatment center offering advanced therapies and support.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Trauma Center", "category": "Emergency", "description": "Level I trauma center providing the highest level of surgical care for traumatic injuries.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Women''s Health", "category": "Women''s Health", "description": "Comprehensive medical services for women, including gynecology and obstetric care.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Urgent Care Clinics", "category": "Urgent Care", "description": "Walk-in care for non-life-threatening illnesses and injuries at multiple locations.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Center for Digestive and Liver Health", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Specialized care for digestive and liver conditions.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Post Acute Care Transition (PACT) Program", "category": "Care Coordination", "description": "Support for patients transitioning from hospital to home or other care settings.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}], "short_description": "Santa Clara Valley Medical Center is a community-based public teaching hospital providing comprehensive and innovative healthcare services to all residents of Santa Clara County.", "google_website_url": "https://scvmc.scvh.org/home", "insurance_accepted": ["Blue Cross Blue Shield"], "google_primary_type": "Hospital", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "751 S Bascom Ave, San Jose, CA 95128, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/115732047219313086656", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVk6Hpw_Fx-N8TCe06XdG6mOcr5RBkekjl3KIThxCUli_bMHmd-=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Alynn Nguyen"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/115732047219313086656", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVk6Hpw_Fx-N8TCe06XdG6mOcr5RBkekjl3KIThxCUli_bMHmd-=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Alynn Nguyen"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/102451632647716590904", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUm15zg6NzhrI1DKyNvyNeWDOPZm63WP615kbzoqgolEpk5fZZF=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jonathan Phan"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/106048594040559266687", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVg33M_gxvkIZ3cBvRiYj9MeXMGSd3uOfmmZDNrrxaU2UQ-zoNB=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "B W"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/115556772821417558314", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjX1ZlHoEBTX7cJzzKQgLdCD4BL1Q5E6ybnSPRG0jw3hHtCCDCMZ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jeff Zander"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-25T15:51:17.248954+00:00', 'santa-clara-valley-medical-center', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

Abierta los 7 días de la semana, la clínica ofrece consultas médicas desde $30 y cuenta con un equipo que habla español, facilitando la comunicación para la comunidad hispana. Los pacientes destacan la excelente atención, el profesionalismo y la amabilidad del personal, así como la claridad en las explicaciones médicas.

Ubicada en Dallas, TX, la clínica está comprometida con la salud integral de sus pacientes, ofreciendo servicios como ultrasonidos, radiografías, EKG, pruebas de embarazo, Papanicolau y evaluaciones para escuelas, transporte y procesos migratorios.', '3068 Forest Ln Suite 121, Dallas, TX 75234, US', 'Dallas', 'TX', '75234', '+1 (214) 647-1040', ARRAY['Spanish', 'Vietnamese']::text[], 'Primary Care', FALSE, '{"email": "clinicahispanavidaplus@gmail.com", "images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/clinica-hispana-vidaplus-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/clinica-hispana-vidaplus-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/clinica-hispana-vidaplus-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/clinica-hispana-vidaplus-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/clinica-hispana-vidaplus-google-5.webp"], "rating": 5, "pricing": [{"name": "Consulta médica", "notes": "Cita a tan solo $30.", "price": "$30", "category": "exam", "price_range": null}], "reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-11T22:06:22.959508389Z", "text": "I love this place it’s really good you guys should definitely go it’s amazing very nice people they treat you perfectly and professionally", "author": "Angelina Perez", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110183608144145076391/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-18T17:16:13.345777855Z", "text": "Great experience from the moment I walked in, friendly staff.  Dr was incredibly kind and attentive, felt comfortable.", "author": "Cindy Carmona", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118289350750174136246/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-20T14:27:34.373622512Z", "text": "Treated me like family.  I would definitely recommend this place to everyone.", "author": "Jeff Lay", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105571765307753243368/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-18T17:13:41.952386976Z", "text": "Very friendly staff and wait time was short and got seen quickly!", "author": "Randy Alfred", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111360998508778736115/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-11-23T22:55:00.369372752Z", "text": "Great customer service! Very caring & professional", "author": "Edgar Barrera", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108244371619628019889/reviews"}], "website": "http://www.clinicahispanavidaplus.com/", "location": {"latitude": 32.9085047, "longitude": -96.87395}, "services": ["Chequeos generales y control", "Urgencias menores y procedimientos", "Diagnóstico e imagenología", "Salud masculina", "Salud femenina", "Exámenes especiales"], "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Consulta médica desde $30", "detail": "Cita a tan solo $30.", "category": "pricing"}, {"title": "Abierto los 7 días de la semana", "detail": "Lunes a Sábado: 8:00 AM - 12:00 AM | Domingo: 10:00 AM - 5:00 PM.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Atención en español", "detail": "Todo el contenido y la comunicación están en español, orientado a la comunidad hispana.", "category": "culture"}, {"title": "Más de 2,400 pacientes atendidos", "detail": "Se enorgullecen de haber atendido a miles de pacientes con servicio personalizado.", "category": "reviews"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "http://www.clinicahispanavidaplus.com/", "appointment": {"bo