, I called and asked if there would be a big difference between in network and out of network dentists, with my insurance and I was told it wasn’t too significant. I’ve never used dental insurance in the US before and should have done more research.\n\nAfter my appointment, I was quoted over $7k for all the procedures they recommended. I was shocked and wanted to get a second opinion. My friend insisted I go to an in-network dentist.\n\nI requested x-rays that were taken during the visit at Dr.Singhs, and they sent the wrong x-rays (a different patient’s) to me for the new visit, which made my other dentist appointment twice as long.\n\nAfter getting a quote from the new dentist, the new cost of the recommended treatment was under $1000. I should have known about the in-network and out-of-network differences, but I feel like the front desk team were not transparent. I also think they made recommendations that were not necessary.", "author": "ECH", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104143133380842805066/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-29T20:35:17.102477635Z", "text": "Great approach. Seemed like excellent dental talent. Lovely style.   Unfortunately, the industry is priced way out of the market for people that actually need dental help. That is why people go to other countries. Not a smart way to lose clients.  But loved the  dental practice", "author": "Carolyn Rose-Avila", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102975881517009377539/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "First Hill Dental Center - Dr. Singh DMD has a 4.8 star Google rating from 898 Google reviews. Patients commonly mention friendly staff, clear explanations, comfortable visits, strong results.", "about_highlight": "First Hill Dental Center is your neighborhood clinic in Seattle, providing exceptional oral health care in a stress-free environment. Led by Dr. Singh DMD, our team practices with compassion, trust, and 