We offer same-day visits for urgent issues, transparent cash pricing for those without insurance coverage, and accept a growing list of insurance plans including Anthem, Cigna, Aetna, Scan Health, and Seoul Medical Group. Our doctor, Dr. Joo, is known for thorough medication reviews, conservative evidence-based treatments, and a patient-centered approach that has helped patients reduce medications and improve chronic conditions like diabetes.

Whether you are covered by insurance or paying out-of-pocket, we strive to make primary care accessible and straightforward. Schedule a visit online, by phone, or by text, and fill out intake forms before your appointment for a seamless experience.', '3511 W Olympic Blvd Suite 202, Los Angeles, CA 90019', 'Los Angeles', 'CA', '90019', '(310) 294-8090', ARRAY['English', 'Korean']::text[], 'Primary Care', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/solid-primary-care-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/solid-primary-care-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/solid-primary-care-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/solid-primary-care-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/solid-primary-care-google-5.webp"], "rating": 4.8, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-23T01:04:13.988993386Z", "text": "​Highly recommend Dr. Joo!\n​Finding a primary care doctor you truly trust can be tough, but Dr. Joo is absolutely amazing. He is incredibly kind, patient, and takes the time to actually listen to your concerns. You can tell he genuinely cares about his patients, which makes every visit so comfortable.\n\n​On top of that, the clinic itself is exceptionally clean, and the front desk staff are always welcoming and friendly. This has officially become my go-to primary care clinic. If you’re looking for a trustworthy and compassionate doctor, look no further!", "author": "김첼시", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117048918604624478758/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-03T02:16:41.673995465Z", "text": "Dr. Joo has real integrity. Every recommendation he makes is what he actually thinks is best for you. He asks thoughtful questions and listens, and he cares about your health as a whole, not just writing prescriptions. He''s also genuinely kind, and his staff are the same way. You feel respected and well taken care of here. Highly recommend.", "author": "Daniel Cho", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117827590089030760362/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-27T17:27:38.568162601Z", "text": "Dr. Joo is honest and kind.  His nurses are super nice too.  Always prompt to  my request.  I recommended to my friend who didn''t have an insurance. She was 100% satisfied and thanked me again and again.  I am blessed to find Dr. Joo.", "author": "K L", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102368686678701299146/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-11T20:18:07.796705205Z", "text": "The doctor was great, but I had a difficult experience with the blood draw. I felt very lightheaded, almost to the point of fainting. The nurse mentioned that the vein became swollen during the first attempt, and I ended up with a noticeable bruise. (Purple bruise size about 2inch) I wish I can post the photo. The second arm was fine. I’ve had blood drawn many times before and have never experienced this, so I was a bit surprised. I wish there had been more attention to patient comfort during the initial draw.", "author": "Janice Son", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108945618171642788982/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-24T17:09:05.515212685Z", "text": "Dr. Joo is honestly one of the best doctors I’ve had. He’s super nice, very detailed, and really cares about his patients. Unlike a lot of other physicians I’ve seen in Koreatown, he actually calls to go over test results instead of making me come in every time — which I really appreciate!\n\nHe takes the time to listen, explains everything clearly, and never makes me feel rushed. You can tell he really wants his patients to stay healthy and understand what’s going on. The office staff is also friendly and helpful, which makes every visit easy.", "author": "Ye Eun Choi", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107097271546167618943/reviews"}], "website": "http://solidprimarycare.com/", "location": {"latitude": 34.0529395, "longitude": -118.3151905}, "services": ["Primary Care", "Urgent Care (Same-day visits)", "Medication Management", "Chronic Disease Management"], "insurance": {"notes": "Check coverage via member services line on your insurance card, stopping by the clinic, texting, or calling. If not covered, transparent cash pricing is available.", "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": ["Blue Cross Blue Shield", "Seoul Medical Group", "Cigna", "Scan Health", "Aetna"], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": true}, "highlights": [{"title": "Same-day visits", "detail": "We do our best to accommodate same day visits for urgent issues; please call to confirm availability.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Transparent cash pricing", "detail": "If your insurance is not covered, our cash pricing is transparently displayed on our pricing page.", "category": "insurance"}, {"title": "Insurance accepted", "detail": "We accept Anthem, Cigna, Aetna, Scan Health, and Seoul Medical Group. Check coverage by calling, texting, or stopping by.", "category": "insurance"}, {"title": "Patient-centered care", "detail": "We have set a system in place so that you always come first, with a focus on conservative, evidence-based treatments.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Thorough medication reviews", "detail": "Dr. Joo reviews medication lists thoroughly and has helped patients cut their medications in half.", "category": "care"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "http://solidprimarycare.com/", "appointment": {"booking_note": "Schedule a visit through clicking ''book an appointment'', calling us, or texting us. Same day visits for urgent issues are available; please call to confirm.", "appointment_url": "https://app.elationemr.com/book/solidprimarycare", "new_patient_note": "Fill out the intake and consent forms before your visit for your convenience. Forms are processed through HIPAA compliant practice management software.", "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": true, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": false, "scout_query": "Korean doctor in Los Angeles", "search_text": "primary care | family doctor | general practitioner | annual physical | checkup | bác sĩ gia đình | khám tổng quát | nội khoa | 내과 | 가정의학과 | 家庭医生 | 全科医生 | 内科 | english | korean | 한국어 | 한인 | 한국말 | urgent care (same-day visits) | medication management | chronic disease management | emergency | blue cross blue shield | seoul medical group | cigna | scan health | aetna | dr. joo | internal medicine physician", "google_types": ["medical_clinic", "doctor", "local_government_office", "government_office", "health", "point_of_interest", "establishment"], "open_weekend": false, "rating_count": 32, "team_members": [{"name": "Dr. Joo", "role": "Internal Medicine Physician", "bio_snippet": "Dr. Joo is known for thorough medication reviews, conservative evidence-based treatments, and a patient-centered approach. Patients report significant improvements in health, including reduced medications and better diabetes markers.", "languages_spoken": ["English"]}], "open_saturday": false, "quality_score": 100, "working_hours": {"friday": "9:00 AM – 4:00 PM", "monday": "9:00 AM – 4:00 PM", "sunday": "Closed", "tuesday": "9:00 AM – 4:00 PM", "saturday": "Closed", "thursday": "9:00 AM – 4:00 PM", "wednesday": "9:00 AM – 4:00 PM"}, "gallery_images": ["http://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/6660dd70a5bc5a05ac7b8c62/e33c7bac-55f8-4e35-8a22-857a4e0b9483/transparent+logo+longitudinal.png?format=1500w"], "review_profile": {"rating": 4.8, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Clinical Expertise", "mentions": 5, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Dr. Joo is described as honest, detailed, and genuinely caring, with patients appreciating his thoughtful recommendations and clear explanations."}, {"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 4, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "The front desk staff and nurses are consistently praised for being friendly, helpful, and respectful."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Dr. Joo is commended for taking the time to listen, explain clearly, and even calling to discuss test results, making patients feel valued."}, {"theme": "Facility Environment", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "The clinic is noted for being exceptionally clean and welcoming, contributing to a comfortable patient experience."}, {"theme": "Patient Comfort", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "One reviewer experienced discomfort during a blood draw, mentioning a swollen vein and noticeable bruise, wishing for more attention to patient comfort."}], "summary": "Patients consistently praise Dr. Joo for his kindness, attentiveness, and genuine care, making Solid Primary Care a trusted and welcoming clinic. While most reviews highlight positive experiences, a few mention minor discomfort during procedures.", "review_count": 32, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": ["Medication reduction", "Improved diabetes markers", "Conservative evidence-based treatments", "Patient-centered care"], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-23T01:04:13.988993386Z", "text": "​Highly recommend Dr. Joo!\n​Finding a primary care doctor you truly trust can be tough, but Dr. Joo is absolutely amazing. He is incredibly kind, patient, and takes the time to actually listen to your concerns. You can tell he genuinely cares about his patients, which makes every visit so comfortable.\n\n​On top of that, the clinic itself is exceptionally clean, and the front desk staff are always welcoming and friendly. This has officially become my go-to primary care clinic. If you’re looking for a trustworthy and compassionate doctor, look no further!", "author": "김첼시", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117048918604624478758/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-03T02:16:41.673995465Z", "text": "Dr. Joo has real integrity. Every recommendation he makes is what he actually thinks is best for you. He asks thoughtful questions and listens, and he cares about your health as a whole, not just writing prescriptions. He''s also genuinely kind, and his staff are the same way. You feel respected and well taken care of here. Highly recommend.", "author": "Daniel Cho", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117827590089030760362/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-27T17:27:38.568162601Z", "text": "Dr. Joo is honest and kind.  His nurses are super nice too.  Always prompt to  my request.  I recommended to my friend who didn''t have an insurance. She was 100% satisfied and thanked me again and again.  I am blessed to find Dr. Joo.", "author": "K L", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102368686678701299146/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-11T20:18:07.796705205Z", "text": "The doctor was great, but I had a difficult experience with the blood draw. I felt very lightheaded, almost to the point of fainting. The nurse mentioned that the vein became swollen during the first attempt, and I ended up with a noticeable bruise. (Purple bruise size about 2inch) I wish I can post the photo. The second arm was fine. I’ve had blood drawn many times before and have never experienced this, so I was a bit surprised. I wish there had been more attention to patient comfort during the initial draw.", "author": "Janice Son", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108945618171642788982/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-24T17:09:05.515212685Z", "text": "Dr. Joo is honestly one of the best doctors I’ve had. He’s super nice, very detailed, and really cares about his patients. Unlike a lot of other physicians I’ve seen in Koreatown, he actually calls to go over test results instead of making me come in every time — which I really appreciate!\n\nHe takes the time to listen, explains everything clearly, and never makes me feel rushed. You can tell he really wants his patients to stay healthy and understand what’s going on. The office staff is also friendly and helpful, which makes every visit easy.", "author": "Ye Eun Choi", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107097271546167618943/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients consistently praise Dr. Joo for his kindness, attentiveness, and genuine care, making Solid Primary Care a trusted and welcoming clinic. While most reviews highlight positive experiences, a few mention minor discomfort during procedures.", "about_highlight": "Solid Primary Care provides simply good primary care with a focus on helping you live your life to the fullest. Our goal is to remove physical barriers that prevent you from savoring life or hitting your goals. We uphold the time-honored, professional ethos of the physician while appropriately enhancing the patient experience with technology and innovation. Beyond anything else, we have set a system in place so that you always come first.\n\nWe offer same-day visits for urgent issues, transparent cash pricing for those without insurance coverage, and accept a growing list of insurance plans including Anthem, Cigna, Aetna, Scan Health, and Seoul Medical Group. Our doctor, Dr. Joo, is known for thorough medication reviews, conservative evidence-based treatments, and a patient-centered approach that has helped patients reduce medications and improve chronic conditions like diabetes.\n\nWhether you are covered by insurance or paying out-of-pocket, we strive to make primary care accessible and straightforward. Schedule a visit online, by phone, or by text, and fill out intake forms before your appointment for a seamless experience.", "appointment_url": "https://app.elationemr.com/book/solidprimarycare", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=1046956220053097038&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJ5-Dszlq5woARToqmlyKJhw4", "quality_missing": [], "search_keywords": ["primary care", "family doctor", "general practitioner", "annual physical", "checkup", "bác sĩ gia đình", "khám tổng quát", "nội khoa", "내과", "가정의학과", "家庭医生", "全科医生", "内科", "english", "korean", "한국어", "한인", "한국말", "urgent care (same-day visits)", "medication management", "chronic disease management", "emergency", "blue cross blue shield", "seoul medical group", "cigna", "scan health", "aetna", "dr. joo", "internal medicine physician"], "services_offered": [{"name": "Primary Care", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Comprehensive primary care services to help you live your life to the fullest.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Adults seeking general medical care"}, {"name": "Urgent Care (Same-day visits)", "category": "Emergency", "description": "Same-day visits for urgent medical issues; call to confirm availability.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients with acute but non-emergency needs"}, {"name": "Medication Management", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Thorough review and optimization of medications, often reducing unnecessary prescriptions.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients on multiple medications"}, {"name": "Chronic Disease Management", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Management of chronic conditions such as diabetes, with evidence-based treatment plans.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients with diabetes or other chronic conditions"}], "short_description": "Solid Primary Care provides simply good primary care with a focus on helping you live your life to the fullest. We offer same-day visits, transparent pricing, and accept various insurance plans.", "google_website_url": "http://solidprimarycare.com/", "insurance_accepted": ["Blue Cross Blue Shield", "Seoul Medical Group", "Cigna", "Scan Health", "Aetna"], "google_primary_type": "Medical Clinic", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": ["Dr. Joo"], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "3511 W Olympic Blvd #202, Los Angeles, CA 90019, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/116220658487256011634", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU6eNDyvlyEslhDI1HU_0P5pdILZLBAdWfAsX2rBCV6_96Vgns=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Solid Primary Care/주우진 내과"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/116494847820448542373", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI9Y2V1ZLLyBgXH4JBOaeicNI-tPJ44SX0g35koNcqXK00SUg=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Young kim"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/116494847820448542373", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI9Y2V1ZLLyBgXH4JBOaeicNI-tPJ44SX0g35koNcqXK00SUg=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Young kim"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/116494847820448542373", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI9Y2V1ZLLyBgXH4JBOaeicNI-tPJ44SX0g35koNcqXK00SUg=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Young kim"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/116494847820448542373", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI9Y2V1ZLLyBgXH4JBOaeicNI-tPJ44SX0g35koNcqXK00SUg=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Young kim"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-25T19:30:14.903743+00:00', 'solid-primary-care', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

The practice provides a range of services including annual physicals, work physicals, bloodwork, immunizations, and management of chronic conditions such as diabetes, hypertension, asthma, COPD, coronary artery disease, gastritis, GERD, arthritis, allergies, and depression. Additionally, procedures like EKG, spirometry, and joint injections are available to help patients live active and productive lives.

Dr. Kim welcomes patients with Medicare HMO plans exclusively, accepting plans from Anthem Blue Cross, Blueshield, Wellcare, UnitedHealthcare (Secure Horizons), Central Health Plan, SCAN, Humana, Brand New Day, and Alignment. The practice belongs to Seoul Medical Group (SMG) and does not accept Commercial HMO or PPO insurance plans.', '903 Crenshaw Blvd, STE 104, Los Angeles, CA 90019', 'Los Angeles', 'CA', '90019', '714-562-9139 / 323-250-2008', ARRAY['English', 'Korean']::text[], 'Internal Medicine', FALSE, '{"fax": "213-769-0007", "email": "info@drkims.org", "images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/sung-hyun-kim-m.d.-internal-medicine-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/sung-hyun-kim-m.d.-internal-medicine-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/sung-hyun-kim-m.d.-internal-medicine-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/sung-hyun-kim-m.d.-internal-medicine-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/sung-hyun-kim-m.d.-internal-medicine-google-5.webp"], "rating": 4.2, "reviews": [{"date": "2025-08-13T22:46:59.583270330Z", "text": "Dr. Kim is amazing! The front staff as well are all welcoming and treats patients so kindly. Everything was done efficiently and with little to no wait time.", "author": "eunah kim", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106012370749963254089/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-09-11T18:51:39.711728040Z", "text": "I went to Dr. Sung Hyun Kim’s clinic for my annual check-up, and every time I visit, the staff and the doctor are always very kind and provide quick, efficient service. I truly think this is the best clinic in LA.", "author": "JOY JUNG", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114773312494174751679/reviews"}, {"date": "2023-01-20T02:25:48.618684Z", "text": "Dr. Kim is an outstanding internist and very kind. Whenever I visit him, I can relax and feel warm. His staffs are also very kind, dedicated for patients and always prepared so I could save some time that I didn''t expect. To go to see a doctor is not easy for me and actually very stressful but Dr. Kim is always ready to listen to the patients. Five thumbs up!", "author": "Grace Choo", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112630421016841260429/reviews"}, {"date": "2022-08-24T15:58:43.007777Z", "text": "Very friendly. Highly recommend.", "author": "Minsu Kim", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100978356597014556579/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-05-15T22:03:23.087192Z", "text": "SNS에서 추천댓글이 많아서 방문하였습니다.\n전화상담도 친절하셨고, 당일방문도 가능하게 해주셨습니다.\n모든 직원분들과 의사선생님도 친절하게 설명과 진료를 해주셨으며, 그리고 다른검진의 안내까지 등등, 처음부터 마무리까지 매우 만족하는 내과병원임을 느끼게 되었습니다.\n병원을 다녀본곳 중에서 가장 친절한 곳임을 공유하고자 리뷰를 남깁니다.\n매우 감사드립니다 !!! 👍👍👍👍👍\n\n이후로 계속 방문하게 되어도 변함없이 밝게 환자들을 대해 주심에 감동하며 감사드립니다!!!", "author": "US", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117323498076607420242/reviews"}], "website": "http://www.drkims.org", "location": {"latitude": 34.0563348, "longitude": -118.3224817}, "services": ["Physical Checkup", "Bloodwork", "Immunization", "Chronic Medical Conditions Management", "Procedures"], "insurance": {"notes": "We are pleased to welcome Patients with Medicare HMO plans exclusively. At this moment, we do not accept Commercial HMO or PPO insurance plans. Medical Group: Seoul Medical Group (SMG).", "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": true, "accepted_networks": ["Blue Cross Blue Shield", "Wellcare", "UnitedHealthcare", "Central Health Plan", "SCAN", "Humana", "Brand New Day", "Alignment", "Medicare"], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": true}, "highlights": [{"title": "Holistic Patient-Centered Care", "detail": "Dr. Kim views each patient as a whole, treating the person rather than a single symptom.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Bilingual Services Available", "detail": "The practice offers both English and Korean language pages, indicating bilingual accessibility.", "category": "culture"}, {"title": "Medicare HMO Accepted", "detail": "Accepts multiple Medicare HMO plans including Anthem Blue Cross, Blueshield, Wellcare, UnitedHealthcare, and others.", "category": "insurance"}, {"title": "Two Office Locations", "detail": "Conveniently located in Los Angeles (LA Office) and Buena Park (Orange County Office).", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Online Scheduling Available", "detail": "Patients can schedule visits online through the Elation EMR booking system.", "category": "convenience"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "http://www.drkims.org/", "appointment": {"booking_note": "Schedule a Visit Online", "appointment_url": "https://app.elationemr.com/book/411026836094980", "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": true, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": false, "scout_query": "Korean doctor in Los Angeles", "search_text": "internal medicine | internist | primary care | nội khoa | bác sĩ nội | 내과 | 内科 | english | korean | 한국어 | 한인 | 한국말 | physical checkup | bloodwork | immunization | chronic medical conditions management | procedures | preventive | diagnostic | blue cross blue shield | wellcare | unitedhealthcare | central health plan | scan | humana | brand new day | alignment | medicare | sung hyun kim | internal medicine physician", "google_types": ["medical_clinic", "doctor", "health", "point_of_interest", "establishment"], "open_weekend": false, "rating_count": 15, "team_members": [{"name": "Sung Hyun Kim", "role": "Internal Medicine Physician", "bio_snippet": "Dr. Kim is dedicated to a client-centered medical experience, building strong and long-lasting bonds with each patient through sound medical advice and responsible diagnoses.", "languages_spoken": ["English", "Korean"]}], "open_saturday": false, "quality_score": 100, "working_hours": {"friday": "Closed", "monday": "Closed", "sunday": "Closed", "tuesday": "8:00 AM – 4:00 PM", "saturday": "Closed", "thursday": "8:00 AM – 4:00 PM", "wednesday": "Closed"}, "gallery_images": ["https://static.wixstatic.com/media/70c820cce59c49458578c60380ee909c.jpg/v1/crop/x_0,y_899,w_4832,h_2261/fill/w_940,h_440,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/Patient%20with%20Healthcare%20Nurse.jpg", "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/4c4ad544629b42d4a0fcc89e738a002b.jpg/v1/fill/w_460,h_340,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/Doctor''s%20Visit.jpg", "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8f301d7844d348f9ad32e99f1ee17ebb.jpg/v1/fill/w_460,h_340,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/Petri%20Dish.jpg", "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/11062b_a4a8ce10cd884a52a42b6518c527525b~mv2.jpg/v1/crop/x_0,y_0,w_5455,h_4032/fill/w_460,h_340,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/Medical%20Consultation.jpg", "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/11062b_b77adf2d89984b338094ce77679ab7df~mv2.jpeg/v1/fill/w_460,h_340,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/Joint%20Pain.jpeg"], "review_profile": {"rating": 4.2, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 5, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Every reviewer highlights the friendly, knowledgeable staff who provide quick and efficient service."}, {"theme": "Doctor''s Kindness", "mentions": 4, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Dr. Kim is described as very kind, attentive, and ready to listen to patients, making visits relaxing and warm."}, {"theme": "Efficiency", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients appreciate the efficient service with little to no wait time, saving them unexpected time."}, {"theme": "Facility Environment", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "The clinic is noted for its welcoming atmosphere, making patients feel comfortable from start to finish."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Reviewers mention clear and kind explanations from both the doctor and staff, enhancing their overall experience."}], "summary": "Patients consistently praise Dr. Kim and his staff for their kindness, efficiency, and welcoming atmosphere, making visits stress-free and highly satisfactory.", "review_count": 15, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2025-08-13T22:46:59.583270330Z", "text": "Dr. Kim is amazing! The front staff as well are all welcoming and treats patients so kindly. Everything was done efficiently and with little to no wait time.", "author": "eunah kim", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106012370749963254089/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-09-11T18:51:39.711728040Z", "text": "I went to Dr. Sung Hyun Kim’s clinic for my annual check-up, and every time I visit, the staff and the doctor are always very kind and provide quick, efficient service. I truly think this is the best clinic in LA.", "author": "JOY JUNG", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114773312494174751679/reviews"}, {"date": "2023-01-20T02:25:48.618684Z", "text": "Dr. Kim is an outstanding internist and very kind. Whenever I visit him, I can relax and feel warm. His staffs are also very kind, dedicated for patients and always prepared so I could save some time that I didn''t expect. To go to see a doctor is not easy for me and actually very stressful but Dr. Kim is always ready to listen to the patients. Five thumbs up!", "author": "Grace Choo", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112630421016841260429/reviews"}, {"date": "2022-08-24T15:58:43.007777Z", "text": "Very friendly. Highly recommend.", "author": "Minsu Kim", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100978356597014556579/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-05-15T22:03:23.087192Z", "text": "SNS에서 추천댓글이 많아서 방문하였습니다.\n전화상담도 친절하셨고, 당일방문도 가능하게 해주셨습니다.\n모든 직원분들과 의사선생님도 친절하게 설명과 진료를 해주셨으며, 그리고 다른검진의 안내까지 등등, 처음부터 마무리까지 매우 만족하는 내과병원임을 느끼게 되었습니다.\n병원을 다녀본곳 중에서 가장 친절한 곳임을 공유하고자 리뷰를 남깁니다.\n매우 감사드립니다 !!! 👍👍👍👍👍\n\n이후로 계속 방문하게 되어도 변함없이 밝게 환자들을 대해 주심에 감동하며 감사드립니다!!!", "author": "US", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117323498076607420242/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients consistently praise Dr. Kim and his staff for their kindness, efficiency, and welcoming atmosphere, making visits stress-free and highly satisfactory.", "about_highlight": "Sung Hyun Kim, M.D. Internal Medicine is a client-centered internal medicine practice serving the communities of Los Angeles and Orange County. Dr. Kim emphasizes building strong, long-lasting bonds with each patient through sound medical advice, responsible diagnoses, and procedures. The practice offers a holistic approach to medicine, viewing each patient as a whole rather than a single symptom to be treated.\n\nThe practice provides a range of services including annual physicals, work physicals, bloodwork, immunizations, and management of chronic conditions such as diabetes, hypertension, asthma, COPD, coronary artery disease, gastritis, GERD, arthritis, allergies, and depression. Additionally, procedures like EKG, spirometry, and joint injections are available to help patients live active and productive lives.\n\nDr. Kim welcomes patients with Medicare HMO plans exclusively, accepting plans from Anthem Blue Cross, Blueshield, Wellcare, UnitedHealthcare (Secure Horizons), Central Health Plan, SCAN, Humana, Brand New Day, and Alignment. The practice belongs to Seoul Medical Group (SMG) and does not accept Commercial HMO or PPO insurance plans.", "appointment_url": "https://app.elationemr.com/book/411026836094980", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=14391323469540684449&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJDZkAyEO5woARofK2cXJAuMc", "quality_missing": [], "search_keywords": ["internal medicine", "internist", "primary care", "nội khoa", "bác sĩ nội", "내과", "内科", "english", "korean", "한국어", "한인", "한국말", "physical checkup", "bloodwork", "immunization", "chronic medical conditions management", "procedures", "preventive", "diagnostic", "blue cross blue shield", "wellcare", "unitedhealthcare", "central health plan", "scan", "humana", "brand new day", "alignment", "medicare", "sung hyun kim", "internal medicine physician"], "services_offered": [{"name": "Physical Checkup", "category": "Preventive", "description": "Annual physical and work physical examinations.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients needing routine checkups or work-related physicals."}, {"name": "Bloodwork", "category": "Diagnostic", "description": "Laboratory blood tests to support diagnosis and health monitoring.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients requiring blood tests for health assessment."}, {"name": "Immunization", "category": "Preventive", "description": "Vaccinations to help patients stay healthy.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients needing routine or recommended vaccines."}, {"name": "Chronic Medical Conditions Management", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Management of diabetes, hypertension, asthma, COPD, coronary artery disease, gastritis, GERD, arthritis, allergies, depression, and more.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients with ongoing chronic health conditions requiring regular management."}, {"name": "Procedures", "category": "Diagnostic", "description": "EKG, spirometry, and joint injections.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients needing cardiac, respiratory, or joint-related diagnostic or therapeutic procedures."}], "short_description": "Sung Hyun Kim, M.D. provides quality internal medicine care with a holistic, patient-centered approach, serving Los Angeles and Orange County communities.", "google_website_url": "http://www.drkims.org/", "insurance_accepted": ["Blue Cross Blue Shield", "Wellcare", "UnitedHealthcare", "Central Health Plan", "SCAN", "Humana", "Brand New Day", "Alignment", "Medicare"], "google_primary_type": "Doctor", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": ["Sung Hyun Kim"], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "903 Crenshaw Blvd #104, Los Angeles, CA 90019, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/106218058622212432085", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUdpozrEA88C4q2G2gKyB5JLeN6JY1v_OuMq-VBw7H6spgQxuQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "김성현 내과 | SUNG HYUN KIM, MD. Internal Medicine"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/106218058622212432085", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUdpozrEA88C4q2G2gKyB5JLeN6JY1v_OuMq-VBw7H6spgQxuQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "김성현 내과 | SUNG HYUN KIM, MD. Internal Medicine"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/106218058622212432085", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUdpozrEA88C4q2G2gKyB5JLeN6JY1v_OuMq-VBw7H6spgQxuQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "김성현 내과 | SUNG HYUN KIM, MD. Internal Medicine"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/106218058622212432085", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUdpozrEA88C4q2G2gKyB5JLeN6JY1v_OuMq-VBw7H6spgQxuQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "김성현 내과 | SUNG HYUN KIM, MD. Internal Medicine"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/106218058622212432085", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUdpozrEA88C4q2G2gKyB5JLeN6JY1v_OuMq-VBw7H6spgQxuQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "김성현 내과 | SUNG HYUN KIM, MD. Internal Medicine"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-25T19:33:26.050931+00:00', 'sung-hyun-kim-md-internal-medicine', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

The institution is committed to patient-centered care, offering digital tools like MyChart for online appointment scheduling, medical record access, and video doctor visits. NYU Langone Health also provides extensive patient and visitor support services, including language and disability services, international patient services, and resources for LGBTQ+ community members, veterans, and military families.

As a leading academic health system, NYU Langone Health integrates cutting-edge research and education through its affiliated medical schools, ensuring patients receive innovative, evidence-based treatments. The organization emphasizes quality, safety, and accessibility, with a dedicated focus on serving diverse communities across its many locations.', '550 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016', 'New York', 'NY', '10016', '646-929-7800', ARRAY['English', 'Vietnamese']::text[], 'Hospital', TRUE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/nyu-langone-health-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/nyu-langone-health-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/nyu-langone-health-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/nyu-langone-health-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/nyu-langone-health-google-5.webp"], "rating": 3.7, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-06-07T13:36:33.805628609Z", "text": "I have only wonderful things to say about this hospital, especially the neurosurgery staff. We spent four days split between surgery and the 16th-floor ICU. Every single person we came into contact with—nurses, techs, administrators, and everyone else—was kind, knowledgeable, and genuinely fun! While the room wasn’t the cleanest I’ve ever seen, the excellent care we received is what truly matters. Plus, you can''t beat the views! My husband is an avid sailor, and watching the river made his stay so much easier. Thank you to everyone at NYU Langone! I hope we never have to return.\nP.S. Special thanks to the nurses and staff including but not limited to: Kathleen Jennette, Guetty Joseph, Karen Marie Fernandez, Alyssa Hackney, Frankee Cooper, Lauren Deonarine, Julia Flaim, and (Other) Julia. Also, Dr. Khan, Dr. Carter, Danny NP, Madalyn PA, and all of the Neuro Surgery residents. Apologies and thanks to anyone I forgot. You were all amazing!", "author": "Amy Bogatch", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117819909878384023665/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-14T21:04:55.774190418Z", "text": "NYU LANGONE is the only hospital our family will use, especially after the A+ experience when expecting our first child.\n\nThis one will take some time, but I have to express how we feel.\n\nWe learned we were with child right as the pandemic shutdown. We made several calls to pediatricians around the city, and most of them gave us excuses why they wouldn''t take us as patients; age of the mother, \"risk factors\", etc., after some independent research we decided to try NYU.\n\nFrom the first experience, my wife was treated with the utmost of respect. Every phase of the process was explained in great detail, every doctor, nurse, and medical professional did not hesitate to repeat anything we didn''t understand, and handled my wife''s concerns with respect, kindness, and dignity.\n\nOut of the dozens of people that were a part of her natal team, there was one doctor who did not act professionally toward her - we had a telehealth conference and at some point when my wife was asking a question, the doctor laughed and disregarded her question. I immediately voiced my objection to her, and before the day was over she was removed from her care team. The other doctors apologized for this, and there was never a repeat of this treatment.\n\nThe day we checked in for her delivery was nerve racking and (I''ll admit) frightening. Everyone we met and worked with treated my wife better than royalty. We spent a few days in the hospital after delivery for several reasons, but each day passed with more care and compassion. By the time we checked out, we had our beautiful baby boy and I had my wife; as healthy and as safe as when we checked in.\n\nWe will forever remember the wonderful doctors, nurses, PAs, and all staff that made this the finest experience it could be.\n\nALL of our medical needs are through the NYU system - we would go to no other hospital if we could help it.\n\nIf you''re reading this and are considering having a baby, BYU is for you.", "author": "Richie Giordano", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112088814221247701601/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-28T23:07:27.914007894Z", "text": "The team at NYU was incredibly kind, compassionate, and professional during a very stressful time. A special thank you to Dr. Ruth McCann for her genuine care, empathy, and warmth.\n\nShe made a difficult experience feel much less overwhelming and treated everyone with such respect and humanity. You can truly tell she cares deeply about her patients and the people around them.\n\nNYU is very lucky to have a doctor like her.", "author": "n n", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112210511082833168549/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-03-05T20:30:17.845526631Z", "text": "I am grateful for the chance to be alive. Two years ago I had the kidney transplant surgery and can''t be more happier. Special thanks to Dr. Johnathan Berger,  all nurses and doctors who were next to me during my treatment in the hospital. Great people 👏,  great  facility. God bless you all. 🙏", "author": "Aleksandr Zagalskiy", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113154904064952709959/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-24T11:18:31.319476308Z", "text": "I am so sad to write another review since my first one was a glowing 5 stars. As many good experiences I had with NYU, I am beyond disappointed with my recent, and last, experience that I had with them. After surgery in February, I was feel awful in March. I was presenting with all symptoms for my chronic disease, including bleeding and abdominal pain. I went back to NYU and was almost immediately dismissed. Told to follow-up outpatient with my surgeon and GI doctor. I messaged my surgeon, Dr. Simon, whose team redirected me to Dr. Chang, my GI doctor. No tests were ordered; Dr. Chang is prideful of her intelligence, I assume, because she was able to diagnose my symptoms as the very disease that I''ve had for 12 years and just had surgery for weeks ago. Instead of tests or any in-person follow-up, I was seen for 10 minutes virtually and prescribed Prednisone. I messaged Dr. Chang a week later as I couldn''t keep food down. I was vomitting everything I ate and the pain was worse. Again, no in-person follow-up occurred, and this time, not even a virtual visit. Instead, she prescribed an additional medication and sent me on my merry way. After trying NYU''s emergency room once more, and being entirely dismissed, I made my way to Mount Sinai. I presented my symptoms and they immediately ordered a scope and an MRI. Lo and behold, it turns out that the disease I was suffering from was at Mayo Score 3 (the most severe it can be) with SEVERE COLON DISTENTION!! I ended up at Mount Sinai for 3 weeks as I ended up needed emergency inpatient surgery because of how severe the disease was. Also, my CURRENT surgeon at Mount Sinai (who I will 100% recommend to anyone over ANY NYU doctor or surgeon) told me that the surgery was difficult because it turns out that Dr. Simon''s work was sloppy and left me with so much scarring that turned a 4-5 hour surgery, into an 8 hour surgery. My current surgeon said the scarring was so bad that the team was very close to having to open me up completely rather than doing everything lapriscopically (which didn''t happen, thankfully). I am beyond disappointed with NYU and their lack of compassion and ability. Neither time I went to their ER did a proper evaluation ensure. No scope or scan was done, no blood work was properly worked up. Their dismissal of my situation could have killed me had I not been pestering different hospital systems. I will forever be grateful for Mount Sinai for literally saving my life and taking me seriously over NYU, where they would have let me die rather than do their jobs properly. Safe to say my previous 5 stars has been balled up and trashed and burned. I would not recommend NYU for many things. Unless you are presenting something at surface level, don''t expect anyone to listen to you or help you. Please advocate for yourself! If you KNOW something is not right, please speak up. Find another hospital that will take you seriously!", "author": "Summer Rosario", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110647403253629209950/reviews"}], "website": "https://nyulangone.org", "location": {"latitude": 40.7421225, "longitude": -73.9739642}, "services": ["Primary Care Services", "Imaging Services", "Emergency Care", "Urgent Care", "Virtual Urgent Care", "Care on Demand (Primary Care)", "Orthopedic Immediate Care", "Brain & Spine Care", "Cancer Care", "NYU Langone Heart", "NYU Langone Orthopedics", "Pediatrics & Hassenfeld Children''s Hospital", "Women’s Health"], "insurance": {"notes": "Insurance and billing information is available on the website but specific accepted plans are not listed on this page.", "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Over 6,000 Providers", "detail": "Search more than 6,000 providers and schedule an appointment online.", "category": "access"}, {"title": "Same-Day Care Options", "detail": "Offers virtual urgent care, urgent care, care on demand, orthopedic immediate care, and emergency care.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Digital Health Tools", "detail": "MyChart patient portal, NYU Langone Health app, and video doctor visits available.", "category": "technology"}, {"title": "Comprehensive Specialty Care", "detail": "Expertise in brain & spine, cancer, heart, orthopedics, pediatrics, primary care, women''s health, and more.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Language & Disability Services", "detail": "Specialized services for language access, disability support, LGBTQ+ community, veterans, and international patients.", "category": "access"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://nyulangone.org/doctors", "appointment": {"booking_note": "Search more than 6,000 providers and schedule an appointment online.", "appointment_url": "https://nyulangone.org/doctors", "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": true, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": true, "scout_query": "Vietnamese speaking hospital in New York, NY", "search_text": "hospital | english | vietnamese | tiếng việt | người việt | bác sĩ việt | primary care services | imaging services | emergency care | urgent care | virtual urgent care | care on demand (primary care) | orthopedic immediate care | brain & spine care | cancer care | nyu langone heart | nyu langone orthopedics | pediatrics & hassenfeld children''s hospital | women’s health | primary care | diagnostic | emergency | telehealth | orthopedic | neurology | oncology | cardiology | pediatrics | women''s health", "google_types": ["hospital", "health", "point_of_interest", "service", "establishment"], "open_weekend": true, "rating_count": 531, "open_saturday": true, "quality_score": 92, "working_hours": {"friday": "Open 24 hours", "monday": "Open 24 hours", "sunday": "Open 24 hours", "tuesday": "Open 24 hours", "saturday": "Open 24 hours", "thursday": "Open 24 hours", "wednesday": "Open 24 hours"}, "review_profile": {"rating": 3.7, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 4, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Multiple reviewers highlight the kindness, knowledge, and respect shown by doctors, nurses, and staff."}, {"theme": "Clinical Expertise", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients commend the high level of medical expertise and compassionate care from the clinical teams."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Reviewers appreciate detailed explanations and repeated clarifications from the medical staff."}, {"theme": "Facility Environment", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "One reviewer mentions the pleasant views and overall great facility, despite minor cleanliness issues."}, {"theme": "Dismissive Care", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "A patient reports feeling dismissed and receiving inadequate follow-up care post-surgery."}], "summary": "Overall, patients report highly positive experiences with NYU Langone Health, praising the staff''s professionalism, kindness, and expertise, though some mention isolated negative experiences with dismissive care.", "review_count": 531, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-06-07T13:36:33.805628609Z", "text": "I have only wonderful things to say about this hospital, especially the neurosurgery staff. We spent four days split between surgery and the 16th-floor ICU. Every single person we came into contact with—nurses, techs, administrators, and everyone else—was kind, knowledgeable, and genuinely fun! While the room wasn’t the cleanest I’ve ever seen, the excellent care we received is what truly matters. Plus, you can''t beat the views! My husband is an avid sailor, and watching the river made his stay so much easier. Thank you to everyone at NYU Langone! I hope we never have to return.\nP.S. Special thanks to the nurses and staff including but not limited to: Kathleen Jennette, Guetty Joseph, Karen Marie Fernandez, Alyssa Hackney, Frankee Cooper, Lauren Deonarine, Julia Flaim, and (Other) Julia. Also, Dr. Khan, Dr. Carter, Danny NP, Madalyn PA, and all of the Neuro Surgery residents. Apologies and thanks to anyone I forgot. You were all amazing!", "author": "Amy Bogatch", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117819909878384023665/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-14T21:04:55.774190418Z", "text": "NYU LANGONE is the only hospital our family will use, especially after the A+ experience when expecting our first child.\n\nThis one will take some time, but I have to express how we feel.\n\nWe learned we were with child right as the pandemic shutdown. We made several calls to pediatricians around the city, and most of them gave us excuses why they wouldn''t take us as patients; age of the mother, \"risk factors\", etc., after some independent research we decided to try NYU.\n\nFrom the first experience, my wife was treated with the utmost of respect. Every phase of the process was explained in great detail, every doctor, nurse, and medical professional did not hesitate to repeat anything we didn''t understand, and handled my wife''s concerns with respect, kindness, and dignity.\n\nOut of the dozens of people that were a part of her natal team, there was one doctor who did not act professionally toward her - we had a telehealth conference and at some point when my wife was asking a question, the doctor laughed and disregarded her question. I immediately voiced my objection to her, and before the day was over she was removed from her care team. The other doctors apologized for this, and there was never a repeat of this treatment.\n\nThe day we checked in for her delivery was nerve racking and (I''ll admit) frightening. Everyone we met and worked with treated my wife better than royalty. We spent a few days in the hospital after delivery for several reasons, but each day passed with more care and compassion. By the time we checked out, we had our beautiful baby boy and I had my wife; as healthy and as safe as when we checked in.\n\nWe will forever remember the wonderful doctors, nurses, PAs, and all staff that made this the finest experience it could be.\n\nALL of our medical needs are through the NYU system - we would go to no other hospital if we could help it.\n\nIf you''re reading this and are considering having a baby, BYU is for you.", "author": "Richie Giordano", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112088814221247701601/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-28T23:07:27.914007894Z", "text": "The team at NYU was incredibly kind, compassionate, and professional during a very stressful time. A special thank you to Dr. Ruth McCann for her genuine care, empathy, and warmth.\n\nShe made a difficult experience feel much less overwhelming and treated everyone with such respect and humanity. You can truly tell she cares deeply about her patients and the people around them.\n\nNYU is very lucky to have a doctor like her.", "author": "n n", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112210511082833168549/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-03-05T20:30:17.845526631Z", "text": "I am grateful for the chance to be alive. Two years ago I had the kidney transplant surgery and can''t be more happier. Special thanks to Dr. Johnathan Berger,  all nurses and doctors who were next to me during my treatment in the hospital. Great people 👏,  great  facility. God bless you all. 🙏", "author": "Aleksandr Zagalskiy", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113154904064952709959/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-24T11:18:31.319476308Z", "text": "I am so sad to write another review since my first one was a glowing 5 stars. As many good experiences I had with NYU, I am beyond disappointed with my recent, and last, experience that I had with them. After surgery in February, I was feel awful in March. I was presenting with all symptoms for my chronic disease, including bleeding and abdominal pain. I went back to NYU and was almost immediately dismissed. Told to follow-up outpatient with my surgeon and GI doctor. I messaged my surgeon, Dr. Simon, whose team redirected me to Dr. Chang, my GI doctor. No tests were ordered; Dr. Chang is prideful of her intelligence, I assume, because she was able to diagnose my symptoms as the very disease that I''ve had for 12 years and just had surgery for weeks ago. Instead of tests or any in-person follow-up, I was seen for 10 minutes virtually and prescribed Prednisone. I messaged Dr. Chang a week later as I couldn''t keep food down. I was vomitting everything I ate and the pain was worse. Again, no in-person follow-up occurred, and this time, not even a virtual visit. Instead, she prescribed an additional medication and sent me on my merry way. After trying NYU''s emergency room once more, and being entirely dismissed, I made my way to Mount Sinai. I presented my symptoms and they immediately ordered a scope and an MRI. Lo and behold, it turns out that the disease I was suffering from was at Mayo Score 3 (the most severe it can be) with SEVERE COLON DISTENTION!! I ended up at Mount Sinai for 3 weeks as I ended up needed emergency inpatient surgery because of how severe the disease was. Also, my CURRENT surgeon at Mount Sinai (who I will 100% recommend to anyone over ANY NYU doctor or surgeon) told me that the surgery was difficult because it turns out that Dr. Simon''s work was sloppy and left me with so much scarring that turned a 4-5 hour surgery, into an 8 hour surgery. My current surgeon said the scarring was so bad that the team was very close to having to open me up completely rather than doing everything lapriscopically (which didn''t happen, thankfully). I am beyond disappointed with NYU and their lack of compassion and ability. Neither time I went to their ER did a proper evaluation ensure. No scope or scan was done, no blood work was properly worked up. Their dismissal of my situation could have killed me had I not been pestering different hospital systems. I will forever be grateful for Mount Sinai for literally saving my life and taking me seriously over NYU, where they would have let me die rather than do their jobs properly. Safe to say my previous 5 stars has been balled up and trashed and burned. I would not recommend NYU for many things. Unless you are presenting something at surface level, don''t expect anyone to listen to you or help you. Please advocate for yourself! If you KNOW something is not right, please speak up. Find another hospital that will take you seriously!", "author": "Summer Rosario", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110647403253629209950/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Overall, patients report highly positive experiences with NYU Langone Health, praising the staff''s professionalism, kindness, and expertise, though some mention isolated negative experiences with dismissive care.", "about_highlight": "NYU Langone Health is a world-class academic medical center offering comprehensive care across all specialty areas. With over 6,000 providers, the institution provides expert medical services ranging from primary care to highly specialized treatments in cancer, heart, orthopedics, neurology, and pediatrics. Patients benefit from a network of hospitals and outpatient locations throughout the New York City area, Florida, and beyond, with convenient access to same-day care options including virtual urgent care, urgent care centers, and emergency services.\n\nThe institution is committed to patient-centered care, offering digital tools like MyChart for online appointment scheduling, medical record access, and video doctor visits. NYU Langone Health also provides extensive patient and visitor support services, including language and disability services, international patient services, and resources for LGBTQ+ community members, veterans, and military families.\n\nAs a leading academic health system, NYU Langone Health integrates cutting-edge research and education through its affiliated medical schools, ensuring patients receive innovative, evidence-based treatments. The organization emphasizes quality, safety, and accessibility, with a dedicated focus on serving diverse communities across its many locations.", "appointment_url": "https://nyulangone.org/doctors", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=5369810764853601218&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJdUrffUJZwokRwuMqrnBmhUo", "quality_missing": ["insurance", "team_members"], "search_keywords": ["hospital", "english", "vietnamese", "tiếng việt", "người việt", "bác sĩ việt", "primary care services", "imaging services", "emergency care", "urgent care", "virtual urgent care", "care on demand (primary care)", "orthopedic immediate care", "brain & spine care", "cancer care", "nyu langone heart", "nyu langone orthopedics", "pediatrics & hassenfeld children''s hospital", "women’s health", "primary care", "diagnostic", "emergency", "telehealth", "orthopedic", "neurology", "oncology", "cardiology", "pediatrics", "women''s health"], "services_offered": [{"name": "Primary Care Services", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Our doctors partner with you to help you reach your wellness goals and treat illnesses that arise.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Imaging Services", "category": "Diagnostic", "description": "From X-rays to MRI scans, we offer imaging services throughout the New York area.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Emergency Care", "category": "Emergency", "description": "We provide emergency care for adults and children at several specialized locations.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Urgent Care", "category": "Urgent Care", "description": "We offer urgent care for non-emergency medical concerns that need care as soon as possible.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Virtual Urgent Care", "category": "Telehealth", "description": "Virtual urgent care for non-emergency medical concerns.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Care on Demand (Primary Care)", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "On-demand primary care services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Orthopedic Immediate Care", "category": "Orthopedic", "description": "Immediate care for orthopedic issues.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Brain & Spine Care", "category": "Neurology", "description": "Specialty care for brain and spine conditions.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Cancer Care", "category": "Oncology", "description": "Comprehensive cancer care services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "NYU Langone Heart", "category": "Cardiology", "description": "Heart and vascular care services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "NYU Langone Orthopedics", "category": "Orthopedic", "description": "Orthopedic care and surgery.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Pediatrics & Hassenfeld Children''s Hospital", "category": "Pediatrics", "description": "Pediatric care and children''s hospital services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Women’s Health", "category": "Women''s Health", "description": "Comprehensive women''s health services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}], "short_description": "NYU Langone Health is a leading academic medical center with over 6,000 providers offering expert care across all specialties, from primary care to advanced treatments, at locations throughout the New York City area and Florida.", "google_website_url": "https://nyulangone.org/doctors", "google_primary_type": "Hospital", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "550 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/101140409814028774850", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVYo32eG_VqzxV7BnxMrPW8jO7zxUadd9p6SnOVVls5B_tapIRmzQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Lic. Horus Ruiseco Jacobo"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/115242945858791105780", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXfuua9bnm3aC4pTW2T1DlUdz1KiHCJaui4WgYOigTxjQkJit9WDg=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jiang Li"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/100902619982961453181", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUmQmmk0VRtBCGYYzovGWii-WZM030NCE0DNmJnkrVXfRPds6LWkG0=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Garamon Kanegon (Spacegizmo)"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/110066267342233936698", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIW3sNaFEH6VJ9N_x_77jriLCs09HBEBHDOADX9cr_PljwnKA=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "NYU Langone Health"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/108354362204629736611", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV2e3f_xpNpOqukgnue305YsCZ1-LVOCwFgqMY96Ml3xXMzEHv2oA=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Rational Realm"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-25T20:00:48.992392+00:00', 'nyu-langone-health', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

Our hospital features a Level II trauma center, a Level III neonatal intensive care unit (NICU), and a state-of-the-art Heart & Vascular Center. The Grand Tower houses an expanded emergency department and a Family Birth Center, all designed to provide comfortable, convenient, and patient-centered care.', '1401 S Grand Ave', 'Los Angeles', 'CA', '90015', '213-748-2411', ARRAY['English', 'Vietnamese']::text[], 'Hospital', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/dignity-health-california-hospital-medical-center-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/dignity-health-california-hospital-medical-center-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/dignity-health-california-hospital-medical-center-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/dignity-health-california-hospital-medical-center-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/dignity-health-california-hospital-medical-center-google-5.webp"], "rating": 4.1, "reviews": [{"date": "2022-09-20T06:14:39.522437Z", "text": "If I could rate it higher I would! Thank you to everyone in the NICU department for all you all have done for my baby! I couldn''t have done it without you all leading the way! The Doctors great leaders! Thank you all so much! Great attention to detail! Caring loving and understanding!", "author": "Edith Lima", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112963386017974692781/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-29T02:35:32.940756020Z", "text": "My experience was a humble experience. I know it''s named Dignity Health, but it will always be California Medical Hospital to me and my family. Both of my children was born there Neville 34 and Precious 24 now. Lol and believe it are not my daughter Precious just had her first child there October 2023. I live nowhere near the hospital but l traveled there because I knew that I would get top notch care which I did receive. From the emergency room to my room a couple of people was rude to me. The lady that pressured me to hurry and get my doctors phone number was very rude. My doctor sent me to the emergency room. And the second shift nurse was rude as well. But the first shift nurse Sonya was amazin she notice my fear of needles and she comfort me where l didn''t really feel when she gave me my shots. The emergency room looks amazin, it was a state of art emergency room.  And l didn''t have to wait 10 hours to be seen. I recommend California Medical Hospital to anyone. I truly thank you for the service. Please 🙏 keep up the amazin service to the community.", "author": "Leithelle Williams", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106325743404798190327/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-29T00:59:36.892011122Z", "text": "I feel very comfortable and calm through throughout the whole process and procedure. All the nurses, Doctors and specialists were very professional and made sure I understood and took it seriously. Every interaction I had with the staff was awesome. Very lively. :D", "author": "Andree Santos", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105419687223994959373/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-14T00:01:15.531932657Z", "text": "The emergency room staff were able to provide me the best care and assess my symptoms. Also, the doctor provided at home recommendations and things I can buy at the local pharmacy as I’m on budget and would rather save my insurance claim for something that is more life threatening. I appreciate all the medical staff looking out for my health and best interests!", "author": "Gonzalo Antonio Paz", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113793662288824896308/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-18T02:40:40.597477034Z", "text": "Highly disorganized. Nurses had no idea where patients were because others would grab them for a test without there being any way to know who took them. Absolutely disgusted by the bathroom in the ER, too. Waited 7 hours without a doctor looking over any of my scans or tests before I got up and left. My report that I obtained the next day showed that a doctor hadn’t reviewed it for 13 hours after I arrived. Seek ER care elsewhere.", "author": "Richard Hawkins", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114892771292098991823/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.commonspirit.org/find-a-location/dignity-health-california-hospital-medical-center-1246", "location": {"latitude": 34.0375121, "longitude": -118.26625679999998}, "services": ["Cancer Care", "Neurology", "Heart Care", "Family Birth Center", "Emergency Room", "Rehabilitation Therapy", "Dignity Health Imaging"], "insurance": {"notes": "For details on accepted insurance plans, visit the billing and insurance page.", "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Level II Trauma Center", "detail": "Our hospital features a Level II trauma center for advanced emergency care.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Comprehensive Medical Services", "detail": "Offering a full range of services from cancer care to heart and vascular care.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Family Birth Center", "detail": "State-of-the-art Family Birth Center with expanded emergency department.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Language Assistance", "detail": "Language interpretation services available for diverse patient populations.", "category": "access"}, {"title": "24/7 Emergency Care", "detail": "Emergency room open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Over 130 Years of Service", "detail": "Serving the Los Angeles community with compassion and excellence for over 130 years.", "category": "culture"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://www.commonspirit.org/find-a-location/dignity-health-california-hospital-medical-center-1246", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": null, "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": null, "online_booking_available": null, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": true, "scout_query": "Vietnamese speaking hospital in Los Angeles, CA", "search_text": "hospital | english | vietnamese | tiếng việt | người việt | bác sĩ việt | cancer care | neurology | heart care | family birth center | emergency room | rehabilitation therapy | dignity health imaging | cancer center | specialty center | birth center | therapy services | diagnostic imaging center", "google_types": ["hospital", "health", "service", "point_of_interest", "establishment"], "open_weekend": true, "rating_count": 3231, "language_note": "The hospital offers language interpretation services, spiritual care, and provides culturally-competent care as stated in its equal visitation policy. Classes are offered in English and Spanish.", "open_saturday": true, "quality_score": 90, "working_hours": {"friday": "Open 24 hours", "monday": "Open 24 hours", "sunday": "Open 24 hours", "tuesday": "Open 24 hours", "saturday": "Open 24 hours", "thursday": "Open 24 hours", "wednesday": "Open 24 hours"}, "gallery_images": ["https://storage.googleapis.com/blockit-storage-profile-images-prod/2597f22f-66dc-4db9-9fb8-b0cd90ea3c01.jpeg"], "review_profile": {"rating": 4.1, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Many reviewers highlight the professionalism and care of doctors and nurses, especially in critical departments like NICU and emergency care."}, {"theme": "Facility Environment", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Mixed", "summary_quote": "While some praise the state-of-the-art emergency room, others criticize the disorganization and cleanliness issues in certain areas."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients appreciate the clear communication and understanding from staff, ensuring they feel informed and comfortable."}, {"theme": "Treatment Outcomes", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Several reviews commend the effective treatment and care received, particularly in emergency and NICU settings."}, {"theme": "Staff Attitude", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "A few patients report instances of rudeness from some staff members, affecting their overall experience."}], "summary": "Most patients report positive experiences with the hospital, praising the professional and caring staff, especially in the NICU and emergency departments, though some mention occasional disorganization and rudeness.", "review_count": 3231, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2022-09-20T06:14:39.522437Z", "text": "If I could rate it higher I would! Thank you to everyone in the NICU department for all you all have done for my baby! I couldn''t have done it without you all leading the way! The Doctors great leaders! Thank you all so much! Great attention to detail! Caring loving and understanding!", "author": "Edith Lima", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112963386017974692781/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-29T02:35:32.940756020Z", "text": "My experience was a humble experience. I know it''s named Dignity Health, but it will always be California Medical Hospital to me and my family. Both of my children was born there Neville 34 and Precious 24 now. Lol and believe it are not my daughter Precious just had her first child there October 2023. I live nowhere near the hospital but l traveled there because I knew that I would get top notch care which I did receive. From the emergency room to my room a couple of people was rude to me. The lady that pressured me to hurry and get my doctors phone number was very rude. My doctor sent me to the emergency room. And the second shift nurse was rude as well. But the first shift nurse Sonya was amazin she notice my fear of needles and she comfort me where l didn''t really feel when she gave me my shots. The emergency room looks amazin, it was a state of art emergency room.  And l didn''t have to wait 10 hours to be seen. I recommend California Medical Hospital to anyone. I truly thank you for the service. Please 🙏 keep up the amazin service to the community.", "author": "Leithelle Williams", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106325743404798190327/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-29T00:59:36.892011122Z", "text": "I feel very comfortable and calm through throughout the whole process and procedure. All the nurses, Doctors and specialists were very professional and made sure I understood and took it seriously. Every interaction I had with the staff was awesome. Very lively. :D", "author": "Andree Santos", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105419687223994959373/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-14T00:01:15.531932657Z", "text": "The emergency room staff were able to provide me the best care and assess my symptoms. Also, the doctor provided at home recommendations and things I can buy at the local pharmacy as I’m on budget and would rather save my insurance claim for something that is more life threatening. I appreciate all the medical staff looking out for my health and best interests!", "author": "Gonzalo Antonio Paz", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113793662288824896308/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-18T02:40:40.597477034Z", "text": "Highly disorganized. Nurses had no idea where patients were because others would grab them for a test without there being any way to know who took them. Absolutely disgusted by the bathroom in the ER, too. Waited 7 hours without a doctor looking over any of my scans or tests before I got up and left. My report that I obtained the next day showed that a doctor hadn’t reviewed it for 13 hours after I arrived. Seek ER care elsewhere.", "author": "Richard Hawkins", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114892771292098991823/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Most patients report positive experiences with the hospital, praising the professional and caring staff, especially in the NICU and emergency departments, though some mention occasional disorganization and rudeness.", "about_highlight": "Located in the heart of Downtown Los Angeles, California Hospital Medical Center is a 318-bed nonprofit hospital that has been caring for Angelenos with compassion and excellence for more than 130 years. We offer a full range of comprehensive medical services including cancer care, women''s health, orthopedics, advanced heart and vascular care, and more.\n\nOur hospital features a Level II trauma center, a Level III neonatal intensive care unit (NICU), and a state-of-the-art Heart & Vascular Center. The Grand Tower houses an expanded emergency department and a Family Birth Center, all designed to provide comfortable, convenient, and patient-centered care.", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=5652718317684762005&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJM9J-ccbHwoARlaXxTFx9ck4", "quality_missing": ["insurance", "team_members", "appointment_url"], "search_keywords": ["hospital", "english", "vietnamese", "tiếng việt", "người việt", "bác sĩ việt", "cancer care", "neurology", "heart care", "family birth center", "emergency room", "rehabilitation therapy", "dignity health imaging", "cancer center", "specialty center", "birth center", "therapy services", "diagnostic imaging center"], "cultural_context": "The hospital offers language interpretation services, spiritual care, and provides culturally-competent care as stated in its equal visitation policy. Classes are offered in English and Spanish.", "services_offered": [{"name": "Cancer Care", "category": "Cancer Center", "description": "Comprehensive cancer care services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Neurology", "category": "Specialty Center", "description": "Neurological care services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Heart Care", "category": "Specialty Center", "description": "Advanced heart and vascular care.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Family Birth Center", "category": "Birth Center", "description": "Maternity and birthing services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Emergency Room", "category": "Emergency Room", "description": "24/7 emergency medical care.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Rehabilitation Therapy", "category": "Therapy Services", "description": "Rehabilitation therapy services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Dignity Health Imaging", "category": "Diagnostic Imaging Center", "description": "Diagnostic imaging services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}], "short_description": "A 318-bed nonprofit hospital in Downtown Los Angeles offering comprehensive medical services with compassion and excellence for over 130 years.", "google_website_url": "https://www.commonspirit.org/find-a-location/dignity-health-california-hospital-medical-center-1246", "google_primary_type": "Hospital", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "1401 S Grand Ave, Los Angeles, CA 90015, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/110503901769107291863", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXdAUFJWAbuiHUBwUSagfLz1rQaWeNTQOXo6VC1-crR3zBL3iG8=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Dignity Health - California Hospital Medical Center"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/110503901769107291863", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXdAUFJWAbuiHUBwUSagfLz1rQaWeNTQOXo6VC1-crR3zBL3iG8=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Dignity Health - California Hospital Medical Center"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/104908431756212890221", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVLhLKEG66XhPcylcZav9m_pLmq3QMjHOooEbZcW9u2utXLvCe31w=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jay E. Jenkins"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/115193843521742918065", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXWWbKbE6vGksCBLxRG08VCvFvyxA5Z3wrfnVtyw73m12nw4gid=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Demetrio Hernandez"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/109197046125367093452", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUQYJ24OPxp5dCg4PR_TkwH6ngBs2ogtdUuekHdIVDTpv-1Cebp=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "anamaria surmava"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-25T20:10:08.088848+00:00', 'dignity-health-california-hospital-medical-center', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

The hospital is nationally recognized for quality, as a DNV-certified Primary Stroke Center and a Breast Imaging Center of Excellence by the American College of Radiology. The medical team includes over 800 physicians, 1,600 employees, and 80 volunteers dedicated to community health.

Piedmont Eastside provides convenient access with two locations, compassionate care, and a commitment to patient safety and quality. The hospital also offers a range of patient and visitor services, including campus maps, visitor policies, and helpful resources for patients and families.', '1700 Medical Way, Snellville, GA 30078', 'Snellville', 'GA', '30078', '770.979.0200', ARRAY['English']::text[], 'Hospital', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/piedmont-eastside-medical-center-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/piedmont-eastside-medical-center-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/piedmont-eastside-medical-center-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/piedmont-eastside-medical-center-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/piedmont-eastside-medical-center-google-5.webp"], "rating": 3.9, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-06-21T12:33:48.807201577Z", "text": "My experience at Piedmont Eastside Medical Center this past Thursday was quite pleasant. I was running behind for my appointment and I informed the mammogram department of such. The young lady at the desk was very pleasant and helpful. She told me I would have somewhat of a wait, but for certain I would still be able to have my mammogram done. It turned out that my wait was  minimal (I would have gladly waited anyway because it was my fault that I had to wait) and everything went smoothly! I believe in treating others well no matter the circumstances. So, I am most pleased to publicly say my visit to Eastside Medical Center on Thursday June 18th was most positive. At the end of my visit, the technician most kindly told me that she had enjoyed our conversation during my visit! Great customer service! Blessings to all.", "author": "Judith B", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101167907212909539705/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-03-03T13:56:32.426137073Z", "text": "From the time I arrived for my surgery the staff was very friendly and helpful. I had to stay at the hospital for this surgery for a couple of days and was able to meet some wonderful nurses that were able to take care of me and explain everything thru the process. I would like to thank my surgical Nurse Jessica, she went above and beyond she traveled with me to my recovery floor and still helped there. I had the best nightshift Nurse Goodness, she was exceptional she was able to handle everything from making sure I was comfortable to my family made sure my medicine was given on time she went above and beyond. Then my last Nurse Emma made sure to explain my discharge information and showed how my dressing of my wound should be done. Thank you to the staff and hospital for taking care of me and my Surgeon Dr.Fred Koch, who came everyday to check on me thank you so much Resurgens(decatur).", "author": "Desha Jackson", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117419245609225473127/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-30T16:07:16.069115070Z", "text": "We had an amazing experience with the birth of our child two weeks ago.  We flew in from out of town to be there for our surrogate as she gave birth, and so of course, we wondered if we would be treated differently as the parents or if there would be confusion over the birth of the baby via surrogacy - would it be easy to get access, would we all be allowed to be together, would we be treated well?\n\nEverything from start to finish was absolutely perfect.   The front desk staff of the women''s care floor were outstanding - friendly and caring.  They took a genuine interest in us and the exciting next chapter in our lives.  They were kind and helpful to everyone we saw come into the waiting room.\n\nThe nurses and helpers in the delivery ward and then especially in the family care center where both our surrogate and (separately) we recovered/acclimated to the birth and wonderful new baby were all amazingly loving and careful and outgoing.  Their level of empathy and consideration and helpfulness was out of this world.  The food was good - but especially the stork dinner for the new parents - that was really delicious.   While we were glad to leave and start our next steps, we truly do miss the friendly faces and smart, professional care we had while living such an exciting, special moment.\n\nWe also sincerely appreciated how well the staff cared for our surrogate and helped recognize how we were all enjoying this special time together, and with great joy.\n\nI would also like to say that we felt a level of Southern Hospitality that warmed our hearts. I was just chatting with a friend up north who had a baby and while their experience at a great hospital was very good, he was impressed with several of the little special touches I mentioned we had during our stay at Piedmont Eastside.\n\nThank you.", "author": "Chris Wallgren", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104208004668069889629/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-30T11:29:41.927681911Z", "text": "The foodservice dept is incompetent and doesn’t use common sense. 5 days I’ve been here, I don’t eat 4 things and that’s a problem. I told them they can sent the same bfast every day ( 2 pc toast sausage and unsweetened tea) and today out of surgery haven’t eaten for 24 hours and another phone call I had to make. Then the person said well you should have ordered it yesterday. I was in surgery! They sent up a plate of potatoes pancakes toast as I get given my cloresteral pills. Makes me not trust anything about the food and patients are supposed to eat to heal. For a hospital with such a wonderful staff, the food service dept. Makes it hard on them bc food workers have to always double back for incompetent workers. You would think someone can get it right after 4 phone calls but apparently the patients don’t count when you need to eat. So my advise is to pack a picnic if your hungry bc they def will not get it right! The sad part  here for 3 more days!!\n\nUpdate the Food and  Beverage Manager came to talk to me about the situation in depth listening and understanding my grievances.  They stepped up their game and with this managers empathy and respect makes me more confident. They went above and beyond to understand and fix the opportunities. It shows the caring and compassion he has for his dept.", "author": "Jennifer Moen", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105433285235607030548/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-31T17:34:56.813577040Z", "text": "Delivered my babygirl here and everyone at L&D and postpartum care were awesome! Round the clock care and support. Couldn’t ask for a better team. Everyone was attentive to my needs and ensured the delivery of my baby was safe and healthy.", "author": "Noemi Mercado", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114508140598115428641/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.piedmont.org/locations/piedmont-eastside-medical-center", "location": {"latitude": 33.8769038, "longitude": -84.0210179}, "services": ["24/7 Emergency Services", "Bariatric Surgery", "Behavioral Health", "Cancer Care", "Emergency Medicine", "Heart Care", "Intensive Care", "Maternity with Neonatal Intensive Care", "Neurosciences", "Orthopedic Care", "Rehabilitation", "Robotic Surgery", "Urgent Care"], "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "