 call u can look it up that your full so ppl don''t waste gas and money.", "author": "Eunice Davis", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100972293302769025848/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-05T05:27:43.218945495Z", "text": "Please do not put yourself or a family member in here. They have the worst doctors here and I also got sexually assaulted by one of the night nurses he was a male African American nurse. I’m guessing he is Nigerian but he worked at night when I was there. I was stuck there for almost two weeks even though I wasn’t even suicidal and went there voluntarily and they would not let me out at all until I called the cops and the number to get this on a case. It was the worst time there and they left us with no water sometimes and the bathrooms were disgusting. Also my family had a horrible time dealing with these people from the outside.", "author": "beautybyana109", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111510428532070222012/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Reviews for UTHealth Houston Harris County Psychiatric Center are mixed, with some patients praising the compassionate staff and supportive environment, while others report negative experiences including long wait times, poor communication, and concerns about safety and treatment.", "about_highlight": "UTHealth Harris County Psychiatric Center (HCPC) is the largest provider of inpatient psychiatric care in Houston, providing compassionate, patient-centered care to 9,000 patients yearly, including adults, adolescents, and children. It also provides outpatient ECT services in its ECT Clinic.\n\nHCPC is the teaching hospital within McGovern Medical School at the University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth). Its team of psychiatrists and psychologists are faculty members in the Louis A. Faillace, MD, Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences, bringing world-class expertise and professional care to behavioral health services across the region.\n\nUTHealth is a member of the Statewide Behavioral Health Coordinating Council, charged by the Texas Legislature with developing a strategic plan to coordinate behavioral health services statewide. HCPC also received a State of Texas Resolution in recognition of its Joint Commission award as a Top Performer in Key Quality Measures.", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=13427157872522784466&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJB-aDUpa_QIYR0m7P5vHYVro", "quality_missing": ["insurance", "team_members", "appointment_url"], "search_keywords": ["mental health", "psychiatry", "psychiatrist", "psychology", "therapist", "counseling", "depression", "anxiety", "tâm lý", "tâm thần", "trầm cảm", "정신과", "심리상담", "心理医生", "精神科", "english", "vietnamese", "tiếng việt", "người việt", "bác sĩ việt", "inpatient psychiatric care", "outpatient ect services", "child & adolescent services", "dual diagnosis program", "interpreter and translation services", "inpatient", "outpatient", "support"], "services_offered": [{"name": "Inpatient Psychiatric Care", "category": "Inpatient", "description": "Compassionate, patient-centered inpatient care for adults, adolescents, and children.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Adults, adolescents, and children requiring inpatient psychiatric treatment."}, {"name": "Outpatient ECT Services", "category": "Outpatient", "description": "Electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) services provided in the ECT Clinic.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients requiring outpatient ECT treatment."}, {"name": "Child & Adolescent Services", "category": "Inpatient", "description": "Inpatient psychiatric services specifically for children and adolescents.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Children and adolescents needing inpatient psychiatric care."}, {"name": "Dual Diagnosis Program", "category": "Inpatient", "description": "Inpatient program