Day pass", "notes": "Good for 24 hours with no limit to the number of times they can be used.", "price": "$13", "category": "parking", "price_range": null}, {"name": "Valet parking", "notes": "Valet locations: Building 105 (Mon-Fri 8am-4pm), Marcus Tower (Mon-Fri 5am-9pm), Emergency department turnaround (24/7).", "price": "$12", "category": "parking", "price_range": null}], "reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-15T01:10:59.420790633Z", "text": "The hospital was nice, considering the reason for the visit.  The doctors were patient and knowledgeable. The staff was friendly.   The nurses, mostly, were great.  Always friendly and willing to help as needed, with a positive attitude, especially Kenny, Dirah, and Ellie in the ICU.  The only negative was an ICU nurse named Haley.  She seemed to show a little too much of an intimate tendency towards male patient, instead of being professional.  It would have been a 5 star if she had behaved properly.", "author": "Chell Mar", "rating": 4, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103881164843114401016/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-11T05:57:15.109318457Z", "text": "Since patient experience has not responded to my three emails I’m reviewing my recent experience at Piedmont Atlanta hospital.  I was there from 11/18/2025-11/22/205.\nMy recent hospitalization at Piedmont Atlanta following a 3 level back surgery has been one the worst experiences ever.  The surgery went smoothly. The aftercare was not adequate at all. The first night the nurse was attentive somewhat because I was coming off of anesthesia and didn’t require much.\nI think it was Thursday that I had to ring the bell for assistance and then it took forever for people to respond. One night I was yelling out for someone to come so I could get pain meds because I couldn’t reach the call button. I asked the last to leave it on the bed. Obviously she didn’t do that because I couldn’t find or reach it.\nMedication was supposed to be given at 8:50 Pm she arrived at 11:14 pm saying she has my medication. My friend called one day to speak with the charge nurse about the lackluster care, she came in once. I don’t remember what she said. I think I felt better by Friday and asked to speak with the manager. I was told she was on vacation and no one was covering her. Then the tech comes in with the contact information for patient experience and within a few minutes someone from “patient experience” came in asking me why didn’t I want the nursing staff to walk me? Which was lie because I didn’t even know that was an option and my frustration was with the lackluster treatment from the nursing staff and medications. I don’t think she really addressed my concerns but she did state that pain medications were PRN. I didn’t know that either but I would think the nursing staff would check on their patients outside of treatment and lab checks. I didn’t have to “ask” for the pain medication any other time. There’s so much more I just can’t write it all. And on top of that the room was not kept too clean and didn’t even flush after me a few times. The last Tech threw the wipes in the toilet. After I already had told here they were not disposable. You wanna know how I know she threw them in the toilet because the last time I struggled to the toilet on my own the toilet was not flush.\nYour people need to do better. Teara the tech, Jennifer from OT and Clement from PT were great. It was an OT person and respiratory person that found me in distress and helped me. Jennifer really helped me after I had been laying in my urine for an hour. The nursing staff didn’t come or they came later. Even though I could barely walk I was so glad to go home.", "author": "Ms. Lis", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101074030452589290448/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-02T03:27:33.449311286Z", "text": "My daughter and I had appointments together last week at the Doris Sheen Breast center.\nI have been going to Piedmont Practically\nAll my life. I was born at the old Piedmont\nYears ago and just happened to live near\nPeachtree where the new Hospital is  Wlocated. I have watched it grow and grow\nand every Doctor I have seen over the years have been amazing. I feel very close to each and every Doctor I have seen. Plus the staff has always been superior compared to other Hospitals I have been to.\nSeriously , our experience at your Breast\nCenter went perfect  My daughter was a little nervous but was immediately put at ease at the front desk. She was adorable.\nIn fact all of the check in girls were lovely.\nWe both had a great experience. My nurse was Debbie who could not have been any nicer. She was great ! My daughter also had a sweet nurse who did her exam. Everyone we came in contact with were\nVery polite and respectful. Dee Glass", "author": "Dee Glass", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104157375401760841532/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-04T17:04:29.756532142Z", "text": "A very friendly, caring and accommodating staff take excellent care of you. Minimal wait time.  A most pleasant experience filled with important knowledgeable information.  Dr. Shore makes you feel most comfortable and relaxed and is very knowledgeable and answers every question thoroughly.  It is so pleasant to not feel rushed. And his advice is priceless.  I look forward to my next visit!", "author": "Layne Taylor", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103229230428953648599/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-08T12:11:38.501885885Z", "text": "Check in was great both ladies were very nice and personable. The mammo tech Morgan was amazing. She was friendly and had a great sense of humor. I appreciate her knowledge and gentle hand as we all know mammograms are very uncomfortable. The US tech was not the best, I felt like she just wanted to get me in and out as quickly as possible. She didn’t answer my questions and I felt very “blown off”.  She could at least smile and have some personality. Also take a minute to answer questions and help me feel like I’ve been heard.", "author": "Brian and Marsha Hanson", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113355660985600724112/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.piedmont.org/locations/piedmont-atlanta", "location": {"latitude": 33.808886799999996, "longitude": -84.394939}, "services": ["Emergency services", "Cancer care", "Heart care", "Orthopedic care", "Neurology services", "Transplant medicine", "Women''s care", "Pregnancy and newborn care", "Weight loss surgery"], "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Nationally recognized quality", "detail": "Named the top acute-care community hospital in Atlanta in U.S. News and World Report''s ''Best Hospitals'' list.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Top-rated patient experience", "detail": "Piedmont Atlanta consistently ranks in the top five among Atlanta hospitals in patient experience scores.", "category": "reviews"}, {"title": "Total care, one destination", "detail": "You''ll find 24-hour emergency services, plus all major medical, diagnostic and surgical specialties on one campus.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Experienced team", "detail": "Staffed by over 1,000 experienced physicians and 4,000 health care professionals.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Located in Buckhead", "detail": "Piedmont Atlanta is conveniently located in Atlanta''s Buckhead neighborhood.", "category": "convenience"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://www.piedmont.org/locations/piedmont-atlanta?utm_source=directorylisting&utm_medium=seo&utm_campaign=10223&y_source=1_MTI5OTY4MzYtNzE1LWxvY2F0aW9uLndlYnNpdGU%3D", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": "https://www.care.piedmon