icine clinic for the whole family in Silicon Valley, I highly recommend this place.", "author": "Kyoungsoo Kim", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103332365012807462588/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-17T02:53:18.369153781Z", "text": "I have been visiting Soo Acupuncture Clinic for the past six months for my back pain and I am very satisfied—I highly recommend it. Out of about five clinics I''ve been to in the last four years in the Bay Area, this one is the most friendly and clean. They are also easy to schedule with and accommodate changes, and I''m happy with the pain relief I feel after the acupuncture and massage.", "author": "윤석", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102378270878376838602/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-29T06:21:34.465490238Z", "text": "Very effective acupuncture & massage therapy keep me and my husband coming back to this clinic.\n\nThe doctor is extremely qualified and you can tell she''s so knowledgeable. The entire staff is very attentive and will really listen to you in order to take care of any kind of bodily pain you might have.\n\nI initially came here for shoulder pain, which improved tremendously after getting treated here consistently (about once every 2 weeks). Now we''re working on my lower back since I have some issues with it from working out and I''m seeing great results with that too.\n\nI cannot recommend this place enough. If you''re dealing with any kind of chronic pain that''s hard to manage, give this clinic a try!!", "author": "Aly Park", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105359294956259083455/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-29T06:36:20.146115796Z", "text": "Highly recommend this place.\n\nI''ve been suffering from neck pain for years and went to a number of acupuncture centers in both Korea and the US. Doctor Soo is definitely one of the best. She performs extremely precise and skillful acupuncture treatment and it works immediately that you could actually feel the pain go away and have much better circulation in your body.\n\nThis place also provides skincare and they took care of a skin concern on my back which was a pain in the butt for a few years.\n\nIf you are looking for an authentic acupuncture treatment clinic, this is the one.", "author": "Brian Yu", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114994910966921726238/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-02-15T01:41:42.784651Z", "text": "I first visited this clinic upon a friend''s recommendation due to neck and shoulder pain. I received acupuncture and massage treatment once a week for about two months, which significantly improved my condition. Since then, I have continued visiting the clinic periodically for over eight months. The clinic is always clean and quiet, providing a comfortable environment to focus on treatment. The staff is incredibly kind, and the doctors communicate well with patients, ensuring a smooth and reassuring experience. My daughter also suffered from chronic abdominal pain for a long time, but thanks to the doctor’s continuous care, she recovered remarkably quickly. She is now pain-free and enjoying a bright and healthy school life. Because of these experiences, my family has complete trust in this clinic. I highly recommend it to anyone seeking effective and compassionate treatment.", "author": "Hyun Kim", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104139951452594176993/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients consistently praise SOO Korean Medicine & Acupuncture Center for its highly effective treatments, clean and welcoming environment, and compassionate, skilled staff. Many reviewers highlight significant pain relief and improved mobility after acupuncture and massage therapies.", "about_highlight": "SOO Korean Medicine & Acupuncture Center, led by SooHee Han (KMD, LA.c), offers holistic Korean Medicine and acupuncture services in Santa Clara, CA. SooHee Han graduated from Dongguk University of Korean Medicine in Korea and is a California licensed acupuncturist. She has extensive experience treating pain patients, as well as pediatric and female patients, providing integrated treatment through pain relief programs, herbal medicine, and specialized programs for holistic health.\n\nThe clinic accepts major insurance plans including Anthem Blue Cross, Cigna, United Healthcare, and Blue Shield, and is currently accepting new clients. Services range from back pain and chronic pain management to women''s health, weight loss, pediatric growth clinic, anti-aging skincare, and more. Treatment approaches include acupuncture, cupping therapy, myofascial release therapy, and MTS needling.\n\nLocated at 3350 Scott Blvd Ste 4902 in Santa Clara, the center is dedicated to unlocking the body''s natural healing ability using time-tested Korean Medicine techniques. Patients can schedule appointments by calling 669-770-5795.", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=6862726806850019165&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJAfBCIRXJj4ARXZ_YqKtNPV8", "quality_missing": ["appointment_url"], "search_keywords": ["acupuncture & tcm", "acupuncture", "chinese medicine", "tcm", "herbal medicine", "cupping", "pain relief", "châm cứu", "đông y", "y học cổ truyền", "한의원", "침술", "한약", "中医", "针灸", "中药", "english", "korean", "한국어", "한인", "한국말", "back pain", "chronic pain", "neck pain", "muscle tension and joint pain", "women''s health", "weight loss", "grow clinic for kids", "anti-aging skincare", "auto mts", "korean medicine", "cupping therapy", "myofascial release therapy", "mts needling", "pain management", "wellness", "pediatric", "cosmetic", "therapy", "approach", "blue cross blue shield", "cigna", "unitedhealthcare", "soohee han", "korean medicine doctor & licensed acupuncturist"], "cultural_context": "Korean Medicine practice led by a Korean Medicine Doctor (KMD) trained at Dongguk University in Korea, offering culturally responsive care for Asian and immigrant communities.", "services_offered": [{"name": "Back Pain", "category": "Pain Management", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Chronic Pain", "category": "Pain Management", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Neck Pain", "category": "Pain Management", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Muscle Tension and Joint Pain", "category": "Pain Management", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Women''s Health", "category": "Women''s Health", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Weight Loss", "category": "Wellness", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Grow Clinic for Kids", "category": "Pediatric", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Children"}, {"name": "Anti-Aging Skincare", "category": "Cosmetic", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Auto MTS", "category": "Therapy", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Acupuncture", "category": "Approach", "description": "Time-tested technique to promote wellness and balance.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Korean Medicine", "category": "Approach", "description": "Holistic Korean Medicine treatments.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Cupping Therapy", "category": "Approach", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Myofascial Release Therapy", "category": "Approach", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "MTS Needling", "category": "Approach", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}], "short_description": "Expert acupuncturist using time-tested Korean Medicine techniques to promote wellness and balance.", "google_website_url": "https://sookoreanmedi.com/", "insurance_accepted": ["Blue Cross Blue Shield", "Cigna", "UnitedHealthcare"], "google_primary_type": "Medical Clinic", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": ["SooHee Han"], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "accepting_new_patients": true, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "3350 Scott Blvd #4902, Santa Clara, CA 95054, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/103332365012807462588", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVj7KAP5secwpWVGtkwwOIkFXT01zVnp5GNaGjrO9WXNZcj3unb=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Kyoungsoo Kim"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/108619127195381310117", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIQBvqFKZLUKUfN0AC8YYA4726BCoO-Uc5kRW7RH8Atr8MhGg=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "김유진"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/113597247749137958403", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXqSn3zsTCkjl_CKADKFRbBQs0279oxL8moaGS1L3sHnikqto4=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "수 한의원 산타클라라, SOO Korean Medicine & Acu Center"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/104464759940292366882", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVkGKfOHFE906z68Rd4jQklH117PBDux6d7AtEBmKxefQEueezR_Q=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jimin Chung"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/101561886284172381834", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJjrF5FMZwjwUWj-MmiQ-PvNDJ3mnGxUKjQF-2nyiCyAkPuBRs=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "dami kim"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-26T10:51:58.359213+00:00', 'soo-korean-medicine-acupuncture-center', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

The Winship Cancer Institute at Emory Midtown, located one block from the hospital, is Georgia''s NCI-designated comprehensive cancer center and won a 2024 Healthcare Design Award from the American Institute of Architects. The hospital also offers specialized wound care and hyperbaric oxygen therapy, full radiology and imaging services, and a 24/7 emergency department. Recognitions include U.S. News & World Report rankings, Magnet® designation for nursing excellence since 2025, and America''s Best Maternity Hospitals 2024 by Newsweek.

The hospital provides a range of patient and visitor resources, including a MyChart patient portal, language interpretation services, and clear financial assistance and price transparency information. It maintains an open visitor policy and is dedicated to non-discrimination, LGBTQIA cultural competency, and respecting patient rights.', '550 Peachtree Street, NE, Atlanta, GA 30308', 'Atlanta', 'GA', '30308', '(404) 686-4411', ARRAY['English', 'Vietnamese']::text[], 'Hospital', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/emory-university-hospital-midtown-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/emory-university-hospital-midtown-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/emory-university-hospital-midtown-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/emory-university-hospital-midtown-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/emory-university-hospital-midtown-google-5.webp"], "rating": 3, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-26T19:46:43.952567524Z", "text": "I just want to say thank you to Tae for how professional and kind she was today. We were definitely frustrated because we confirmed my mom’s appointment this morning around 9:15 AM, drove all the way from Columbus, checked in, and then were told at 3:10 that the appointment had supposedly been rescheduled. So at that point we were hot and confused trying to understand what happened.\n\nEven with all of that, Tae still handled us with patience, professionalism, and care. She didn’t dismiss our frustration and really tried to help find a solution. We truly appreciated her getting someone else to see my mom and even helping with a parking voucher for the inconvenience.\n\nGood customer service is hard to find these days, and Tae genuinely made a stressful situation better. Please let her know we appreciated her.\n\nAppointment at Medical Office Tower. Cardiologist 6th floor", "author": "Tiffany Wright", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100109236942307607172/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-02T17:52:21.139965565Z", "text": "I’m writing this review to recognize the amazing  care teams I had at EUHM and to bring ease to a mom who may be a bit nervous to give birth at this hospital because of things they may have heard online.\n\nI gave birth in March of 2026 at EUHM and from the moment I arrived at L&D I was well taken care of. The triage team, L&D nurses, mother/baby nurses, lactation consultants, and pediatricians made my experience so memorable. They took great care of me and baby from beginning to end. I chose to deliver unmedicated and had some minor post birth concerns. The doctors and nurses listened to my concerns and checked in regularly to ensure I was healing appropriately. I never felt unsafe in the care of EUHM and that’s important as a woman of color in Atlanta. My one word of advice is to not be afraid to advocate for yourself. Know your birth plan and ensure your doctor is aligned. However, your baby does not read the birth plan so make sure you trust your provider to pivot when necessary.\n\nI want to give a special recognition to one of my amazing L&D nurses (Jordan) and my doctor (Dr.Eaton). The whole care team was special, but these 2 left a lasting impression on both me and my husband. I would recommend a friend to deliver here and would do it all over again. Thank you EUHM.", "author": "Abreona Nixon", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117358215040029037306/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-08T15:47:45.205285599Z", "text": "I want to share the positive experience I had at Emory Hospital Midtown over the weekend. The staff was amazing—professional, courteous, and truly comforting from start to finish. I was diagnosed with diabetes, and they made sure I understood that it wasn’t a life-ending diagnosis. They kept me calm, informed, and reassured throughout the entire process.\n\nThe hospital was spotless, and parking was easy with plenty of available spaces. Special shoutout to Jaelin, Amanda, Jennifer, and Glenn for their exceptional care. Unit 71 is absolutely top-notch—professional, compassionate, and one of the best teams I’ve ever encountered.\n\nUnder the circumstances, this was honestly one of the best emergency room visits I’ve had in my entire life. They truly did an incredible job.", "author": "Brian Lawson", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100706151112158668165/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-30T22:19:02.430229853Z", "text": "My experience at this hospital was totally amazing. I came in for sickle cell crisis, and the doctor was so so nice and he took care of my pain. The nurses were amazing. My doctor name was Dr. Ross. He listened to me. He understood me and he took care of everything to make me feel comfortable and my nurse my dhea and a charged nurse Miss Randy did my ultrasound IV. She was totally amazing. Both of them are immaculate and perfect person. At least my experience here was amazing and it’s probably one of the best hospitals I’ve ever been to in Atlanta very way better than Gwinnett cause Gwinnett was horrible. Thank you.", "author": "Tasha Wallace", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101647044162441873175/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-10T21:46:25.128501018Z", "text": "I want to extend my sincere gratitude to the nursing team on the 7th floor at Emory Healthcare for the exceptional care they provided to my father.\n\nIn particular, I want to recognize Takisha, Kate, Samaria, Maria and Overcomer. Each of them showed not only a high level of professionalism, but also genuine compassion and attentiveness. They took the time to connect with both my father and our family in a way that truly mattered.\n\nWhat stood out most was how they brought warmth and light into a stressful situation. We shared laughs, had real conversations, and they made my father smile during a time when that meant everything. That kind of care goes far beyond medical treatment, it makes a lasting impact.\n\nI also want to acknowledge the broader team, as there were many others who contributed to the same level of thoughtful and attentive care. It’s clear that this unit operates with a strong sense of teamwork and dedication.\n\nThank you for treating my father with such dignity, kindness, and humanity. It did not go unnoticed, and it will not be forgotten.\n\nOne downside would be that Valet wasn’t available on the weekends. But it is what it is", "author": "morgan alexander", "rating": 4, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110323085553985225284/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.emoryhealthcare.org/locations/hospitals/emory-university-hospital-midtown", "location": {"latitude": 33.7686442, "longitude": -84.38619290000001}, "services": ["Bariatric Center", "Emergency Department", "Radiology & Imaging", "Wound Care and Hyperbaric Oxygen Therapy", "Winship Cancer Institute at Emory Midtown"], "insurance": {"notes": "Links to insurance information and price transparency pages are available. No specific insurance plans are listed on this page.", "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Level 1 Emergency Cardiac Care Center & Certified Primary Stroke Center", "detail": "The hospital is designated as a Level 1 Emergency Cardiac Care Center and a Certified Primary Stroke Center, ensuring expert care for heart and stroke emergencies.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "MBSAQIP Accredited Comprehensive Bariatric Center", "detail": "The Emory Bariatric Center is an MBSAQIP Accredited Comprehensive Facility and named a Center of Excellence by most major health insurers.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Magnet® Designation for Nursing Excellence", "detail": "Magnet® designated since 2025 for excellence in nursing professionalism, teamwork and superiority in patient care.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Award-Winning Winship Cancer Institute", "detail": "Winship Cancer Institute at Emory Midtown is Georgia''s NCI-designated comprehensive cancer center and won a 2024 Healthcare Design Award from the American Institute of Architects.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "24/7 Emergency Department", "detail": "Emergency medical doctors and nursing specialists are always on-site, 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.", "category": "convenience"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://www.emoryhealthcare.org/locations/hospitals/emory-university-hospital-midtown?&utm_campaign=brand_euh_ra_gmb-locations&utm_source=google&utm_medium=gmb&utm_content=gmb_locations?&utm_campaign=brand_all_non&utm_source=google&utm_medium=gmb&utm_content=gmb-locations", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": "https://www.emoryhealthcare.org/patients-visitors/appointments", "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": null, "online_booking_available": null, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": true, "scout_query": "Vietnamese speaking hospital in Atlanta, GA", "search_text": "hospital | english | vietnamese | tiếng việt | người việt | bác sĩ việt | bariatric center | emergency department | radiology & imaging | wound care and hyperbaric oxygen therapy | winship cancer institute at emory midtown | weight loss | emergency | diagnostic imaging | wound care | cancer care", "google_types": ["hospital", "health", "point_of_interest", "service", "establishment"], "open_weekend"