at’s important as a woman of color in Atlanta. My one word of advice is to not be afraid to advocate for yourself. Know your birth plan and ensure your doctor is aligned. However, your baby does not read the birth plan so make sure you trust your provider to pivot when necessary.\n\nI want to give a special recognition to one of my amazing L&D nurses (Jordan) and my doctor (Dr.Eaton). The whole care team was special, but these 2 left a lasting impression on both me and my husband. I would recommend a friend to deliver here and would do it all over again. Thank you EUHM.", "author": "Abreona Nixon", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117358215040029037306/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-08T15:47:45.205285599Z", "text": "I want to share the positive experience I had at Emory Hospital Midtown over the weekend. The staff was amazing—professional, courteous, and truly comforting from start to finish. I was diagnosed with diabetes, and they made sure I understood that it wasn’t a life-ending diagnosis. They kept me calm, informed, and reassured throughout the entire process.\n\nThe hospital was spotless, and parking was easy with plenty of available spaces. Special shoutout to Jaelin, Amanda, Jennifer, and Glenn for their exceptional care. Unit 71 is absolutely top-notch—professional, compassionate, and one of the best teams I’ve ever encountered.\n\nUnder the circumstances, this was honestly one of the best emergency room visits I’ve had in my entire life. They truly did an incredible job.", "author": "Brian Lawson", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100706151112158668165/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-30T22:19:02.430229853Z", "text": "My experience at this hospital was totally amazing. I came in for sickle cell crisis, and the doctor was so so nice and he took care of my pain. The nurses were amazing. My doctor name was Dr. Ross. He listened to me. He understood me and he took care of everything to make me feel comfortable and my nurse my dhea and a charged nurse Miss Randy did my ultrasound IV. She was totally amazing. Both of them are immaculate and perfect person. At least my experience here was amazing and it’s probably one of the best hospitals I’ve ever been to in Atlanta very way better than Gwinnett cause Gwinnett was horrible. Thank you.", "author": "Tasha Wallace", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101647044162441873175/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-10T21:46:25.128501018Z", "text": "I want to extend my sincere gratitude to the nursing team on the 7th floor at Emory Healthcare for the exceptional care they provided to my father.\n\nIn particular, I want to recognize Takisha, Kate, Samaria, Maria and Overcomer. Each of them showed not only a high level of professionalism, but also genuine compassion and attentiveness. They took the time to connect with both my father and our family in a way that truly mattered.\n\nWhat stood out most was how they brought warmth and light into a stressful situation. We shared laughs, had real conversations, and they made my father smile during a time when that meant everything. That kind of care goes far beyond medical treatment, it makes a lasting impact.\n\nI also want to acknowledge the broader team, as there were many others who contributed to the same level of thoughtful and attentive care. It’s clear that this unit operates with a strong sense of teamwork and dedication.\n\nThank you for treating my father with such dignity, kindness, and humanity. It did not go unnoticed, and it will not be forgotten.\n\nOne downside would be that Valet wasn’t available on the weekends. But it is what it is", "author": "morgan alexander", "rating": 4, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110323085553985225284/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients generally appreciate the professionalism and kindness of staff at Emory University Hospital Midtown, though some experienced scheduling frustrations. Many highlight exceptional care, especially in labor and delivery, emergency services, and specialized treatments.", "about_highlight": "Emory University Hospital Midtown is a full-service, more than 600-bed specialized care hospital in the heart of Atlanta. Since 1908, it has provided outstanding quality healthcare, consistently ranking among Georgia''s top hospitals for cancer, cardiology and heart surgery, ear/nose/throat, diabetes and endocrinology, gynecology, nephrology, neurology/neurosurgery, geriatrics, and more. The hospital is a Level 1 Emergency Cardiac Care Center, a Certified Primary Stroke Center, a MBSAQIP Accredited Comprehensive Bariatric Center, and has a Level III Neonatal Intensive Care Unit (NICU). With more than 2,000 physicians across a vast array of specialties, its team collaborates to deliver comprehensive care and quality outcomes, supported by advanced research and ties to Emory University.\n\nThe Winship Cancer Institute at Emory Midtown, located one block from the hospital, is Georgia''s NCI-designated comprehensive cancer center and won a 2024 Healthcare Design Award from the American Institute of Architects. The hospital also offers specialized wound care and hyperbaric oxygen therapy, full radiology and imaging services, and a 24/7 emergency department. Recognitions include U.S. News & World Report rankings, Magnet® designation for nursing excellence since 2025, and America''s Best Maternity Hospitals 2024 by Newsweek.\n\nThe hospital provides a range of patient and visitor resources, including a MyChart patient portal, language interpretation services, and clear financial assistance and price transparency information. It maintains an open visitor policy and is dedicated to non-discrimination, LGBTQIA cultural competency, and respecting patient rights.", "appointment_url": "https://www.emoryhealthcare.org/patients-visitors/appointments", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=15043808532116501154&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJ42AWonoE9YgRonLLiSdYxtA", "quality_missing": ["insurance", "team_members"], "search_keywords": ["hospital", "english", "vietnamese", "tiếng việt", "người việt", "bác sĩ việt", "bariatric center", "emergency department", "radiology & imaging", "wound care and hyperbaric oxygen therapy", "winship cancer institute at emory midtown", "weight loss", "emergency", "diagnostic imaging", "wound care", "cancer care"], "services_offered": [{"name": "Bariatric Center", "category": "Weight Loss", "description": "Offers weight loss expertise, treatments and technology, including the safest and most effective weight loss surgery techniques. Partnered with major health insurers as a Center of Excellence.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients seeking medical or surgical weight loss options."}, {"name": "Emergency Department", "category": "Emergency", "description": "Open 24/7, with emergency medical doctors and nursing specialists always on-site. Patients are triaged at arrival and seen in priority order based on the seriousness of their condition.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients with urgent or emergency medical needs."}, {"name": "Radiology & Imaging", "category": "Diagnostic Imaging", "description": "Advanced imaging technology including Bone Density (DEXA), CT scan, Fluoroscopy, Interventional radiology, MRI, Nuclear medicine, PET Scan, Ultrasound, and X-ray. Located on the ground floor.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients needing diagnostic imaging services."}, {"name": "Wound Care and Hyperbaric Oxygen Therapy", "category": "Wound Care", "description": "Specialized wound care treatment including hyperbaric oxygen therapy for wounds that aren''t healing following radiation therapy, other chronic or non-healing wounds, and carbon monoxide poisoning. Treatments provided between 7 a.m. and 2 p.m., Monday through Friday.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients with chronic or non-healing wounds, or requiring hyperbaric oxygen therapy."}, {"name": "Winship Cancer Institute at Emory Midtown", "category": "Cancer Care", "description": "Georgia''s NCI-designated comprehensive cancer center, pioneering advances in prevention, diagnosis, and treatment. Located one block from the hospital.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients seeking cancer care and treatment."}], "short_description": "Emory University Hospital Midtown is a full-service, more than 600-bed specialized care hospital in the heart of Atlanta, consistently ranked among Georgia''s top hospitals for cancer, cardiology, and many other specialties. It is a Level 1 Emergency Cardiac Care Center, a Certified Primary Stroke Center, and home to an award-winning cancer institute.", "google_website_url": "https://www.emoryhealthcare.org/locations/hospitals/emory-university-hospital-midtown?&utm_campaign=brand_euh_ra_gmb-locations&utm_source=google&utm_medium=gmb&utm_content=gmb_locations?&utm_campaign=brand_all_non&utm_source=google&utm_medium=gmb&utm_content=gmb-locations", "google_primary_type": "Hospital", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "550 Peachtree St NE, Atlanta, GA 30308, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/104774663059562237282", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWLfHuyaFLKbhKfDTiQT9XjzTy5l9r7TbaRV95Oty6f5OtLw7eFAQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Otis Lee"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/117228881186763617643", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLMCm0X8b6qTE_B9rmRPau6SB_H3AI6lTSaWBvr9n10MdwTDg=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Elisa Davidsen"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/114894022645493611460", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUFHsInz-2Prrfg9uJL3uP_O0fPPuKNF05RA2NpfnD0tIfbBeY=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Keith Henderson"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/114894022645493611460", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUFHsInz-2Prrfg9uJL3uP_O0fPPuKNF05RA2NpfnD0tIfbBeY=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Keith Henderson"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/118013236208234950808", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJo2sZdNALShihMsZIf4ZOVv5aM-rIUxKyFwTrzoL7BHggl4H5X=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Hunter -"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-25T20:58:36.007989+00:00', 'emory-university-hospital-midtown', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

The center is deeply committed to community and patient-centered care, providing a wide range of services from primary care to specialized programs like the Bailey-Boushay House, the first U.S. skilled nursing and outpatient program for people with HIV/AIDS. For added accessibility, virtual urgent care and telehealth options are available.

Virginia Mason Medical Center also prioritizes inclusive care with language and interpreter services and a dedicated focus on diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging. Patients can easily manage their health through the CommonSpirit Patient Portal and mobile app, which has replaced the MyVirginiaMason portal.', '1100 9th Ave.', 'Seattle', 'WA', '98101', '206-624-1144', ARRAY['English', 'Vietnamese']::text[], 'Hospital', TRUE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/virginia-mason-medical-center-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/virginia-mason-medical-center-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/virginia-mason-medical-center-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/virginia-mason-medical-center-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/virginia-mason-medical-center-google-5.webp"], "rating": 3.9, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-06-06T18:49:53.109784382Z", "text": "I’ve been a Virginia Mason patient for 50 years. Their care givers are great…merger with Franciscan?  Horrible and Incompetent management. This review is about Franciscan management choices impacting the patient experience. This is the 30 minute line to check in. This is almost two months after the disastrous implementation. No added check in  staff to ease patients pain. Julie Manas the President sent an apology but has not responded by actually adding staff. There are now far fewer check in staff during this disasterois takeover. They cancelled standing appointments already in the system, poorly executed the rollout, have not addressed additional staffing to ease the pain. This is months after the rollout. Sheer incompetence. And on top of it all it appears they may be planning to rename the long standing institution St. Anne? There were confusing St. Anne signs everywhere. Really? How tone deaf. Again this is not a reflection of the care givers and Doctors and Nurses. It is a comment on a very incompetent merger management. We don’t need an apology we need solutions Julie Manas.", "author": "Polly Cee", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109218419458336007807/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-15T01:09:47.212772121Z", "text": "This was not my first colonoscopy. This experience was so different from previous experiences I must commend Dr. Vedamurthy and the team for the care I received. I have never felt more cared for and considered in any medical experience. I felt seen not solely as a patient, but more importantly, as a person.\n\nI appreciated the candor when I expressed my concerns. I was concerned about the prep,  the possible discovery of cancer and death. I need not have worried.\n\nThe nurses and technicians never left me alone as I waited. I appreciated their relaxed demeanor.  They were all professional, knowledgeable, and kind.\n\nI appreciated Dr. Marko and his part of the procedure. Previously, general anesthesia has left me feeling awful. I felt fine when I returned home.\n\nThough my procedure was late Friday afternoon everyone felt fresh rather than tired at the end of the week. Excellent communication and teamwork made me feel safe.\n\nThank you for the care and consideration I received.", "author": "Barbara Wu", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117495258505364090380/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-11T17:42:06.649872846Z", "text": "​I am writing this review because my recent post-surgical stay at this hospital was an absolute nightmare, and I felt completely neglected and mistreated by the staff.\n​Immediately following my surgery, I was wheeled into my room and forced to struggle into my hospital bed completely on my own without any physical assistance from the staff. To make matters worse, my room''s restroom had zero basic toiletries provided.\n​The nursing care was dangerously slow and punitive. When I used my call light, it took forever for anyone to respond. When I was in severe pain (a 7/10) and asked for my prescribed pain medication, the nurse refused to give it to me until she checked my blood pressure. She explicitly told me that she would only give me the medication if my blood pressure went up to \"prove\" I was in pain. This is an completely outdated, cruel, and incorrect way to manage a post-op patient''s suffering.\n​Communication from the medical team was non-existent. My doctor, Dr. Kyle A. Williams-Brown, came to see me the next day but provided absolutely no important information about my surgery or condition. Later, when I requested to speak with him again to get actual answers about my health, I literally heard Dr. Williams-Brown standing right outside my door talking to the nurse, stating that he \"couldn''t see me.\"\n​I felt completely abandoned, unsafe, and dehumanized. The only thing I wanted to do was leave. Nobody should be treated this way after undergoing surgery. I highly advise avoiding this facility if you expect competent, compassionate care.", "author": "Aminata diallo", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104597567716994243491/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-16T05:41:11.269060164Z", "text": "I was in town for work training and ended up dislocating my right shoulder. I was in excruciating pain. But first, I need to praise my very compassionate EMTs that brought me to the ER, Marcus & Eden, thank you for delivering me safely and quickly as possible. Thank you for your gentleness, patience and kindness. Now to ER staff. Ashley, Tine, Dr. Simons the young tech who helped me dress, and my XRay tech (sorry for not retaining your name info), you all were an absolutely amazing team. I just want you to know, from a home healthcare worker to professional healthcare workers, please know that you are seen and deeply appreciated. Each of you were right where you needed to be for me that evening, and I know I was blessed to have you all. Deepest regards- Deborah Bennett; Billings, MT", "author": "Deb Bennett", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105786005873811287217/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-18T23:03:19.593694608Z", "text": "The physicians and clinical staff at this hospital are professional and compassionate. Unfortunately, the administrative side of the organization is the exact opposite.\n\nspeaking from my own experience, I was overcharged by thousands of dollars, and when I contacted the billing department to dispute the charges, I was met with hostility, dismissiveness, and outright accusations instead of assistance. It took multiple formal letters and repeated escalation before anyone in leadership finally acknowledged the issue and addressed it seriously.\n\nMore recently, the hospital’s transition to a new patient portal was handled so poorly that I temporarily lost access to essential medication. When I called for help, the response was shockingly indifferent. The representative was rude, unhelpful, and simply told me to return to a phone queue I had already spent hours waiting in.\n\nMistakes can happen at any organization. What matters is how those mistakes are handled. In this case, the pattern is consistent: poor communication, lack of accountability, and open disrespect toward patients trying to resolve legitimate problems.\n\nThe quality of the medical care at VMFH is hugely undermined by an administrative system that appears deeply dysfunctional. Based on my experience, I would strongly caution anyone against relying on this hospital unless absolutely necessary.", "author": "Ashkan S", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104262369581436919690/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.vmfh.org/our-hospitals/virginia-mason-medical-center", "location": {"latitude": 47.609935, "longitude": -122.3275125}, "services": ["Cancer Care", "Cardiology", "Emergency Department", "Orthopedics & Sports Medicine", "Primary Care", "Urgent Care", "Bailey-Boushay House", "Laboratories", "Virtual Urgent Care", "Telehealth", "Gynecology", "Obstetrics", "Concierge Medicine", "Executive Health Program", "Neurosciences & Spine", "Digestive Health", "Weight Management"], "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Nationally Ranked Hospital", "detail": "Consistently ranked among the best hospitals in Washington by Healthgrades and U.S. News & World Report.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Emergency Department with Lower Wait Times", "detail": "Emergency Department offers wait times lower than the national and Washington state averages.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Comprehensive Cancer Care", "detail": "Nationally renowned cancer experts deliver state-of-the-art cancer care with exceptional outcomes.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Language and Interpreter Services", "detail": "Offers language and interpreter services to support diverse patient populations.", "category": "access"}, {"title": "Virtual Urgent Care Available", "detail": "Virtual urgent care and telehealth services are offered for convenient access to care.", "category": "technology"}, {"title": "Patient Portal & Mobile App", "detail": "The CommonSpirit Patient Portal and mobile app allows patients to manage their care online.", "category": "technology"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://www.vmfh.org/our-hospitals/virginia-mason-medical-center", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_u