 administrative side of the organization is the exact opposite.\n\nspeaking from my own experience, I was overcharged by thousands of dollars, and when I contacted the billing department to dispute the charges, I was met with hostility, dismissiveness, and outright accusations instead of assistance. It took multiple formal letters and repeated escalation before anyone in leadership finally acknowledged the issue and addressed it seriously.\n\nMore recently, the hospital’s transition to a new patient portal was handled so poorly that I temporarily lost access to essential medication. When I called for help, the response was shockingly indifferent. The representative was rude, unhelpful, and simply told me to return to a phone queue I had already spent hours waiting in.\n\nMistakes can happen at any organization. What matters is how those mistakes are handled. In this case, the pattern is consistent: poor communication, lack of accountability, and open disrespect toward patients trying to resolve legitimate problems.\n\nThe quality of the medical care at VMFH is hugely undermined by an administrative system that appears deeply dysfunctional. Based on my experience, I would strongly caution anyone against relying on this hospital unless absolutely necessary.", "author": "Ashkan S", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104262369581436919690/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients report a mix of exceptional clinical care and significant frustrations with administrative processes, particularly post-merger management and billing issues.", "about_highlight": "Virginia Mason Medical Center is one of the premier health care facilities in the Pacific Northwest, consistently ranked among the best hospitals in Washington by Healthgrades and U.S. News & World Report. As part of the Virginia Mason Franciscan Health system, one of the largest in the Seattle-Tacoma area, the center offers a full spectrum of nationally renowned services including cancer care, cardiology, orthopedics and sports medicine, and emergency care with lower than average wait times.\n\nThe center is deeply committed to community and patient-centered care, providing a wide range of services from primary care to specialized programs like the Bailey-Boushay House, the first U.S. skilled nursing and outpatient program for people with HIV/AIDS. For added accessibility, virtual urgent care and telehealth options are available.\n\nVirginia Mason Medical Center also prioritizes inclusive care with language and interpreter services and a dedicated focus on diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging. Patients can easily manage their health through the CommonSpirit Patient Portal and mobile app, which has replaced the MyVirginiaMason portal.", "appointment_url": "https://www.vmfh.org/content/vmfhorg/en/our-hospitals/virginia-mason-medical-center/patient-visitors/make-an-appointment", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=10908412116613558774&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJx3kMjY8NkFQR9nFRWgZ3Ypc", "quality_missing": ["insurance", "team_members"], "search_keywords": ["hospital", "english", "vietnamese", "tiếng việt", "người việt", "bác sĩ việt", "cancer care", "cardiology", "emergency department", "orthopedics & sports medicine", "primary care", "urgent care", "bailey-boushay house", "laboratories", "virtual urgent care", "telehealth", "gynecology", "obstetrics", "concierge medicine", "executive health program", "neurosciences & spine", "digestive health", "weight management", "specialty care", "emergency", "diagnostic"], "services_offered": [{"name": "Cancer Care", "category": "Specialty Care", "description": "Nationally renowned cancer experts delivering state-of-the-art cancer care and exceptional outcomes.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Cardiology", "category": "Specialty Care", "description": "Devoted to maximizing patients'' quality