 Hospital have a 24-hour emergency room?", "@type": "Question", "acceptedAnswer": {"text": "Yes, we offer 24/7 emergency room services with on-site MRI, CT imaging, surgical suites, and lab. Walk-ins welcome, no appointment needed.", "@type": "Answer"}}, {"name": "Is Twelve Oaks Hospital the same as River Oaks Hospital?", "@type": "Question", "acceptedAnswer": {"text": "Yes, River Oaks Hospital & Clinics is located at 4200 Twelve Oaks Place in Houston TX 77027. Some people refer to it as \"Twelve Oaks Hospital\" or \"12 Oaks Hospital.\"", "@type": "Answer"}}, {"name": "Does River Oaks Hospital accept my insurance?", "@type": "Question", "acceptedAnswer": {"text": "Yes, we are in-network for most major insurance plans and accept worker''s compensation and Medicare. Call (713) 980-7900 to verify your coverage.", "@type": "Answer"}}]}], "@context": "https://schema.org"}], "quality_missing": ["languages (non-default)", "team_members"], "search_keywords": ["hospital", "english", "24/7 emergency room", "diagnostic imaging", "surgery", "vascular care", "subacute trauma", "pharmacy", "multispecialty clinics", "emergency", "diagnostic", "surgical", "specialty", "primary care", "most major insurance plans", "worker''s compensation", "medicare"], "services_offered": [{"name": "24/7 Emergency Room", "category": "Emergency", "description": "Walk-in emergency care with on-site MRI, CT imaging, surgical suites, and lab. No appointment needed.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients requiring immediate medical attention"}, {"name": "Diagnostic Imaging", "category": "Diagnostic", "description": "Advanced imaging including MRI, CT, and ultrasound for accurate diagnosis.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients needing diagnostic imaging"}, {"name": "Surgery", "category": "Surgical", "description": "Surgical suites for a range of procedures, supported by on-site imaging and pharmacy.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients requiring surgical intervention"}, {"name": "Vascular Care", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Specialized vascular care as part of the hospital''s multispecialty services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients with vascular conditions"}, {"name": "Subacute Trauma", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Specialized program for subacute trauma care, coordinated with emergency and surgical services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients recovering from trauma"}, {"name": "Pharmacy", "category": "Pharmacy", "description": "On-site pharmacy for convenient medication access.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "All patients"}, {"name": "Multispecialty Clinics", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Access to multiple specialties under one roof for coordinated care.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients needing specialist consultations"}], "short_description": "River Oaks Hospital Houston – 24/7 ER, surgery, MRI/CT imaging & vascular care. Walk-ins welcome. Call (713) 980-7900.", "google_website_url": "https://adhealthcare.com/locations/river-oaks/", "insurance_accepted": ["Most major insurance plans", "Worker''s Compensation", "Medicare"], "google_primary_type": "General Hospital", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "accepting_new_patients": true, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "4200 Twelve Oaks Pl, Houston, TX 77027, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/108610639089564269940", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWQfnCxhGxu71GXgqrBz04CbTjT6cC0qy13u3VhwItnHG0QxgjY=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "River Oaks Hospital & Clinics"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/111565527287783571090", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU_FO4EQS8bPNnydZMMNOfo5JOf7a0gh3xF8jmV_7XvZFRB49LR=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "David Linh Doan"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/108610639089564269940", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWQfnCxhGxu71GXgqrBz04CbTjT6cC0qy13u3VhwItnHG0QxgjY=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "River Oaks Hospital & Clinics"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/108610639089564269940", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWQfnCxhGxu71GXgqrBz04CbTjT6cC0qy13u3VhwItnHG0QxgjY=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "River Oaks Hospital & Clinics"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/108610639089564269940", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWQfnCxhGxu71GXgqrBz04CbTjT6cC0qy13u3VhwItnHG0QxgjY=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "River Oaks Hospital & Clinics"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-25T14:17:19.008697+00:00', 'river-oaks-hospital-clinics', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

The clinic offers care in many languages and dialects, including English, Cantonese, Mandarin, Toishan, Vietnamese, Tagalog, Burmese, Korean, Spanish, and Hindi. The unique multilingual and culturally sensitive direct service staff allows patients to adequately express themselves in a familiar environment to increase the relevancy and excellence of care they receive. Health education programs and health promotion, which bridge the gap between Western and Asian medical practices, are available at the clinic and through social media.

NEMS is a licensed community clinic organization, Health Center Program grantee under 42 U.S.C. § 254b, and a deemed Public Health Service employee under 42 U.S.C. §§ 233(g)-(n). Their mission is to provide affordable, comprehensive, compassionate and quality health care services in a linguistically competent and culturally sensitive manner to improve the health and well-being of our community.', '1870 Lundy Avenue, San Jose, CA 95131', 'San Jose', 'CA', '95131', '1-888-500-1886', ARRAY['Hindi', 'Spanish', 'Cantonese', 'Burmese', 'Mandarin', 'English', 'Toishan', 'Tagalog', 'Korean', 'Vietnamese']::text[], 'Community Health Center', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/north-east-medical-services-nems-1870-lundy-clinic-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/north-east-medical-services-nems-1870-lundy-clinic-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/north-east-medical-services-nems-1870-lundy-clinic-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/north-east-medical-services-nems-1870-lundy-clinic-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/north-east-medical-services-nems-1870-lundy-clinic-google-5.webp"], "rating": 3.8, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-13T00:57:29.570855924Z", "text": "Absolutely not a place you want to be ever seen!! It takes now them 3 months to schedule you to see your doctor.  This has been going on for a while now, and I am done with this place.   I have been going there for @ 2years and instead of treating their patients the right way, it''s the opposite!  The longer you stay there, the worst it gets!!   You can get an appointment for months.\nPlease do yourself a favor, find a doctor elsewhere that will appreciate to have you as a patient.", "author": "Catherine Cosse", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116937957055182738125/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-03T01:55:55.519084467Z", "text": "This is for the dental appointment. Dental assistants have zero patience with kids. My daughter had the x-ray done, and afterward, we already told the staffs my daughter only wanted a checkup and no tooth cleaning due to having loose tooth. The assistant still set up and tested the tools which had sounds that really made us uncomfortable. My daughter started to get nervous and did not want to lay down and started crying. I tried to encourage her to lay down and open her mouth, and I communicated with my daughter in English and Cantonese ourselves. We did not need any translators. Then out of nowhere the assistant brought in a Cantonese speaking staff, who just said things like, “Oh if you don’t get a clean up, you may have painful cavities”, “you should not act this way in your age”, blablabla, typical way to threaten instead of soothing. It was no help at all. They make you feel like you are wasting their time, and they do not allow kids to have some down time.\n\nDo not leave kids alone with them. You never know what they will say to your kids and traumatize them. We will not come again.", "author": "Polly Chiu", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116952268779697599484/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-03-27T04:10:13.321902883Z", "text": "NEMS is, quite honestly, one of the BEST providers around -- it provides in-person translators for patients, excellent services, and even provides a transportation service (NEMS PACE) for the elderly or those who are otherwise unable to drive. For those who plan to stay in network, only need primary care, or need their translation services, NEMS is superb. From the perspective of a medical professional, NEMS is cooperative and efficient; they answer the phone, generally get back to insurance requests in a timely manner, and are overall polite. I''ve personally had EXCELLENT experiences with Crystal from NEMS PACE, she is always kind and very thorough (please give her a raise!).\n\nHowever, for out-of-direct-network services, they are one of the WORST insurance companies to work with. Because NEMS tends to withhold patient payments, other practices are hesitant to accept NEMS, so your base provider network is small outside of the NEMS network; this makes it a nightmare for non-NEMS providers to refer patients out to other services they may need. For patients who require specialty care (ie. surgical oncology, orthopedics, psychiatry, etc) this is DETRIMENTAL to your health and care -- insurance companies like Optum or SCCIPA will be a much better fit due to the larger out-of-insurance provider network. Please beware if you are a patient requiring special services!", "author": "RaspberryJuice27", "rating": 4, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105571530489700579055/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-20T16:16:32.634248469Z", "text": "Clinic was very clean, very responsive, neatly maintained , easy to make appointment , easy for parking , Dr. Hou Leong, MD  was excellent and very responsive , paid attention to details and caring. Appointment was fast and clear no waiting time at all.", "author": "Mrudula", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101644992843962803738/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-09-09T16:26:12.904681270Z", "text": "All medical staff and doctors are here to help the patient. They are polite, helpful, kind and always ready to resolve your medical questions.\n\nAs a patient, I feel the patient experience is extraordinary, and I would come back again for any other medical assistance", "author": "Xiaofei Z.", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104000548498629367477/reviews"}], "website": "https://nems.org", "location": {"latitude": 37.3925936, "longitude": -121.89002920000001}, "services": ["Internal Medicine", "Family Practice", "Pediatrics", "Dental", "Optometry", "Acupuncture", "Chiropractic", "Laboratory", "Radiology", "Pharmacy", "Endocrinology", "Behavioral Health", "Health Education", "Member Services"], "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Multilingual Staff", "detail": "Care available in English, Cantonese, Mandarin, Toishan, Vietnamese, Tagalog, Burmese, Korean, Spanish, and Hindi.", "category": "culture"}, {"title": "Comprehensive Services", "detail": "Offers Internal Medicine, Family Practice, Pediatrics, Dental, Optometry, Acupuncture, Chiropractic, Radiology, Pharmacy, and more.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Federally Qualified Health Center", "detail": "NEMS is an FQHC, providing care to uninsured and low-income patients.", "category": "insurance"}, {"title": "NCQA Patient Centered Medical Home", "detail": "Attained NCQA PCMH Level 3 recognition.", "category": "technology"}, {"title": "Extended Hours", "detail": "Clinic open Monday to Friday 8:00 AM - 6:00 PM and Saturday 8:00 AM - 12:00 PM, 1:00 PM - 5:00 PM.", "category": "convenience"}], "price_tier": "$", "source_url": "https://nems.org/about-us/#locations", "appointment": {"booking_note": "Call 1-888-500-1886 or use MyChart for online scheduling (Primary Medical Care, Dental and Nutrition). New patients should register first at Become a Member page.", "appointment_url": "https://mychart.nems.org/", "new_patient_note": "If you are new to NEMS, please register first by visiting our ''Become a Member'' page.", "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": true, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": false, "scout_query": "Vietnamese speaking medical clinic in San Jose, CA", "search_text": "community health center | community health | fqhc | sliding scale | medicaid | medicare | low cost | trung tâm y tế cộng đồng | 커뮤니티 헬스 | 社区医疗中心 | hindi | spanish | cantonese | chinese | 粤语 | 广东话 | tiếng quảng đông | burmese | mandarin | 中文 | 普通话 | 国语 | tiếng trung | tiếng phổ thông | english | toishan | tagalog | korean | 한국어 | 한인 | 한국말 | vietnamese | tiếng việt | người việt | bác sĩ việt | internal medicine | family practice | pediatrics | dental | optometry | acupuncture | chiropractic | laboratory | radiology | pharmacy | endocrinology | behavioral health | health education | member services | primary care | preventive", "google_types": ["medical_clinic", "medical_lab", "dentist", "pharmacy", "doctor", "health", "store", "point_of_interest", "service", "establishment"], "open_weekend": true, "rating_count": 133, "language_note": "NEMS targets the medically underserved population, many of whom are uninsured or low income. The clinic offers care in many languages and dialects including English, Cantonese, Mandarin, Toishan, Vietnamese, Tagalog, Burmese, Korean, Spanish, and Hindi. Health education programs bridge the gap between Western and Asian medical practices.", "open_saturday": true, "quality_score": 92, "working_hours": {"friday": "8:00 AM – 6:00 PM", "monday": "8:00 AM – 6:00 PM", "sunday": "Closed", "tuesday": "8:00 AM – 6:00 PM", "saturday": "8:00 AM – 12:00 PM, 1:00 – 5:00 PM", "thursday": "8:00 AM – 6:00 PM", "wednesday": "8:00 AM – 6:00 PM"}, "gallery_images": ["https://www.nems.org/wp-content/uploads/1870lundy2.jpg"], "review_profile": {"rating": 3.8, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Compassionate care", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight compassionate care in their feedback."}, {"theme": "Friendly staff", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight friendly staff in their feedback."}, {"theme": "Clear explanations", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight clear explanations in their feedback."}, {"theme": "Comfortable visits", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight comfortable visits in their feedback."}], "summary": "North East Medical Services (NEMS) - 1870 Lundy Clinic has a 3.8 star Google rating from 133 Google reviews. Patients commonly mention compassionate care, friendly staff, clear explanations, comfortable visits.", "review_count": 133, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-13T00:57:29.570855924Z", "text": "Absolutely not a place you want to be ever seen!! It takes now them 3 months to schedule you to see your doctor.  This has been going on for a while now, and I am done with this place.   I have been going there for @ 2years and instead of treating their patients the right way, it''s the opposite!  The longer you stay there, the worst it gets!!   You can get an appointment for months.\nPlease do yourself a favor, find a doctor elsewhere that will appreciate to have you as a patient.", "author": "Catherine Cosse", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116937957055182738125/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-03T01:55:55.519084467Z", "text": "This is for the dental appointment. Dental assistants have zero patience with kids. My daughter had the x-ray done, and afterward, we already told the staffs my daughter only wanted a checkup and no tooth cleaning due to having loose tooth. The assistant still set up and tested the tools which had sounds that really made us uncomfortable. My daughter started to get nervous and did not want to lay down and started crying. I tried to encourage her to lay down and open her mouth, and I communicated with my daughter in English and Cantonese ourselves. We did not need any translators. Then out of nowhere the assistant brought in a Cantonese speaking staff, who just said things like, “Oh if you don’t get a clean up, you may have painful cavities”, “you should not act this way in your age”, blablabla, typical way to threaten instead of soothing. It was no help at all. They make you feel like you are wasting their time, and they do not allow kids to have some down time.\n\nDo not leave kids alone with them. You never know what they will say to your kids and traumatize them. We will not come again.", "author": "Polly Chiu", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116952268779697599484/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-03-27T04:10:13.321902883Z", "text": "NEMS is, quite honestly, one of the BEST providers around -- it provides in-person translators for patients, excellent services, and even provides a transportation service (NEMS PACE) for the elderly or those who are otherwise unable to drive. For those who plan to stay in network, only need primary care, or need their translation services, NEMS is superb. From the perspective of a medical professional, NEMS is cooperative and efficient; they answer the phone, generally get back to insurance requests in a timely manner, and are overall polite. I''ve personally had EXCELLENT experiences with Crystal from NEMS PACE, she is always kind and very thorough (please give her a raise!).\n\nHowever, for out-of-direct-network services, they are one of the WORST insurance companies to work with. Because NEMS tends to withhold patient payments, other practices are hesitant to accept NEMS, so your base provider network is small outside of the NEMS network; this makes it a nightmare for non-NEMS providers to refer patients out to other services they may need. For patients who require specialty care (ie. surgical oncology, orthopedics, psychiatry, etc) this is DETRIMENTAL to your health and care -- insurance companies like Optum or SCCIPA will be a much better fit due to the larger out-of-insurance provider network. Please beware if you are a patient requiring special services!", "author": "RaspberryJuice27", "rating": 4, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105571530489700579055/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-20T16:16:32.634248469Z", "text": "Clinic was very clean, very responsive, neatly maintained , easy to make appointment , easy for parking , Dr. Hou Leong, MD  was excellent and very responsive , paid attention to details and caring. Appointment was fast and clear no waiting time at all.", "author": "Mrudula", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101644992843962803738/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-09-09T16:26:12.904681270Z", "text": "All medical staff and doctors are here to help the patient. They are polite, helpful, kind and always ready to resolve your medical questions.\n\nAs a patient, I feel the patient experience is extraordinary, and I would come back again for any other medical assistance", "author": "Xiaofei Z.", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104000548498629367477/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "North East Medical Services (NEMS) - 1870 Lundy Clinic has a 3.8 star Google rating from 133 Google reviews. Patients commonly mention compassionate care, friendly staff, clear explanations, comfortable visits.", "about_highlight": "North East Medical Services (NEMS) is a non-profit community health center that offers comprehensive health care services to a variety of patients, a majority of whom are uninsured or low income. The 1870 Lundy Clinic in San Jose provides a wide range of services including Internal Medicine, Family Practice, Pediatrics, Acupuncture, Chiropractic, Dental, Optometry, Laboratory, Radiology, Pharmacy, Endocrinology, Behavioral Health, Health Education, and Member Services. With over 250 health care providers across 32 sites, NEMS is one of the largest community health centers in the United States targeting the medically underserved population.\n\nThe clinic offers care in many languages and dialects, including English, Cantonese, Mandarin, Toishan, Vietnamese, Tagalog, Burmese, Korean, Spanish, and Hindi. The unique multilingual and culturally sensitive direct service staff allows patients to adequately express themselves in a familiar environment to increase the relevancy and excellence of care they receive. Health education programs and health promotion, which bridge the gap between Western and Asian medical practices, are available at the clinic and through social media.\n\nNEMS is a licensed community clinic organization, Health Center Program grantee under 42 U.S.C. § 254b, and a deemed Public Health Service employee under 42 U.S.C. §§ 233(g)-(n). Their mission is to provide affordable, comprehensive, compassionate and quality health care services in a linguistically competent and culturally sensitive manner to improve the health and well-being of our community.", "appointment_url": "https://mychart.nems.org/", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=11841267181378341641&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJ__CyuhzMj4ARCQuMhMOhVKQ", "quality_missing": ["insurance", "team_members"], "search_keywords": ["community health center", "community health", "fqhc", "sliding scale", "medicaid", "medicare", "low cost", "trung tâm y tế cộng đồng", "커뮤니티 헬스", "社区医疗中心", "hindi", "spanish", "cantonese", "chinese", "粤语", "广东话", "tiếng quảng đông", "burmese", "mandarin", "中文", "普通话", "国语", "tiếng trung", "tiếng phổ thông", "english", "toishan", "tagalog", "korean", "한국어", "한인", "한국말", "vietnamese", "tiếng việt", "người việt", "bác sĩ việt", "internal medicine", "family practice", "pediatrics", "dental", "optometry", "acupuncture", "chiropractic", "laboratory", "radiology", "pharmacy", "endocrinology", "behavioral health", "health education", "member services", "primary care", "preventive"], "cultural_context": "NEMS targets the medically underserved population, many of whom are uninsured or low income. The clinic offers care in many languages and dialects including English, Cantonese, Mandarin, Toishan, Vietnamese, Tagalog, Burmese, Korean, Spanish, and Hindi. Health education programs bridge the gap between Western and Asian medical practices.", "services_offered": [{"name": "Internal Medicine", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Comprehensive primary medical care for adults.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Adults"}, {"name": "Family Practice", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Primary care for patients of all ages.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "All ages"}, {"name": "Pediatrics", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Medical care for children.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Children"}, {"name": "Dental", "category": "Dental", "description": "Comprehensive dental services.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Optometry", "category": "Preventive", "description": "Eye exams and vision care.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Acupuncture", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Traditional Chinese acupuncture treatments.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Chiropractic", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Chiropractic care for musculoskeletal issues.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Laboratory", "category": "Preventive", "description": "On-site lab testing services.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Radiology", "category": "Preventive", "description": "Imaging services including X-rays.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Pharmacy", "category": "Preventive", "description": "On-site pharmacy for prescription medications.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Endocrinology", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Specialized care for hormonal and metabolic disorders.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Behavioral Health", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Mental health counseling and support services.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Health Education", "category": "Preventive", "description": "Health education programs and promotion activities.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Member Services", "category": "Preventive", "description": "Assistance with enrollment and program registrations.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}], "short_description": "North East Medical Services (NEMS) - 1870 Lundy Clinic in San Jose offers comprehensive primary and specialty care with a culturally sensitive, multilingual staff serving the Asian and immigrant community.", "google_website_url": "https://nems.org/about-us/#locations", "google_primary_type": "Medical Clinic", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "accepting_new_patients": true, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "1870 Lundy Ave, San Jose, CA 95131, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/102865309220334461850", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUBmJUdMhpbqZRtKX0BsIgURjcRwRo68TAi1XmZyiMPSJQEakY=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Oliver Hu"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/105960229159626104784", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUCzojKVJRIJ2i3YYCNzusCti0yD5tUO5625IYZxuLipKxpZTOFSA=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Thomas Pham"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/101623503812132967221", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKPI0f-lkVSkQCd59HIlYC5nq6I9LOfR5mDPe-3o7jYjX076w=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Lyn Rogers"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/113902971614407132003", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWlb9nevmB0ss2LkkKOG5y6voMVvUdLNBR7W4OYavtepXhQhAM=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Ian Cheung"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/110530732671928110124", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXSKoG1IV42daJIM4yBxIyj38koxHedlgyb2yJXyQxVXahKZFaH5g=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Anna Ess"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-26T10:48:05.367733+00:00', 'north-east-medical-services-nems-1870-lundy-clinic', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) is based on the foundation of Yin and Yang, treating the human body as the unity of qi, spirit, and physical form. Diagnosis is accomplished by observation, investigation, auscultation, and palpation – the four diagnostic approaches. Treatment modalities include acupuncture, herbal medicine, massage therapy (Tui Na), cupping therapy, Qigong, and dietary modifications to help the body reach the balance of Yin and Yang.

The ultimate goal of TCM treatment is not only to restore bodily health but also to attain physical, emotional, and spiritual well-being, as well as to slow the progression of chronic diseases in order to achieve longevity.', '731 123rd AVE NE, Bellevue WA 98005', 'Bellevue', 'WA', '98005', '425-666-6662', ARRAY['English', 'Chinese']::text[], 'Acupuncture & TCM', FALSE, '{"email": "aomcwang@yahoo.com", "images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/acupuncture-oriental-medical-center-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/acupuncture-oriental-medical-center-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/acupuncture-oriental-medical-center-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/acupuncture-oriental-medical-center-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/acupuncture-oriental-medical-center-google-5.webp"], "rating": 4.3, "reviews": [{"date": "2025-10-20T09:29:45.277783482Z", "text": "Dr Wang is a very caring acupuncturist. Her knowledge and dedication to the patients are very impressive. She is the 7th generation of Chinese medicine doctor in her family medical practice tree. I would highly recommend her to any of the patients who have acupuncture and Chinese medicine care!", "author": "Mini Health Talk", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100355298697891953475/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-24T05:37:27.130246525Z", "text": "I tried acupuncture for the first time after dealing with a stubborn shoulder injury for months. So glad I came to this clinic first after being referred by a friend. Dr. Wang was very warm and intentional when asking about my health - not just my shoulder, but my overall well-being. Knowing that this was my first acupuncture experience, she took time to explain where each needle would be placed and made sure that I was comfortable with each location. With the first placements, she  stopped to make sure I was doing OK and continued to check with me throughout the process.\n\nAfter the needles were in (which I could hardly feel), Dr. Wang recommended that we try applying electric pulses in certain areas which I agreed to. I wasn''t sure what to expect, but she was very reassuring and slowly turned the machine up until we found the right point where I could feel the slight tingling sensation without any discomfort.\n\nThen came what became my favorite part - basking under a heat lamp like a turtle in the sun while I layed in a state of relaxation. During future visits, I would sometimes just settle in and take a little nap. When the treatment was finished, Dr. Wang would return (gently waking me if necessary), carefully remove the needles, and then give me plenty of time to slowly get up at my own pace.\n\nDr. Wang would recommend a series of repeat visits, each time checking for any changes to my health and adjust needle positions as necessary, but I never felt pressured to continue which I appreciated. Very grateful to have found this clinic to help with my recovery. Thank you for the great first-time experience!", "author": "Carson Fisco", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101130511805952154240/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-18T20:17:12.815473289Z", "text": "Dr. Wang is truly the best and I will continue to recommended her and her team to friends and families!\n\nI’ve suffered chronic shoulder pain that shoots down to my arm for more than a decade and tried physical therapy, various exercises, massage therapy, and saw many chiropractors. Nothing worked for me and I was told that I may need to consider surgery.\nAcupuncture was the last resort for me and my biggest regret is not doing it sooner. Not only did my pain go away, I now have full functionality of my right arm and shoulder.\n\nDr. Wang truly cares about her patients—she listens to my symptoms and asks thoughtful questions to help make sure that the treatment plan is customized to my symptoms and health goals. I’m over the moon that I’m no longer dealing with chronic pain and that I’m able to do a wide range of activities with my right arm. I don’t know how she did it but I’m so thankful for Dr. Wang!", "author": "Monica Lo", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100018311679458638430/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-28T19:46:31.079502478Z", "text": "Dr. Wang''s attentive and patient attitude and superb medical skills have helped me with my skin allergies and sleep quality. Thank you, Dr. Wang, for your professionalism and compassion!", "author": "Juliet Engan", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104485848512599022029/reviews"}, {"date": "2024-06-14T07:13:49.526761Z", "text": "I visited two years ago and now finally have the courage to leave a review. At the time I was too shocked to process and just wanted to erase the memory. I was physically violated by Dr Wang. He did not receive any consent to touch me, and multiple times lifted my shirt and caressed me. He was extremely creepy and I should have followed my gut and left immediately. I have visited acupuncturists for more than 10 years and know how it works. Please beware.", "author": "Gwendolyn H", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109211258483275742972/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.aomcwang.com/", "location": {"latitude": 47.6170878, "longitude": -122.17702829999998}, "services": ["Acupuncture", "Chinese Herbal Medicine", "Tui Na (Massage Therapy)", "Cupping Therapy", "Qigong", "Dietary Modifications"], "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Award-Winning Clinic", "detail": "Awarded ''Acupuncture clinic best of Bellevue 2021''.", "category": "reviews"}, {"title": "Traditional Chinese Medicine", "detail": "Combines acupuncture, Chinese herbs, Tui Na, cupping, Qigong, and dietary therapy.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Holistic Approach", "detail": "Treats the whole person to achieve physical, emotional, and spiritual well-being.", "category": "care"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://www.aomcwang.com/", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": null, "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": null, "online_booking_available": null, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": false, "scout_query": "Chinese medical clinic in Seattle", "search_text": "acupuncture & tcm | acupuncture | chinese medicine | tcm | herbal medicine | cupping | pain relief | châm cứu | đông y | y học cổ truyền | 한의원 | 침술 | 한약 | 中医 | 针灸 | 中药 | english | chinese | mandarin | cantonese | 中文 | 普通话 | 国语 | 粤语 | 广东话 | 华人 | chinese herbal medicine | tui na (massage therapy) | cupping therapy | qigong | dietary modifications", "google_types": ["medical_clinic", "doctor", "health", "point_of_interest", "establishment"], "open_weekend": false, "rating_count": 23, "language_note": "The clinic specializes in Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM), based on the foundation of Yin and Yang, treating the human body as the unity of qi, spirit, and physical form. The practice uses Chinese herbs, acupuncture, and Tui Na, reflecting a culturally rooted Eastern medical approach.", "open_saturday": false, "quality_score": 90, "working_hours": {"friday": "10:00 AM – 5:00 PM", "monday": "10:00 AM – 5:00 PM", "sunday": "Closed", "tuesday": "10:00 AM – 5:00 PM", "saturday": "Closed", "thursday": "10:00 AM – 5:00 PM", "wednesday": "10:00 AM – 5:00 PM"}, "gallery_images": ["https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8751a9_ca2133214332454fb6a4157ac261b525~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_70,h_69,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/AOMC-Logo(PS).png", "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/8751a9_33eef26a65c142edb860559b4e7efcf2~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_223,h_256,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/IMG_2190.jpg", "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/11062b_95d34f15761e4114a57b17823228948ef000.jpg/v1/fill/w_1080,h_1080,al_c,q_85,usm_0.33_1.00_0.00,enc_avif,quality_auto/11062b_95d34f15761e4114a57b17823228948ef000.jpg", "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/5bfb6f_5f135e860f384bfbada661317d383592.jpeg/v1/fill/w_1280,h_1280,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/5bfb6f_5f135e860f384bfbada661317d383592.jpeg"], "review_profile": {"rating": 4.3, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Clinical Expertise", "mentions": 4, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Multiple reviewers highlight Dr. Wang''s impressive knowledge and effective treatment outcomes."}, {"theme": "Patient Care", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients consistently mention Dr. Wang''s attentive, compassionate approach and thorough consultations."}, {"theme": "Treatment Outcomes", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Several patients report significant improvement in chronic conditions after treatment."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Reviewers appreciate clear explanations and check-ins during procedures."}, {"theme": "Professional Conduct", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "One review alleges serious boundary violations during treatment."}], "summary": "Most patients highly praise Dr. Wang for her caring approach, clinical expertise, and effective treatments, though one review raises serious concerns about professional conduct.", "review_count": 23, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2025-10-20T09:29:45.277783482Z", "text": "Dr Wang is a very caring acupuncturist. Her knowledge and dedication to the patients are very impressive. She is the 7th generation of Chinese medicine doctor in her family medical practice tree. I would highly recommend her to any of the patients who have acupuncture and Chinese medicine care!", "author": "Mini Health Talk", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100355298697891953475/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-24T05:37:27.130246525Z", "text": "I tried acupuncture for the first time after dealing with a stubborn shoulder injury for months. So glad I came to this clinic first after being referred by a friend. Dr. Wang was very warm and intentional when asking about my health - not just my shoulder, but my overall well-being. Knowing that this was my first acupuncture experience, she took time to explain where each needle would be placed and made sure that I was comfortable with each location. With the first placements, she  stopped to make sure I was doing OK and continued to check with me throughout the process.\n\nAfter the needles were in (which I could hardly feel), Dr. Wang recommended that we try applying electric pulses in certain areas which I agreed to. I wasn''t sure what to expect, but she was very reassuring and slowly turned the machine up until we found the right point where I could feel the slight tingling sensation without any discomfort.\n\nThen came what became my favorite part - basking under a heat lamp like a turtle in the sun while I layed in a state of relaxation. During future visits, I would sometimes just settle in and take a little nap. When the treatment was finished, Dr. Wang would return (gently waking me if necessary), carefully remove the needles, and then give me plenty of time to slowly get up at my own pace.\n\nDr. Wang would recommend a series of repeat visits, each time checking for any changes to my health and adjust needle positions as necessary, but I never felt pressured to continue which I appreciated. Very grateful to have found this clinic to help with my recovery. Thank you for the great first-time experience!", "author": "Carson Fisco", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101130511805952154240/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-18T20:17:12.815473289Z", "text": "Dr. Wang is truly the best and I will continue to recommended her and her team to friends and families!\n\nI’ve suffered chronic shoulder pain that shoots down to my arm for more than a decade and tried physical therapy, various exercises, massage therapy, and saw many chiropractors. Nothing worked for me and I was told that I may need to consider surgery.\nAcupuncture was the last resort for me and my biggest regret is not doing it sooner. Not only did my pain go away, I now have full functionality of my right arm and shoulder.\n\nDr. Wang truly cares about her patients—she listens to my symptoms and asks thoughtful questions to help make sure that the treatment plan is customized to my symptoms and health goals. I’m over the moon that I’m no longer dealing with chronic pain and that I’m able to do a wide range of activities with my right arm. I don’t know how she did it but I’m so thankful for Dr. Wang!", "author": "Monica Lo", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100018311679458638430/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-28T19:46:31.079502478Z", "text": "Dr. Wang''s attentive and patient attitude and superb medical skills have helped me with my skin allergies and sleep quality. Thank you, Dr. Wang, for your professionalism and compassion!", "author": "Juliet Engan", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104485848512599022029/reviews"}, {"date": "2024-06-14T07:13:49.526761Z", "text": "I visited two years ago and now finally have the courage to leave a review. At the time I was too shocked to process and just wanted to erase the memory. I was physically violated by Dr Wang. He did not receive any consent to touch me, and multiple times lifted my shirt and caressed me. He was extremely creepy and I should have followed my gut and left immediately. I have visited acupuncturists for more than 10 years and know how it works. Please beware.", "author": "Gwendolyn H", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109211258483275742972/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Most patients highly praise Dr. Wang for her caring approach, clinical expertise, and effective treatments, though one review raises serious concerns about professional conduct.", "about_highlight": "Acupuncture & Oriental Medical Center is a healing center that treats a broad array of ailments and disorders by promoting overall well-being in order to achieve optimal health. Traditional Chinese medicine is utilized, combining acupuncture treatments, Chinese herbs, and Tui Na, a form of physical manipulation of the body by hands to facilitate healing. The clinic was awarded ''Acupuncture clinic best of Bellevue 2021'' by the US award.\n\nTraditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) is based on the foundation of Yin and Yang, treating the human body as the unity of qi, spirit, and physical form. Diagnosis is accomplished by observation, investigation, auscultation, and palpation – the four diagnostic approaches. Treatment modalities include acupuncture, herbal medicine, massage therapy (Tui Na), cupping therapy, Qigong, and dietary modifications to help the body reach the balance of Yin and Yang.\n\nThe ultimate goal of TCM treatment is not only to restore bodily health but also to attain physical, emotional, and spiritual well-being, as well as to slow the progression of chronic diseases in order to achieve longevity.", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=2655057900570224560&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJiTj-FV9skFQRsCeV7Rep2CQ", "quality_missing": ["insurance", "team_members", "appointment_url"], "search_keywords": ["acupuncture & tcm", "acupuncture", "chinese medicine", "tcm", "herbal medicine", "cupping", "pain relief", "châm cứu", "đông y", "y học cổ truyền", "한의원", "침술", "한약", "中医", "针灸", "中药", "english", "chinese", "mandarin", "cantonese", "中文", "普通话", "国语", "粤语", "广东话", "华人", "chinese herbal medicine", "tui na (massage therapy)", "cupping therapy", "qigong", "dietary modifications"], "cultural_context": "The clinic specializes in Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM), based on the foundation of Yin and Yang, treating the human body as the unity of qi, spirit, and physical form. The practice uses Chinese herbs, acupuncture, and Tui Na, reflecting a culturally rooted Eastern medical approach.", "services_offered": [{"name": "Acupuncture", "category": "TCM", "description": "Acupuncture treatments as part of Traditional Chinese Medicine.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Chinese Herbal Medicine", "category": "TCM", "description": "Use of Chinese herbs to help restore balance.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Tui Na (Massage Therapy)", "category": "TCM", "description": "Physical manipulation of the body by hands to facilitate healing.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Cupping Therapy", "category": "TCM", "description": "Cupping as a treatment modality.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Qigong", "category": "TCM", "description": "Qigong exercises to support healing and balance.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Dietary Modifications", "category": "TCM", "description": "Dietary recommendations to help the body reach the balance of Yin and Yang.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}], "short_description": "A healing center in Bellevue, WA offering Traditional Chinese Medicine including acupuncture, herbs, and Tui Na to promote overall well-being.", "google_website_url": "https://www.aomcwang.com/", "google_primary_type": "Health", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "731 123rd Ave NE, Bellevue, WA 98005, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/117028803537808987528", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXVXifU0SE-YQYb8ewoRaF_I7kG2aP0AhgehGboeh_5NB0XcpxS7Q=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jeff King"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/117028803537808987528", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXVXifU0SE-YQYb8ewoRaF_I7kG2aP0AhgehGboeh_5NB0XcpxS7Q=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jeff King"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/117028803537808987528", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXVXifU0SE-YQYb8ewoRaF_I7kG2aP0AhgehGboeh_5NB0XcpxS7Q=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jeff King"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/117028803537808987528", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXVXifU0SE-YQYb8ewoRaF_I7kG2aP0AhgehGboeh_5NB0XcpxS7Q=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jeff King"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/117028803537808987528", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXVXifU0SE-YQYb8ewoRaF_I7kG2aP0AhgehGboeh_5NB0XcpxS7Q=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jeff King"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-25T19:46:14.892171+00:00', 'acupuncture-oriental-medical-center', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

The hospital has earned numerous recognitions for quality, including an ''A'' grade for patient safety from the Leapfrog Group (November 2024) and designations such as Baby-Friendly USA. U.S. News & World Report has recognized CHA HPMC as high-performing in areas including diabetes, heart attack, heart failure, orthopedics, and spine surgery. These awards reflect the hospital''s dedication to delivering safe, effective, and compassionate care.

To serve its multicultural patient base, CHA HPMC offers multilingual services in Korean, Spanish, Russian, Armenian, Filipino, Chinese (Simplified and Traditional), and English. An International Services department supports patients from around the world. With over 550 physicians and a full range of medical and surgical specialties, the hospital provides accessible, high-quality care close to home.', '1300 North Vermont Avenue, Los Angeles, CA 90027', 'Los Angeles', 'CA', '90027', '213.413.3000', ARRAY['English', 'Korean', 'Chinese (Traditional)', 'Armenian', 'Filipino', 'Russian', 'Chinese (Simplified)', 'Spanish']::text[], 'Hospital', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/cha-hollywood-presbyterian-medical-center-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/cha-hollywood-presbyterian-medical-center-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/cha-hollywood-presbyterian-medical-center-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/cha-hollywood-presbyterian-medical-center-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/cha-hollywood-presbyterian-medical-center-google-5.webp", "http://hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/en-us.png", "http://hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/ko-1.png", "http://hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/es.png", "http://hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/ru.png", "http://hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/hy-1.png", "http://hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/tl.png", "http://hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/zh-CN.png", "http://hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/zh-TW.png", "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/flags/800px-Flag_of_the_U.S..png", "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/plugins/sitepress-multilingual-cms/res/flags/ko.png", "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/02.-180912_HPMC-CI-Horizontal.png", "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/home-slider-ambassador.jpg"], "rating": 2.9, "reviews": [{"date": "2025-08-08T03:24:57.029149746Z", "text": "💫I would like to thank all the medical staff who were on duty the night of July 28, when I had to visit a medical center in the U.S. for the first time. I’m truly grateful that I ended up in their care. Everyone responded very quickly, helped me recover, and surrounded me with attention. The atmosphere was calm, and the staff were kind, attentive, and professional.\nI especially want to mention one doctor, whose name I unfortunately didn’t catch, who spoke to me in Russian and even explained things in my native language. That was both unexpected and very comforting. During the X-ray, the machine also gave instructions in Russian, which helped me feel more calm and confident.\nThank you for your sensitivity, speed, and genuine care. I truly felt supported…🫶", "author": "Yana Ruslan", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113501000340894889672/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-04T04:16:14.182742192Z", "text": "Today I had a bad experience with the security guard and the supervisor at Presbyterian Hospital. The security supervisor was very rude and disrespectful to patients'' relatives. I respect the Hospital''s policy of closing at 8pm. I got from work and was stuck in traffic. I came to the hospital after 8pm and requested that they reconsider me this time for 10 minutes to see my dad. They were so rude and didn''t allow me to see my dad. Sometimes they should reconsider their relatives  because they don''t know what is happening. All nurses and doctors were so nice and provided great services. They should not talk like that. I will fall a complaint to their supervisor", "author": "Sazia Afrin", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105031827952404616968/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-19T18:51:50.294377058Z", "text": "Had an overall good experience at Hollywood Presbyterian. Had to wait hours to get stitches, but the nurses and doctors and staff were all great. Dr. Gong was especially amazing! Funny, kind, and did an excellent job with my sutures (nurses at other offices commented on how well done they were!)", "author": "sid solomon", "rating": 4, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103437014175120956568/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-15T04:21:17.831596177Z", "text": "I had an exceptional experience with my surgery and stay at CHA Hollywood Hospital. From the moment I arrived, I felt genuinely cared for, supported, and at ease. The entire team was professional, attentive, and compassionate, which made a world of difference in my recovery.\nA huge thank you to my incredible nurses Pia, Jevon, Marilou, Jinny, and Michelle. They were absolutely amazing kind, patient, attentive, and always checking in to ensure I was comfortable and well taken care of. Their warmth, compassion, and attention to detail truly made my stay so much better and more reassuring.\nI am beyond grateful for the outstanding care I received and would highly recommend CHA Hollywood Hospital and this amazing team to anyone. Thank you all for taking such wonderful care of me. Truly, THANK YOU!!!", "author": "Michelle Fernandez", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103400790945026118991/reviews"}, {"date": "2024-09-21T14:48:40.352423Z", "text": "The ER here is good as far as I know. Been here twice and the staff is respectful. Particularly Milton, Kelsey, and Taiyesha. The first time I was here I was in and out. Second time was a three hour wait for a minor situation. Wait time was insane for something that took five minutes to take care of. The bathrooms could use some updating. But aside from that, staff is respectful.", "author": "Rebecca Rodriguez", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108029212478746064587/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/", "location": {"latitude": 34.096344699999996, "longitude": -118.29045869999999}, "services": ["Women’s Services (Maternity)", "Fetal Surgery", "Acute Inpatient Rehabilitation & Therapy Services", "Cancer Detection", "Cardiology and Cardiovascular Surgery", "Chalet: Sub Acute Long Term Care Unit", "Emergency Services", "Neuroscience Institute", "Imaging Services", "Orthopedic Services", "Pediatric Services", "Surgical Services (including da Vinci Xi)", "Southern California Eye Institute"], "insurance": {"notes": "Financial assistance available. Contact Patient Accounting at (323)913-4970 for billing questions or cost estimates. Hospital bills insurance directly.", "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": true}, "highlights": [{"title": "Leapfrog ‘A’ Grade for Patient Safety", "detail": "Awarded an ''A'' grade from the Leapfrog Group in November 2024, reflecting a strong commitment to patient safety.", "category": "quality"}, {"title": "Baby-Friendly Designation", "detail": "Recognized by Baby-Friendly USA for supporting breastfeeding and mother-baby bonding.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Multilingual Services", "detail": "Provides care and translation support in Korean, Spanish, Russian, Armenian, Filipino, Chinese (Simplified and Traditional), and English.", "category": "culture"}, {"title": "U.S. News High-Performing Awards", "detail": "Recognized as high-performing in diabetes, heart attack, heart failure, orthopedics, and spine surgery by U.S. News & World Report.", "category": "quality"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "http://hollywoodpresbyterian.com/", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/find-a-doctor/", "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": null, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": true, "scout_query": "Korean speaking hospital in the United States", "search_text": "hospital | english | korean | 한국어 | 한인 | 한국말 | chinese (traditional) | armenian | filipino | russian | chinese (simplified) | spanish | women’s services (maternity) | fetal surgery | acute inpatient rehabilitation & therapy services | cancer detection | cardiology and cardiovascular surgery | chalet: sub acute long term care unit | emergency services | neuroscience institute | imaging services | orthopedic services | pediatric services | surgical services (including da vinci xi) | southern california eye institute | women''s health | surgery | rehabilitation | cancer care | cardiac care | long term care | emergency care | neurology | diagnostic imaging | orthopedics | pediatrics | ophthalmology", "google_types": ["medical_center", "hospital", "health", "service", "point_of_interest", "establishment"], "open_weekend": true, "rating_count": 679, "language_note": "Hollywood Presbyterian Medical Center offers multilingual services in Korean, Spanish, Russian, Armenian, Filipino, Chinese (Simplified and Traditional), and English. The hospital also has an International Services department, catering to a diverse patient population in Los Angeles and welcoming patients from around the world.", "open_saturday": true, "quality_score": 92, "working_hours": {"friday": "Open 24 hours", "monday": "Open 24 hours", "sunday": "Open 24 hours", "tuesday": "Open 24 hours", "saturday": "Open 24 hours", "thursday": "Open 24 hours", "wednesday": "Open 24 hours"}, "gallery_images": ["https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/02.-180912_HPMC-CI-Horizontal.png"], "iframe_sources": ["https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id=GTM-5593CNW"], "review_profile": {"rating": 2.9, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 4, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Multiple reviewers highlight the kindness, attentiveness, and professionalism of the medical staff."}, {"theme": "Facility Environment", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Neutral", "summary_quote": "Some patients note long wait times and suggest the bathrooms could use updating."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients appreciate staff who communicate effectively, including in their native languages."}, {"theme": "Security Staff Behavior", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "One reviewer reported a negative experience with rude and disrespectful security personnel."}, {"theme": "Treatment Outcomes", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients express satisfaction with the quality of medical care and treatment received."}], "summary": "Patients generally appreciate the professionalism and kindness of the medical staff, though experiences vary with some reporting long wait times and issues with security personnel.", "review_count": 679, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2025-08-08T03:24:57.029149746Z", "text": "💫I would like to thank all the medical staff who were on duty the night of July 28, when I had to visit a medical center in the U.S. for the first time. I’m truly grateful that I ended up in their care. Everyone responded very quickly, helped me recover, and surrounded me with attention. The atmosphere was calm, and the staff were kind, attentive, and professional.\nI especially want to mention one doctor, whose name I unfortunately didn’t catch, who spoke to me in Russian and even explained things in my native language. That was both unexpected and very comforting. During the X-ray, the machine also gave instructions in Russian, which helped me feel more calm and confident.\nThank you for your sensitivity, speed, and genuine care. I truly felt supported…🫶", "author": "Yana Ruslan", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113501000340894889672/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-04T04:16:14.182742192Z", "text": "Today I had a bad experience with the security guard and the supervisor at Presbyterian Hospital. The security supervisor was very rude and disrespectful to patients'' relatives. I respect the Hospital''s policy of closing at 8pm. I got from work and was stuck in traffic. I came to the hospital after 8pm and requested that they reconsider me this time for 10 minutes to see my dad. They were so rude and didn''t allow me to see my dad. Sometimes they should reconsider their relatives  because they don''t know what is happening. All nurses and doctors were so nice and provided great services. They should not talk like that. I will fall a complaint to their supervisor", "author": "Sazia Afrin", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105031827952404616968/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-19T18:51:50.294377058Z", "text": "Had an overall good experience at Hollywood Presbyterian. Had to wait hours to get stitches, but the nurses and doctors and staff were all great. Dr. Gong was especially amazing! Funny, kind, and did an excellent job with my sutures (nurses at other offices commented on how well done they were!)", "author": "sid solomon", "rating": 4, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103437014175120956568/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-15T04:21:17.831596177Z", "text": "I had an exceptional experience with my surgery and stay at CHA Hollywood Hospital. From the moment I arrived, I felt genuinely cared for, supported, and at ease. The entire team was professional, attentive, and compassionate, which made a world of difference in my recovery.\nA huge thank you to my incredible nurses Pia, Jevon, Marilou, Jinny, and Michelle. They were absolutely amazing kind, patient, attentive, and always checking in to ensure I was comfortable and well taken care of. Their warmth, compassion, and attention to detail truly made my stay so much better and more reassuring.\nI am beyond grateful for the outstanding care I received and would highly recommend CHA Hollywood Hospital and this amazing team to anyone. Thank you all for taking such wonderful care of me. Truly, THANK YOU!!!", "author": "Michelle Fernandez", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103400790945026118991/reviews"}, {"date": "2024-09-21T14:48:40.352423Z", "text": "The ER here is good as far as I know. Been here twice and the staff is respectful. Particularly Milton, Kelsey, and Taiyesha. The first time I was here I was in and out. Second time was a three hour wait for a minor situation. Wait time was insane for something that took five minutes to take care of. The bathrooms could use some updating. But aside from that, staff is respectful.", "author": "Rebecca Rodriguez", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108029212478746064587/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients generally appreciate the professionalism and kindness of the medical staff, though experiences vary with some reporting long wait times and issues with security personnel.", "about_highlight": "CHA Hollywood Presbyterian Medical Center (CHA HPMC) is a full-service, acute care hospital in Los Angeles, California, and part of the CHA global network. Committed to providing a full spectrum of dynamic healthcare services, CHA HPMC serves the diverse Hollywood and greater Los Angeles communities with a focus on patient safety, clinical excellence, and culturally responsive care.\n\nThe hospital has earned numerous recognitions for quality, including an ''A'' grade for patient safety from the Leapfrog Group (November 2024) and designations such as Baby-Friendly USA. U.S. News & World Report has recognized CHA HPMC as high-performing in areas including diabetes, heart attack, heart failure, orthopedics, and spine surgery. These awards reflect the hospital''s dedication to delivering safe, effective, and compassionate care.\n\nTo serve its multicultural patient base, CHA HPMC offers multilingual services in Korean, Spanish, Russian, Armenian, Filipino, Chinese (Simplified and Traditional), and English. An International Services department supports patients from around the world. With over 550 physicians and a full range of medical and surgical specialties, the hospital provides accessible, high-quality care close to home.", "appointment_url": "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/find-a-doctor/", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=7999170806159857818&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJz5iL3FLHwoARmljVfnfDAm8", "important_links": [{"url": "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/how-to-reach-us/", "text": "Contact Us"}, {"url": "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/billing-and-financial-services/", "text": "Price Transparency"}, {"url": "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/our-services/", "text": "Our Services"}, {"url": "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/our-services/our-transparency-dashboard/", "text": "Our Transparency Dashboard"}, {"url": "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/our-services/maternity-services-at-cha-hollywood-presbyterian-medical-center/", "text": "Women’s Services"}, {"url": "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/our-services/maternity-services-at-cha-hollywood-presbyterian-medical-center/baby-friendly-designation/", "text": "Baby-Friendly"}, {"url": "https://www.hollywoodpresbyterian.com/our-services/maternity-services-at-cha-hollywood-presbyt