The practice is led by founder Andrew S. Cho, M.D., an ophthalmologist, and retina & uveitis specialist Hans H. Kim, M.D. Together, they provide expert guidance for a wide range of eye health needs, from routine check-ups to complex surgeries including laser cataract surgery, minimally invasive glaucoma surgery, and the newest macular degeneration treatments.

Serrano Eye Center accepts most major insurance plans including Anthem, Aetna, Humana, Cigna, and United Healthcare. The clinic welcomes new patients and offers convenient scheduling by phone or online, with same-day appointments often available for urgent concerns.', '4220 W 3rd St #206, Los Angeles, CA 90020', 'Los Angeles', 'CA', '90020', '213-380-8800', ARRAY['English', 'Korean']::text[], 'Ophthalmology', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/serrano-eye-center-medical-group-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/serrano-eye-center-medical-group-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/serrano-eye-center-medical-group-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/serrano-eye-center-medical-group-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/serrano-eye-center-medical-group-google-5.webp"], "rating": 4, "reviews": [{"date": "2025-10-16T18:21:07.719275195Z", "text": "Their appointment schedule is terrible... ignoring the patients'' value of time.  I had the first appointment time in the morning and found out many (much more than 10) people had the same appointment time. People need to wait for a extended time to receive the service.\n\nThe bath room is dirty and out of the toilet seat paper. And the paints on the wall are cracked.\n\nThe staff who did preliminary work on my eyes before the doctor had runny nose and sneezing.  I hope he stays home instead of potentially spreading cold  to patients.", "author": "Yong-Seup Park", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113834100534836350552/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-06-10T23:26:37.263409Z", "text": "Dr Hans Kim is an amazing doctor, very knowledgeable, skilled, kind, and I can tell that he is passionate about caring for patients with ophthalmology health needs. I had a retina tear almost a decade ago and at that time he sealed it up with laser surgery. I moved away from LA and I''m new ophthalmologist commended the surgery even after a decade.\n\nThe staff is also polite. But I do think they get a lot of heat from people and they do their best to accommodate. That said, I understand the comments on the wait times. I do think they can work on scheduling. I think that they have so many patients because he''s such a great doctor. I''m not saying that it''s okay to make patients wait long hours, but, I also know that in general, ophthalmologist visits can easily be couple hours long with tests, waiting for dilation, and such. I usually carve out 3 hours for my once-a-year ophthalmologist visits (I still do with my new opthalmologist).\n\nThat said, I do think they can work on improving their scheduling and maybe even the flow of the visit so that the wait time in the lobby is not as long.", "author": "jane moon", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107889750495339695586/reviews"}, {"date": "2023-08-19T23:01:45.490452Z", "text": "My dad was concerned about an issue he was having with his vision. He’s from\nMichigan and flew into LA on a Friday night. Saturday afternoon we called Serrano, and they took us same day! Within 30 min of entering the doctors office a nurse was treating my dad. He received a full work up and our doctor was FANTASTIC.\n\nI’m grateful for the entire team, their diligent work put my dad’s mind at ease, and consequently mine as well.\n\nI’d give this place 10 stars if I could.", "author": "Chris Hoyle", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118380256861473502202/reviews"}, {"date": "2024-11-15T17:00:02.597469Z", "text": "Please try to avoid dr. Kim as he has tendency of lecturing patients of why patients left their eyes in such bad condition. If I knew what was happening, I would not visit a doctor. Right? I don''t need to feel any more uncomfortable as I am already uncomfortable with bad eye condition.", "author": "sarah shin", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115603337390746702130/reviews"}, {"date": "2019-02-19T04:47:20.680072Z", "text": "I had a terrible experience with this place. I needed a Glaucoma examination due to my periotic check up. I called to make an appointment and I was told that it will cost me $180 for the exam and initial checkup for the first visit. I went there last Saturday. They were so busy and all rooms were all occupied, waiting for the doctor. I was told that I have to wait a while for my check up and it was close to closing time; I told them I will make an another appointment to come back but they made me to wait. I waited a while and the doctor came to my room, asked me a few questions regarding any health issue and wanted me to make an appointment for a Glaucoma exam and he left... That was about a 4 minute consultation. I had to pay $150 for the visit and office admin told me that I have to pay another $220 for the exam. How does this make any sense?? Also, when I make an appointment they said they will claim the bill to my insurance to see if it will be covered but the office admin wanted me to pay first because she thought it would not be covered. I asked them how much is the first visit, they said it will be $80 to $150. They forced me in the room to make a quick $150. I felt so bad when I left.\n\nI do not recommend this place for ANY of your eye needs", "author": "Karen Kim", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114487499174491824556/reviews"}], "website": "http://www.serranoeyecenter.com/", "location": {"lat