. I called this office for the 3rd time to give my info just for the clerk to state I owe $90 from a missed appointment 2017?!! If truly my balance which I doubt, why not send it in the mail, email?! Why ask me for all my info if not going to utilize!! Last time I saw Dr. D was 2021! Paid my dues, purchased products! I am not one to miss my appointments!! And why not mention this balance prior to setting appointment. I had to request early clock out just to make it to this appointment!! Waste of time!!!", "author": "Liz R.", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113377833397146185318/reviews"}, {"date": "2022-04-28T19:05:57.124746Z", "text": "I have been coming to this office for several years and the staff is very friendly and welcoming. Every Dr. I have seen have seen have been helpful and kind. Most recently I had an appointment with Dr.Hsu and she listened to all my concerns. My skin has seen a big improvement since seeing her and I will recommend this office to family and friends.", "author": "josue napoles", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111472946556180434978/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients have mixed experiences at Orange Dermatology and Laser Center, with some praising effective treatments and friendly staff, while others express frustration with billing issues and dismissive care.", "about_highlight": "Orange Dermatology and Laser Center has proudly been serving this community for over 40 years. Founded in 1985 by Dr. Steven Stanowicz with his sister Stahsha Diaz as office manager, the practice began in Villa Park, CA and later moved to its current location at 1506 E. Chapman Ave in Orange, CA, with a second location at 368 S. Glassell Street serving as a dedicated Mohs Surgery Center. Dr. Steven Stanowicz’s daughter, Dr. Sarah Stanowicz, joined the practice in 2010, sharing the same philosophy of treating both employees and patients as family.\n\nTh