## Tips for Navigating Healthcare without Language Barriers

**1. Check insurance and interpreter availability before booking.**
Before scheduling any screening, call the clinic and ask: “Do you accept my insurance?” and “Can you provide a medical interpreter in my language at no cost?” Under federal law, clinics receiving federal funds must offer free interpretation services. Don’t be shy — it’s your right.

**2. Prepare a bilingual care notebook.**
Write down your symptoms, questions, and medical history in both English and your native language. Bring this notebook to every appointment. This simple step can reduce misunderstandings and help your doctor give you the best care.

