 and most importantly, they knew their business! I definitely recommend them!", "author": "Julia Filippova", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103680655326548843931/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-04T20:44:48.497274184Z", "text": "My mother had a heart attack on June 1 and due to the urgency was Emory John''s Creek. Now let me preface with saying my dad had a heart attack a few years ago and was St. Joseph and then Northside. I had a triple bypass at Advent Hospital in Rome, Ga so we''ve experienced a several hospitals.  Emory John''s Creek is BY FAR the WORST experience any of us have had. The ICU nurses were AWFUL. Besides being non-attentive and RUDE they were not gentle, caring nor compassionate with my mom. She was then sent to the 6th floor which was better but not by much. The patient food and cafeteria was HORRIBLE like REALLY REALLY BAD. The nursing staff in general was not even close to the level of any of the other hospitals.  The Chaplin was awesome,  kind, compassionate and friendly.  The lad lady too was very friendly, kind and great at her job (Maggie) and Jennifer on the 6th floor was awesome. That was the only positive experience in a four day stay but seriously,  the ICU was just awful!!!!!!!", "author": "Shannon Robinson", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109171884810004692942/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-24T20:03:43.524505513Z", "text": "Cath Lab & surgical suites - Dr Gregory Robertson Chief/Head & entire team.\n\nAAA+++ Operation. Professionalism personified. Dignified. Empathetic. Attentive. Knowledge, Skill and Competence levels unmatched.\n\nMy opinion - #1 Cardiovascular Interventional team nationwide. There may be others of this standard but none better.", "author": "Mike Macias", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101456567342014462062/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-29T13:31:34.034402673Z", "text": "The nurses were able to detect babies heartbeat, dropping every time my wife had contractions. The nurse scheduled on Shift detected that immediately and called in the doctors for an emergency C-section. I am so thankful that everything went great. The baby is healthy. Wife is good and I am very pleased with my experience at Emory John’s Creek Hospital.", "author": "Haydan Gomez", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100838505952161267548/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Emory Johns Creek Hospital has a 3.1 star Google rating from 725 Google reviews. Patients commonly mention compassionate care, friendly staff, comfortable visits, strong results.", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=10318595309877553894&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJ8wevZy-Z9YgR5mpDmsMDM48", "quality_missing": ["website", "languages (non-default)", "insurance", "team_members", "appointment_url"], "search_keywords": ["hospital", "english", "brain care", "cancer care", "heart & vascular care", "neonatal intensive care", "mother/baby unit"], "google_website_url": "https://www.emoryhealthcare.org/locations/hospitals/emory-johns-creek-hospital?&utm_campaign=brand_all_ra_gmb-locations&utm_source=google&utm_medium=gmb&utm_content=gmb_locations?&utm_campaign=brand_all_non&utm_source=google&utm_medium=gmb&utm_content=gmb-locations", "google_primary_type": "Hospital", "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "6325 Hospital Pkwy, Johns Creek, GA 30097, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/103708203201579358160", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW19HxitEHu3JgaLK-fn0C2Ln0_7LkBDQ2R6po1js2DahmRYKQLFw=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "David Mullis"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/104520832327948153960", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjX5jrJKQWaFfA_Daa4Nkhi