d acne cleared up a lot. She is also very kind and helpful. Highly recommend!!!", "author": "Matthew P.", "rating": null, "source": null}]}, "about_highlight": "At Nuga Medi Spa, we combine cutting-edge technology with personalized care to help you look and feel your best. Whether you''re looking for anti-aging solutions, skin rejuvenation, or non-surgical treatments, our expert team is here to guide you on your beauty journey. We are committed to delivering results that enhance your beauty while maintaining a natural, refreshed look. Our state-of-the-art technology, highly trained and certified professionals, and customized treatment plans ensure a relaxing, spa-like environment for every client.", "appointment_url": "https://www.nugamedispa.com/contact", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=7559696256157720281&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJka4RmQ6j9YgR2Z4hJrFv6Wg", "important_links": [{"url": "https://www.nugamedispa.com/contact", "text": "CONTACT"}, {"url": "https://www.nugamedispa.com/service-deals", "text": "SPECIAL DEALS"}, {"url": "https://www.nugamedispa.com/contact", "text": "Request a Consultation"}, {"url": "http://www.facebook.com/wix", "text": ""}], "json_ld_schemas": [{"url": "https://www.nugamedispa.com", "name": "Nuga Skincare Clinic", "@type": "LocalBusiness", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "postalCode": "30096-4602", "addressRegion": "GA", "streetAddress": "2005 Boggs Road Northwest", "addressCountry": "US", "addressLocality": "Duluth"}, "@context": "https://schema.org/", "telephone": "770-687-2545"}, {"url": "https://www.nugamedispa.com", "name": "nugamedispa", "@type": "WebSite", "@context": "https://schema.org/"}], "quality_missing": ["languages (non-default)", "insurance", "team_members"], "search_keywords": ["aesthetic wellness", "english", "shurink lifting", "thermage flx", "potenza rf", "laser treatments", "injectables", "facials & lymphatic drainage", "skin rejuvenation", "skin tightening", "skin revitalization", "skin treatment", "cosmetic", "relaxation"], "cultural_context": "K-Beauty inspired skincare treatments", "services_offered": [{"name": "Shurink Lifting", "category": "Skin Rejuvenation", "description": "Regenerate collagen and remove wrinkles", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Individuals looking for anti-aging solutions"}, {"name": "Thermage FLX", "category": "Skin Tightening", "description": "Tighten skin, smooth wrinkles, and sculpt your body", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Individuals seeking non-surgical skin tightening"}, {"name": "Potenza RF", "category": "Skin Revitalization", "description": "Advanced skin revitalization with radiofrequency microneedling", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Individuals looking for advanced skin treatments"}, {"name": "Laser Treatments", "category": "Skin Treatment", "description": "Target pigmentation, acne scars, and more for clearer skin", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Individuals with skin pigmentation or acne scars"}, {"name": "Injectables", "category": "Cosmetic", "description": "Botox and fillers to smooth lines and restore volume", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Individuals seeking non-surgical cosmetic enhancements"}, {"name": "Facials & Lymphatic Drainage", "category": "Relaxation", "description": "Relax, rejuvenate, and detoxify with customized facials and massages", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Individuals looking for relaxation and skin detoxification"}], "google_website_url": "https://nugamedispa.com/", "google_primary_type": "Spa", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "2005 Boggs Rd #101, Duluth, GA 30096, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/113943115136033595411", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVTtWUdW1gqZI5q0c9I9SRlpSChRuzBVZ7Iwr2CfH0zvWY-k0GU5Q=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Katharine Miele"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/114970974256127751760", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW7OYDYMVgAEMw85OwPrWC8bhrCpxCRSloUKvqfaLjtYdzsVsKU=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Nuga Skin Clinic"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/114132333449183115231", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjX-hyBsqAdJOHCp41JQadSKcWfPIes8uq-Qd_uiNC6WPRkDmSZCew=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "hanna kim"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-16T09:19:41.970911+00:00', 'nuga-medi-spa', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.clinics ("id", "org_id", "name", "description", "address", "city", "state", "zip_code", "phone", "languages", "specialty", "is_telehealth_available", "metadata", "created_at", "slug", "claimed_by", "is_claimed") VALUES ('1f967c7d-e09e-45ba-acd6-cd5bd30bf0dc', NULL, 'Northeast Georgia Medical Center Braselton', 'Northeast Georgia Medical Center Braselton is a Northeast Georgia Health System hospital campus in Braselton, Georgia. This profile was seeded from Google Places because the official website blocked automated scraping during the demo.', '1400 River Pl, Braselton, GA 30517, USA', 'Braselton', 'GA', '30517', '(770) 848-8000', ARRAY['English']::text[], 'Hospital', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/northeast-georgia-medical-center-braselton-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/northeast-georgia-medical-center-braselton-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/northeast-georgia-medical-center-braselton-google-3.webp", "https://www.nghs.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/ngmc-braselton-2025-1.jpg", "https://www.nghs.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/nghs-logo-2023.webp", "https://www.nghs.com/wp-content/themes/nghs-v2/assets/images/nghs-leaf.svg?v=1.1", "https://www.nghs.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/ngmc-braselton-2025-1-1024x783.jpg"], "rating": 2.9, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-03-04T02:24:04.755530762Z", "text": "Two appointments in one day; neurosurgeon office employees mostly did a good job but there were no updates on a dr. note and the leave and disability paperwork even though I had asked multiple times.  We were sent to the E.R. department for another important issue and while we completely understand their priorities we spent several hours there. An employee did a EKG process on my sibling and then we went to sit and wait again.  The employee that tried to get some bloodwork poked my sibling twice and still couldn''t get anything.  We went back out to sit and then another employee did a checkup on my sibling and she came back to sit and wait again.  Finally, we followed an employee down the hall to some private rooms.  The employee that helped us was consistent in coming back and forth to assist us and finally did get the bloodwork within one try.  We waited hours for the doctor to come by with the prescription and to talk to us but still nothing.  I had inquired about the paperwork process once again for my sibling and the employee that came and updated my siblings personal information said he would have case management come down and followup with us but nothing happened.  Finally, the consistent employee got an authorized release form for our prescription needs and let us go.  Why didn''t we get the release form earlier instead of waiting for the doctor for so long?  Also, I had to go back to the office of suite 402 to get the proper dr. note because E.R. only gave us a note for a few days when my sibling was recommended 6 weeks away from work.  In summary, we understand how busy the hospitals can be but there was a lot of back and forth and lack of followup on their end throughout today.  Big thanks to the employees that were consistently assisting us throughout the day though.", "author": "Paris Yang", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115577640635431585296/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-26T16:36:30.842792261Z", "text": "The staff in Labor & Delivery, as well as the NICU are very professional and took great care of my family. I have no complaints there, whatsoever. They are awesome! However, the ER and especially the billing department are utterly incompetent. If you can go anywhere else for medical treatment, I would encourage it.\n\nAfter three conference calls with our insurance, we were finally able prove to the hospital that our child was indeed on our insurance, despite having already provided the needed documentation to substantiate this. We did not have such issues from our insurance company, only the billing department at the hospital.\n\nMy wife had extremely high blood pressure (190/115 at one point), with dizziness and nausea after a c-section and waited for hours to be cared for by the ER team. Things improved once we got out of the ER, and into a regular room.\n\nTo further complicate matters, the billing department billed us for an item our insurance company had no record of. Insurance told them to resubmit this claim, but this was ignored by the hospital, and they instead sent the bill to collections. Several months after all this, we learned that the billing department used the wrong code and is trying to get even more money out of us. If you use Northeast Georgia Medical Center, make sure you''ve got a few thousand more dollars in savings. They will get as much out of you as they can, insurance or not.", "author": "Rick Cole", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101780132815034183691/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-03-04T14:46:08.041315063Z", "text": "I want to give a shout out and praise to Dr. Mehta in ER! She did a fantastic job handling my 4 year old son with a positive RSV! She took her time and went above and beyond with his care! I wish we had more doctors like her! She is a roll model for all doctors to follow. She showed so much care for a child she only knew for a few hours and her heart is full of kindness. She deserves an award for her excellence care of patients. Thank you Dr. Mehta and William thanks you as well!", "author": "Nicole Johnson", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112832226570759728127/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-05T21:48:03.675251624Z", "text": "As a RN, I felt it was necessary to publicly give this facility the kudos it deserved for the care I recently received. I was send in the urgent care clinic in Dacula, the ER at the medical center in Braselton and was admitted there as a patient on 3West.  I had no issues regarding my care and communication from the staff throughout my entire stay.  My surgeon, Dr. Kwayisi and team were great.  The nurses and techs were great.  I wish I could recall all of them by name, but I do remember Nathan. He was good.  The  tech that needs to enhance her customer services skills was named Stephanie.  She wasn''t bad but there is room for improvement.  The ER staff, from the check-in counter, triage, and the PA I saw were all professional even though they were faced with a busy, challenging night. (The ER was full). I really hope that my review  allows others to be confident in the care they would potentially receive if they are admitted to this facility.", "author": "Eulanda Armstrong", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117264251679181770729/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-14T22:48:45.253300738Z", "text": "My daughter was hospitalized for several days in a Labor & Delivery room at Braselton. Unfortunately she lost her baby but EVERY person we had contact with during that time exhibited compassion and comforted my daughter and son in law when the baby did not survive.  The Bereavement team Jessi and Karen were AMAZING. I was thoroughly impressed.  I would give more than 5 stars if I could.", "author": "Joe Mobley", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115136237669461221581/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-03-04T02:24:04.755530762Z", "text": "Two appointments in one day; neurosurgeon office employees mostly did a good job but there were no updates on a dr. note and the leave and disability paperwork even though I had asked multiple times.  We were sent to the E.R. department for another important issue and while we completely understand their priorities we spent several hours there. An employee did a EKG process on my sibling and then we went to sit and wait again.  The employee that tried to get some bloodwork poked my sibling twice and still couldn''t get anything.  We went back out to sit and then another employee did a checkup on my sibling and she came back to sit and wait again.  Finally, we followed an employee down the hall to some private rooms.  The employee that helped us was consistent in coming back and forth to assist us and finally did get the bloodwork within one try.  We waited hours for the doctor to come by with the prescription and to talk to us but still nothing.  I had inquired about the paperwork process once again for my sibling and the employee that came and updated my siblings personal information said he would have case management come down and followup with us but nothing happened.  Finally, the consistent employee got an authorized release form for our prescription needs and let us go.  Why didn''t we get the release form earlier instead of waiting for the doctor for so long?  Also, I had to go back to the office of suite 402 to get the proper dr. note because E.R. only gave us a note for a few days when my sibling was recommended 6 weeks away from work.  In summary, we understand how busy the hospitals can be but there was a lot of back and forth and lack of followup on their end throughout today.  Big thanks to the employees that were consistently assisting us throughout the day though.", "author": "Paris Yang", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115577640635431585296/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-14T22:48:45.253300738Z", "text": "My daughter was hospitalized for several days in a Labor & Delivery room at Braselton. Unfortunately she lost her baby but EVERY person we had contact with during that time exhibited compassion and comforted my daughter and son in law when the baby did not survive.  The Bereavement team Jessi and Karen were AMAZING. I was thoroughly impressed.  I would give more than 5 stars if I could.", "author": "Joe Mobley", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115136237669461221581/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-07T00:16:31.184782443Z", "text": "I brought my daughter in last Saturday(1/31) night and was seen by Dr Ariel. I always have a good experience at this location, but this time, it was excellent. The level of care and concern my daughter received from Dr Ariel and the staff(Stephanie, Lauren, Justin) was out of this world. I was told that Dr Ariel was new, but I couldn''t tell. She was a natural and took great care of my baby. Thanks Doc for all you do. Continue to make a difference. You Rock!", "author": "Mz Dee", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103237340567343277493/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-05T16:38:48.487405344Z", "text": "I want to leave an important review about this hospital because it’s not about what they did wrong but it’s about the lengths they went to to correct what they did wrong and make it right. I am more than a month out of my stay in the ER and the ICU.\nMy concerns are still being honored and addressed, and rightfully so.\n\nWithout going into details, I feel we need to give credit when a large institution hears the voice of a single person and uses it to better their organization. For that reason, I would not hesitate to recommend this organization. I had three very serious issues and they addressed each one to my satisfaction. I set a high bar with Customer-Service and they leaped over it.", "author": "Marlayna Glynn", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113491286971811882973/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-26T16:36:30.842792261Z", "text": "The staff in Labor & Delivery, as well as the NICU are very professional and took great care of my family. I have no complaints there, whatsoever. They are awesome! However, the ER and especially the billing department are utterly incompetent. If you can go anywhere else for medical treatment, I would encourage it.\n\nAfter three conference calls with our insurance, we were finally able prove to the hospital that our child was indeed on our insurance, despite having already provided the needed documentation to substantiate this. We did not have such issues from our insurance company, only the billing department at the hospital.\n\nMy wife had extremely high blood pressure (190/115 at one point), with dizziness and nausea after a c-section and waited for hours to be cared for by the ER team. Things improved once we got out of the ER, and into a regular room.\n\nTo further complicate matters, the billing department billed us for an item our insurance company had no record of. Insurance told them to resubmit this claim, but this was ignored by the hospital, and they instead sent the bill to collections. Several months after all this, we learned that the billing department used the wrong code and is trying to get even more money out of us. If you use Northeast Georgia Medical Center, make sure you''ve got a few thousand more dollars in savings. They will get as much out of you as they can, insurance or not.", "author": "Rick Cole", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101780132815034183691/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.nghs.com/locations/braselton", "location": {"latitude": 34.1204089, "longitude": -83.837731}, "services": ["Virtual Visits", "Urgent Care", "Symptom Checker", "MyChart Management", "Classes & Events", "Heart services", "Vascular services", "Orthopedics", "Neurosciences", "Cancer treatment", "Surgery", "Emergency services", "Obstetrical services", "NICU care", "Pediatric emergency services", "Cardiopulmonary rehabilitation", "Urgent care", "Imaging", "Endoscopy", "Outpatient lab", "Therapy services", "Emergency care", "Hospital services", "Labor & Delivery", "Medic