 manner; I can tell right off the bat after our first meeting that Dr. Bui genuinely cares about her patients. Overall it was a pleasant first office visit with Dr. Bui !!!! Thank you.", "author": "Charles Gomez", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111962623278168756531/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-03-03T18:48:55.095247621Z", "text": "I can honestly say Dr.Kim Bui is excellent. Out of all the doctors I have seen before, she is by far the best. She truly listens, takes her time to explain everything clearly, and makes you feel comfortable and cared for. I never feel rushed during my appointments, and she always addresses all of my concerns with patience and professionalism. I’m very grateful to have found her and highly recommend her to anyone looking for a knowledgeable and compassionate doctor. The service in Charles B. Wang Community Health Care is excellent 10/10.", "author": "Carolina Orellana", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118010553873920056616/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-03-09T16:23:19.058838783Z", "text": "I am very grateful to Dr. Melissa Groves for her kindness and professionalism. She is a very attentive, calm, and caring doctor who truly listens to her patients. During appointments, she explains everything clearly and makes you feel comfortable and reassured. I especially appreciate how careful and supportive she is during pregnancy. I feel that I am in very safe and professional hands. I highly recommend Dr. Melissa Groves to anyone looking for a wonderful OB/GYN.", "author": "Nazokat Dzhumaeva", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108499321969731950142/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-01T14:51:29.917096885Z", "text": "I absolutely love Dr. Bui and the entire team at Charles B. Wang Community Health Center. Everyone is consistently kind, knowledgeable, and patient. Dr. Bui is incredibly attentive and took the time to address all of my concerns without rushing. It’s a bit out of the way for me, but I’d much rather make the trip to Charles B. Wang and their recommended locations than deal with any other offices.", "author": "Jessica Sierra", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100266359127902374598/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients consistently praise Charles B. Wang Community Health Center for its exceptional care, compassionate staff, and attentive doctors who take time to address concerns thoroughly.", "about_highlight": "Charles B. Wang Community Health Center (CBWCHC) is a federally qualified health center providing high-quality, affordable health care to all, regardless of ability to pay or language spoken. Founded to serve the Asian American community in New York City, it offers comprehensive services including internal medicine, pediatrics, obstetrics & gynecology, dental care, primary eye care, mental health, social work, and health education. With locations in Manhattan and Queens, the center is open seven days a week, offers same-day appointments, and provides a sliding fee discount program for eligible patients.", "appointment_url": "https://www.cbwchc.org/schedule-online", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=11256819073565977541&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJdamJD4pZwokRxeu9ZE5BOJw", "quality_missing": ["insurance", "team_members"], "search_keywords": ["community health center", "community health", "fqhc", "sliding scale", "medicaid", "medicare", "low cost", "trung tâm y tế cộng đồng", "커뮤니티 헬스", "社区医疗中心", "chinese", "mandarin", "cantonese", "中文", "普通话", "国语", "粤语", "广东话", "华人", "english", "internal medicine", "pediatrics", "obstetrics & gynecology", "dental care", "primary eye care", "mental health", "social work", "health education", "primary care", "dental", "support", "preventive"], "cultural_context": "CBWCHC is deeply rooted in serving the Asian American and immigrant communities. The website is available in English and Chinese (中文), reflecting its commitment to language access. The center serves everyone regardless of language spoken, and its programs such as the Hepatitis B Program and Anti-Hate Safety Resources address specific community health needs.", "services_offered": [{"name": "Internal Medicine", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Comprehensive adult primary care services.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Pediatrics", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Care for children from infancy through adolescence.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Obstetrics & Gynecology", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Women''s health services including pregnancy care.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Dental Care", "category": "Dental", "description": "Oral health services for all ages.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Primary Eye Care", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Vision and eye health examinations.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Mental Health", "category": "Mental Health", "description": "Counseling and mental health support services.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Social Work", "category": "Support", "description": "Social work services to address social determinants of health.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Health Education", "category": "Preventive", "description": "Educational programs to promote wellness and disease prevention.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}], "short_description": "High quality and affordable health care for all, with same-day appointments, a sliding fee program, and care in multiple languages.", "google_website_url": "https://www.cbwchc.org/", "google_primary_type": "Medical Center", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "268 Canal St, New York, NY 10013, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/107821815236197059478", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUaV8geDSFkxnwjXYlL1IizH_zGtumUwdLxKhyyOyVH666PjNUHAw=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "sinan erel"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/111298699739698145354", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXpElYtcXmNQJUjugdnDIqXErFuLm57Cm2nTkmGaHMkT535d8DD=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Charles B. Wang Community Health Center"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/111298699739698145354", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXpElYtcXmNQJUjugdnDIqXErFuLm57Cm2nTkmGaHMkT535d8DD=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Charles B. Wang Community Health Center"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/111298699739698145354", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXpElYtcXmNQJUjugdnDIqXErFuLm57Cm2nTkmGaHMkT535d8DD=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Charles B. Wang Community Health Center"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/111298699739698145354", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXpElYtcXmNQJUjugdnDIqXErFuLm57Cm2nTkmGaHMkT535d8DD=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Charles B. Wang Community Health Center"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-25T20:06:56.304651+00:00', 'charles-b-wang-community-health-center', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.clinics ("id", "org_id", "name", "description", "address", "city", "state", "zip_code", "phone", "languages", "specialty", "is_telehealth_available", "metadata", "created_at", "slug", "claimed_by", "is_claimed") VALUES ('f8e5dcce-98ce-498a-9299-6f27eac4c23b', NULL, 'Los Angeles General Medical Center', 'Los Angeles General Medical Center is one of the largest academic, public safety net county facilities in the United States, providing exceptional care and supporting healthy communities in Los Angeles County since 1878. As a comprehensive medical center, it offers a full spectrum of services including primary care, specialty care, emergency services, urgent care, mental health and substance use services, diagnostic services, and pharmacy. The medical center is committed to accessible care and provides language services to meet the needs of its diverse patient population.', '2051 Marengo St, Los Angeles, CA 90033', 'Los Angeles', 'CA', '90033', '(323) 409-1000', ARRAY['English', 'Vietnamese']::text[], 'Hospital', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/los-angeles-general-medical-center-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/los-angeles-general-medical-center-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/los-angeles-general-medical-center-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/los-angeles-general-medical-center-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/los-angeles-general-medical-center-google-5.webp"], "rating": 3.6, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-02-25T17:15:11.443956165Z", "text": "I love this hospital.  It''s one of the best in the nation.  I was born here, my grandmother, mother, father and most of my family have received treatment here.  But, if you really look around you''ll see how the money that can be used to improve the place is being used on ideas that aren''t working.  The best example is that free \"valet\" when the valet program first when it started was 8am to five pm.  The valet would drive the car for you.  Give you a ticket and then once you returned you''d give them the other half of the ticket and then they''d bring your car.  Then slowly it started to close early around 445 pm.  Then now they close around 3pm?  On top of that they don''t even valet the car for you.  The original purpose of the valet program was to get people to their appointments on time.  Now the \"valets\" have the audacity to tell you where to park and how far to park inside the parking spot.  The taxpayer money is not being used in an appropriate manner.  That money could have gone to power washing the existing parking structure.  I bet you in a few more months, they will start to charge for what is existing free public parking.\n\nI just hope that the contract will be ending sooner rather than later.", "author": "Xochitl Sandoval", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102149555089765348811/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-01T22:03:42.889526854Z", "text": "All the doctors here don’t listen and it feels they want to rush you out. I’ve seen 5 different ones and they’re all saying different things about my injury. One of the doctors literally said “what do you want me to do.” And I’ll get a referral for more procedures or different doctors and it always take over 3 weeks to get an appointment a lot of them taking over a month. The only saving grace is the nurses are very kind and try their best to accommodate (not all of them of course but the few I’ve had)", "author": "Cindy Centeno", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106793468939089655850/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-14T15:51:07.654744143Z", "text": "I had a great experience at this hospital. NP Rice was sweet, kind, and very efficient. The nurses were very efficient as well although I can tell they had a lot on their plate, they did their job with a smile and patience. They made sure I was safe and well taken care of. I would definitely be coming back if I ever need to.", "author": "Lil Adrian", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113834975295152849447/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-03-03T06:09:16.418287966Z", "text": "This place is under funded, poorly managed & under staffed.\n\nLAGMC is a level 1 trauma center and really great at saving your life in an emergency situation, and then really poor at everything else. We experienced an absolute crazy town, avoid at all costs if you can get to Cedars instead.\n\nMy husband was brought to the trauma center after a bad cycling accident. The resuscitation team was quick & effective. After that, all downhill. They had him parked in the trauma center for his broken shoulder. A few hours later while waiting on the IV two finish, which  the nurse told us is cheap and constantly gets kinked, we got kicked into the hall for someone in cardiac arrest. Which fair, it''s a resuscitation ward.\n\nWe spend 12 hours there, 3pm to 3am. He should have been transferred to inpatient faster at like 10pm to free up the space and staff and more importantly, to get him more specialized neurology & orthopedic care. He walked out in a broken sling, prescribed ibuprofen and tylenol, his wounds still covered in dirt and debris. Now we can''t get the X-rays they took to get our follow up appointments. The parking lot is sketchy. They don''t take seemingly any private insurance which explains their funding problems. The nurses seem to disappear, not show up to work, straining the ones that do.\n\nAdmin & security staff are courteous. Everyone seems to want to do their job but are using outdated processes & technologies to better serve patients more efficiently. The records department relies on faxes and cds.", "author": "Jordan Gauger", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112181534821915163448/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-11T03:11:39.973861490Z", "text": "This was my first surgery ever, and I was extremely nervous going into it. The procedure was a tonsillectomy, and Dr. Allen Huang and his entire team made the experience unexpectedly smooth and reassuring.\n\nDespite their busy workload, everyone treated me with such care and sensitivity. They took the time to explain everything, checked in with me constantly, and helped ease my anxiety at every step. I truly felt seen and supported throughout the process.\n\nNow, nearly a year later, I can confidently say that the surgery has made a real difference in my quality of life. I’m deeply grateful to Dr. Huang and his team for their professionalism, warmth, and the positive outcome of the procedure.", "author": "Olga Zhuravleva", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111576121442272838565/reviews"}], "website": "https://dhs.lacounty.gov/lageneral/", "location": {"latitude": 34.057685, "longitude": -118.20801069999997}, "services": ["Primary Care", "Emergency Services", "Urgent Care", "Specialty Care", "Mental Health Services", "Substance Use Services", "Diagnostic Services", "Pharmacy", "Language Services"], "insurance": {"notes": "Financial assistance available through Patient Financial Services (PFS) to help with getting coverage and paying bills. Hospital Price Transparency information is available online.", "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Language Services", "detail": "The hospital provides language services to assist patients with limited English proficiency.", "category": "access"}, {"title": "Comprehensive Services", "detail": "Offers a full range of care including primary, specialty, emergency, urgent, mental health, substance use, diagnostic, and pharmacy services.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Safety Net Facility", "detail": "One of the largest academic, public safety net county facilities in the United States, serving all patients regardless of ability to pay.", "category": "access"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://dhs.lacounty.gov/lageneral/", "appointment": {"booking_note": "Appointments and admissions information available on the hospital''s website.", "appointment_url": null, "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": null, "online_booking_available": null, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": true, "scout_query": "Vietnamese speaking hospital in Los Angeles, CA", "search_text": "hospital | english | vietnamese | tiếng việt | người việt | bác sĩ việt | primary care | emergency services | urgent care | specialty care | mental health services | substance use services | diagnostic services | pharmacy | language services | emergency | specialty | mental health | substance use | diagnostic | patient services", "google_types": ["medical_center", "hospital", "doctor", "health", "point_of_interest", "service", "establishment"], "open_weekend": true, "rating_count": 1264, "open_saturday": true, "quality_score": 90, "working_hours": {"friday": "Open 24 hours", "monday": "Open 24 hours", "sunday": "Open 24 hours", "tuesday": "Open 24 hours", "saturday": "Open 24 hours", "thursday": "Open 24 hours", "wednesday": "Open 24 hours"}, "gallery_images": ["https://dhs.lacounty.gov/lageneral/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2020/10/Circle-1-scaled.jpg", "https://dhs.lacounty.gov/lageneral/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2020/11/Circle2_NEW.png", "https://dhs.lacounty.gov/lageneral/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2020/11/Circle3_NEW-scaled.jpg", "https://