 Comments.", "languages_spoken": []}, {"name": "Kristine A. O''Connor, MD", "role": "Pediatrics", "bio_snippet": "Patient Rating 4.5 out of 5, 54 Ratings, 12 Comments.", "languages_spoken": []}, {"name": "Nkechi Y. Quadri, NP", "role": "Family Medicine", "bio_snippet": "Patient Rating 4.9 out of 5, 312 Ratings, 95 Comments.", "languages_spoken": []}, {"name": "Keith L. Riggs, MD", "role": "Obstetrics and Gynecology", "bio_snippet": "Patient Rating 4.7 out of 5, 92 Ratings, 21 Comments.", "languages_spoken": []}, {"name": "Susan M. Stone, CNM", "role": "Certified Nurse Midwife", "bio_snippet": "Patient Rating 4.6 out of 5, 54 Ratings, 8 Comments.", "languages_spoken": []}, {"name": "Marta E. Taylor, FNP-C", "role": "Obstetrics and Gynecology", "bio_snippet": "Patient Rating 4.8 out of 5, 119 Ratings, 37 Comments.", "languages_spoken": []}, {"name": "Espelito C. Torregoza, NP", "role": "Psychiatry", "bio_snippet": "Patient Rating 4.8 out of 5, 124 Ratings, 30 Comments.", "languages_spoken": []}], "open_saturday": true, "quality_score": 95, "working_hours": {"friday": "8:00 AM – 5:00 PM", "monday": "8:00 AM – 5:00 PM", "sunday": "Closed", "tuesday": "8:00 AM – 7:00 PM", "saturday": "8:00 AM – 12:00 PM", "thursday": "8:00 AM – 7:00 PM", "wednesday": "8:00 AM – 5:00 PM"}, "gallery_images": ["https://www.utphysicians.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/greens-exam-room-scaled.jpg", "https://www.utphysicians.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Greens_0001_Layer-7.jpg", "https://www.utphysicians.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Greens_0003_Layer-5.jpg", "https://www.utphysicians.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Greens_0004_Layer-4.jpg", "https://www.utphysicians.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Greens_0006_Layer-2.jpg", "https://www.utphysicians.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Greens_0005_Layer-3.jpg", "https://www.utphysicians.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Greens_0002_Layer-6.jpg", "https://www.utphysicians.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Greens_0007_Layer-1.jpg", "https://www.utphysicians.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/Multi-specialty-greens.jpg"], "review_profile": {"rating": 4.3, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Several reviewers noted unprofessional behavior from specific staff members, including sarcasm and lack of concern."}, {"theme": "Clinical Expertise", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Many reviewers praised the doctors for their expertise and thoroughness in addressing health concerns."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Some patients reported difficulties in communication, particularly with follow-up care and appointment scheduling."}, {"theme": "Facility Environment", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Neutral", "summary_quote": "One reviewer mentioned challenges with navigating the facility layout, though they appreciated the availability of online interpreters."}, {"theme": "Patient Care", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Several reviewers highlighted the caring and attentive nature of the doctors and staff during their visits."}], "summary": "Patients generally appreciate the expertise of the doctors and the helpfulness of most staff, though some have experienced issues with unprofessional behavior and logistical challenges.", "review_count": 329, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-02-25T17:32:30.090491497Z", "text": "Ashley Thurston Rn is the most unprofessional and inconsiderate individual I have been in contact with while going to this location. She is unconcerned and sarcastic towards the needs and requests of patients. But other than that Doctors are great there and most nurses and management are helpful as well. You may have wait time but will get the information needed.", "author": "Parys Burks", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107350950580921244148/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-09T00:57:19.496245526Z", "text": "I have never been made to feel so small and stupid by a provider. I am literally doing what I was told to when I was first diagnosed with hypothyroidism in 2016. I am also following up on the adenoma as I was told it would still needed it to be monitored with the DHEA-S fluctuations.\n\nPrior to this in 2016 I was treated with levothyroxine at that time for thyroid levels much more stable than the latest bloodwork. I was advised back when I started treatment it would need to be continuously monitored and might be something I was on for the rest of my life.  In 2020 it was one of the many health issues that had fell off with the plague which indirectly lead me to having worse issues come 2023 when my gallbladder shut down and put me into pre diabetes and liver failure at the same time.\n\nDuring this meeting she addressed my levels as “sub clinical”, despite me telling her my weight is the highest it has ever been, my hair is coming out in clumps, I’m cold all the time and gain weight despite having no appetite. Couple that with an unrelenting fatigue that has just exacerbated my sleep need from Narcolepsy leaving me sleeping 12+ hours a day. I literally feel like I am wasting away and all she seemed to care to say it couldn’t possibly be a thyroid issue. That treating it wouldn’t help my weight and try to push GLP-1s.\n\nWhat surprised me was the disrespect I received from this provider. I’ve seen endocrinologist before I’ve been on medications for this and other conditions before for endocrinology issues but somehow I am in the wrong for scheduling to see her with the scheduling department.", "author": "Sakura Tsunami", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101048765377690310796/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-11-25T14:35:06.590425825Z", "text": "My daughter and I went together to have our yearly. Dr Ha Nguyen and all the nurses and front desk was amazing. Dr Nguyen was very down to earth and very concerned about me and my daughter’s health. She took her time with us. We were in and out. We will be returning next year. Such an amazing clinic.", "author": "Kimberly Williams", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103945116033089384935/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-03T01:01:03.146322917Z", "text": "Dr. Nguyen is amazing but I''m having to give a 2 star review because of my experience with trying to receive post op care.\nI''m absolutely disappointed in support staff at this clinic. I had a c-section on Dec. 16th and was supposed to have a 2 week follow up with my OB. I called and called and called trying to get an appointment, which for some reason you can''t make a c-section follow up with the receptionist it has to be done through a nurse? Every time they sent me to the nurses line I got the answering machine and never received a call back. Had to speak with a receptionist about this issue and she said she would leave a note with the nursing manager.\nGot a call from her and she explained all of the OBs had the ENTIRE week of off for new years holiday. Which is kind of absurd in my opinion. Then went on to say that the next week all of the OBs were booked. (So this would be past the 2 week point of when I was told by the HOSPITAL to be seen, have my bandage removed and inspected. I''m also still having clots which I mentioned to her. ) She claimed she was going to work on trying to find me an appointment at a different location of theirs and she would call back. Surprise surprise, never got a call back. As much as I really liked having Dr. Nguyen as my OB I will never come back to this place. Their staff doesn''t care about your wellbeing. I spoke with the Hospital I gave birth at and the RN there recommended I go to urgent care because its important that I be seen.\nIf you want to feel cared about. This is not the location to go to.", "author": "Nicole W", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115284125525954314402/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-07T01:02:13.782688630Z", "text": "The suite 150 is not accessible from the main entrance! You have to go out and around the building to find it. I wish I knew that ahead.. found out only thanks to this sign posted on one of the other suites.\n\nGreat, they also have online interpreters (including my niche Czech language) to translate for you, that was really helpful.", "author": "Michaela Honková", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105647279148251960378/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients generally appreciate the expertise of the doctors and the helpfulness of most staff, though some have experienced issues with unprofessional behavior and logistical challenges.", "about_highlight": "This outpatient clinic in Houston is fully equipped and staffed with experts experienced in different specialties to provide comprehensive care for each patient. Unique to this location, the Greens clinic offers medication management and care coordination as valued-added services supported by a dedicated team including physicians, advanced care providers, clinical case managers, social workers, pharmacists, nurses, and medical assistants. In 2021, the American Heart Association recognized this clinic for 70% or greater high cholesterol control among its adult patients. Parking is free and the clinic serves adult and pediatric patients across multiple specialties.", "appointment_url": "https://www.utphysicians.com/request-an-appointment/?preferredclinic_name=UT+Physicians+Multispecialty+-+Greens", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=12734543443590860534&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJv0mgr47JQIYR9k4DnMovurA", "quality_missing": ["insurance"], "search_keywords": ["ob/gyn", "obgyn", "obstetrics", "gynecology", "women''s health", "prenatal", "pregnancy