 is a caring and knowledgeable practitioner with a solid background in Traditional Chinese Medicine. Highly recommended!", "author": "Paul B.", "rating": null, "source": "Website"}, {"date": null, "text": "I came to see Dr. Fan after having two miscarriages... The pregnancy took about 4 months of acupuncture and Chinese herbs which I also took for the first 12 weeks to prevent miscarriage.", "author": "Alice D.", "rating": null, "source": "Website"}, {"date": null, "text": "In a few short treatments I experienced measured improvement. Now I go for relaxation and to treat other maladies. I highly recommend using him for any extreme pain issues (back, leg, migraines, etc.). Shu is tremendous.", "author": "Mary T", "rating": null, "source": "Website"}]}, "review_summary": "Featured patient reviews highlight Mr. Fan''s caring approach and effectiveness in stress reduction, fertility support, and pain management.", "about_highlight": "At Washington Acupuncture Center, we are dedicated to providing therapeutic benefit and result-oriented service in the field of Chinese Medicine, maintaining a patient-centered and enjoyable experience. We offer a full range of holistic therapies, including acupuncture, Chinese herbal medicine, Asian bodywork, and moxibustion, serving the Washington DC area, Northern Virginia, and Maryland. Our services address a wide array of health concerns, from pain management and fertility support to stress, anxiety, sleep disorders, and digestive issues, all guided by a caring and knowledgeable professional with a solid background in Traditional Chinese Medicine.", "appointment_url": "https://dc-acupuncture-chinesemedicine.com/appointment-form", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=5805967611769227305&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJBzLOh9G3t4kRKYjtFMjwklA", "quality_missing": ["insurance"], "search_keywords": ["acupuncture & tcm", "acupuncture", "chinese medicine", "tcm", "herbal medicine", "cupping", "pain relief", "châm cứu", "đông y", "y học cổ truyền", "한의원", "침술", "한약", "中医", "针灸", "中药", "english", "chinese", "mandarin", "cantonese", "中文", "普通话", "国语", "粤语", "广东话", "华人", "chinese herbal medicine", "asian bodywork", "moxibustion", "tai chi", "consultation", "allergies", "fertility support", "oncology support", "addiction", "facial rejuvenation", "digestive disorders", "stress anxiety", "sleep disorder", "pain management", "holistic therapy", "service", "shu fan", "acupuncturist, l.ac & national certification of oriental medicine"], "cultural_context": "The clinic specializes in Traditional Chinese Medicine, offering services such as acupuncture, Chinese herbal medicine, Asian bodywork, and moxibustion, which are deeply rooted in Eastern medical traditions. The practice serves the Washington DC area, including communities in Northern Virginia and Maryland, and emphasizes a holistic, culturally-responsive approach to health and healing.", "services_offered": [{"name": "Acupuncture", "category": "Holistic Therapy", "description": "Effective at relieving pain associated with neurological conditions, inflammation and restoring body normal function.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients seeking pain relief, stress reduction, or general wellness."}, {"name": "Chinese Herbal Medicine", "category": "Holistic Therapy", "description": "Individualized formulation to meet your specific condition and constitution.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Asian Bodywork", "category": "Holistic Therapy", "description": "Promotion, maintenance and restoration of healthy body/mind/spirit.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Moxibustion", "category": "Holistic Therapy", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Tai Chi", "category": "Holistic Therapy", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Consultation", "category": "Holistic Therapy", "description": null, "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Allergies", "category": "Service", "description": "Alternative approach to managing allergies, addressing side effects of conventional medications.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients seeking alternatives to allergy medications."}, {"name": "Fertility Support", "category": "Service", "description": "Chinese Medicine used alone or with Western medicine to support conception, including IVF.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Individuals or couples trying to conceive, including those using IVF."}, {"name": "Oncology Support", "category": "Service", "description": "Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine to complement cancer treatment, alleviating symptoms and balancing body, mind, and spirit.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Cancer patients undergoing treatment."}, {"name": "Addiction", "category": "Service", "description": "Acupuncture and Chinese medicine address symptoms and psychological imbalances associated with addictions.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Individuals struggling with addiction."}, {"name": "Facial Rejuvenation", "category": "Service", "description": "Non-surgical method to maintain beauty, radiance and vitality, and improve overall health.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Those interested in non-surgical facial rejuvenation."}, {"name": "Digestive Disorders", "category": "Service", "description": "Treats conditions like gastrointestinal infections, inflammatory diseases, IBS using acupuncture, moxibustion, and herbs.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients with digestive issues such as IBS or inflammatory bowel disease."}, {"name": "Stress Anxiety", "category": "Service", "description": "Chinese medicine addresses stress, anxiety, depression by restoring smooth energy flow throughout the body.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Individuals experiencing stress, anxiety, or depression."}, {"name": "Sleep Disorder", "category": "Service", "description": "Acupuncture and Chinese Medicine improve insomnia symptoms, fatigue, sleep quality, and depression.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Patients with insomnia or other sleep disorders."}, {"name": "Pain Management", "category": "Service", "description": "Acupuncture effectively relieves pain from neurological conditions, inflammation, and restores normal function.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Those suffering from migraines, headaches, back pain, neck pain, or other chronic pain."}], "short_description": "Washington Acupuncture Center offers the highest quality Acupuncture and Chinese Medicine in the DC area, led by Mr. Shu Fan, L.AC. We provide personalized holistic care to promote wellness and restore balance.", "google_website_url": "https://dc-acupuncture-chinesemedicine.com/", "google_primary_type": "Medical Clinic", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": ["Shu Fan"], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "1712 I St NW 4th Floor, Washington, DC 20006, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/103389182886856883439", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLCUc5QrcHFGSef3AFW2XIOmonTXypBav0JanI_-TmDa_H4SA=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Washington Acupuncture Center"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/103389182886856883439", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLCUc5QrcHFGSef3AFW2XIOmonTXypBav0JanI_-TmDa_H4SA=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Washington Acupuncture Center"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-26T11:52:16.020332+00:00', 'washington-acupuncture-center', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.clinics ("id", "org_id", "name", "description", "address", "city", "state", "zip_code", "phone", "languages", "specialty", "is_telehealth_available", "metadata", "created_at", "slug", "claimed_by", "is_claimed") VALUES ('afb3d7bb-b102-48fb-bdf8-bc7fe0b185cf', NULL, 'Piedmont Atlanta', 'Piedmont Atlanta is a 643-bed, private, not-for-profit hospital that has played a role in transforming health care across our region for the past 100 years. Nationally recognized for quality and patient satisfaction, we strive to make a positive difference in every life we touch and are committed to the communities we serve. Our state-of-the-art facilities, specialty services and compassionate care teams foster real change close to home.
INSERT INTO public.clinics ("id", "org_id", "name", "description", "address", "city", "state", "zip_code", "phone", "languages", "specialty", "is_telehealth_available", "metadata", "created_at", "slug", "claimed_by", "is_claimed") VALUES ('52ffea81-1abb-4f1f-ad0c-6a7ccfd6bb7c', NULL, 'Emory Saint Joseph''s Hospital', 'Emory Saint Joseph''s Hospital, Atlanta''s first hospital founded in 1880 by the Sisters of Mercy, has grown from a small house into a 32-acre campus in north Atlanta. Today, it is considered one of the top specialty-referral hospitals in the Southeast, offering nationally ranked Centers of Excellence in cancer, heart & vascular, orthopaedics, and more. The hospital is known for its compassionate, patient- and family-centered care and has earned recognition as the first community hospital in the world to receive seven straight Magnet® designations for nursing excellence. Physicians come from around the world to train here, and the hospital continues to provide exceptional care in the spirit of loving service.', '5665 Peachtree Dunwoody Rd', 'Atlanta', 'GA', '30342', '678-843-7001', ARRAY['English', 'Vietnamese']::text[], 'Hospital', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/emory-saint-josephs-hospital-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/emory-saint-josephs-hospital-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/emory-saint-josephs-hospital-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/emory-saint-josephs-hospital-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/emory-saint-josephs-hospital-google-5.webp"], "rating": 3.1, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-06-02T10:39:02.582162300Z", "text": "The management of this hospital is failing both its patients and its staff. The volume of patients is clearly more than they can handle, yet leadership has done nothing to improve workflow, staffing, or communication. As a result, the staff is overwhelmed, patients are left without answers, and the entire environment feels chaotic and unorganized.\n\nPatients wait for 10 hour''s with no updates, no guidance, and no sense that anyone is in control. This is not a free service — we are paying for care, and the level of service should match the cost. Instead, management allows long delays, confusion, and a complete lack of accountability.\n\nThis leadership team needs to do better. Healthcare is a responsibility, not a business transaction. When patients come in seeking help, they deserve timely information, proper coordination, and a system that works. Right now, this hospital’s management is not meeting even the basic standards of patient care. At the moment of this review I’m waiting 7 hours. So AI fall my case in the category of  Leve 3-5 - Urgent to Non urgent: can wait hours yep 7 hours and counting.", "author": "Zayra Sanchez", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116779336126320613762/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-29T21:33:47.816964402Z", "text": "stayed with my husband while he was admitted at St. Joseph''s Emory Hospital and had a great experience. The doctors, nurses, dietitians, physical therapists, and food service staff were all caring, professional, and supportive. Everyone from Emergency, ICU to room each one treated us with care,respect and made his stay more comfortable. I’m grateful for the excellent care and support we received. Thank you for making a difficult time much easier.", "author": "Jaya Butani", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107813879714796440578/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-11-19T03:10:06.547494211Z", "text": "This hospital earns 3 stars when it comes to caring for people with sickle cell disease, and that rating comes from a mix of positive moments and real areas that need improvement. On the good side, the staff members who truly understand sickle cell can be compassionate, patient, and willing to explain treatment options clearly. When you get the right doctor or nurse, you feel heard, and they make sure you’re hydrated, medicated on time, and monitored closely. Some techs and nurses go out of their way to check in, warm blankets are offered, and a few providers genuinely try to move with urgency. Those individual efforts do make a difference.\n\nBut the biggest issue—and the reason this hospital doesn’t rise above 3 stars—is consistency. For sickle cell patients, timing is everything. Long delays in triage or in receiving pain medication can turn a manageable pain crisis into a miserable, exhausting experience. Too often, you’re left waiting while in severe pain, even after explaining your medical history and crisis patterns. Some staff seem unfamiliar with sickle cell protocols or hesitate to follow them, which slows down treatment and leaves patients feeling judged instead of cared for. Being questioned about your pain or made to feel like you’re exaggerating is not the standard anyone should expect in a hospital.\n\nCommunication between departments also needs serious improvement. You might tell one team your pain level, medical plan, medications, or previous treatments, and still end up repeating the same information multiple times. Discharge planning can feel rushed, and follow-up instructions aren’t always clear. For a condition as complex as sickle cell, consistency and continuity matter, and those gaps show.\n\nThe facility itself is clean and generally organized, but crowded waiting rooms and understaffed shifts make everything slower. There are definitely some caring employees here, and the hospital isn’t terrible by any means, but the overall experience depends too much on who happens to be working that day. Sickle cell patients deserve reliable, timely, educated care every time they walk in—not just on a good day with the right team.\n\nOverall, it’s a 3-star hospital: not the worst, not the best, but one that has real potential if it invests in better staff training, faster pain-management protocols, and more consistent respect for the unique needs of people living with sickle cell disease.", "author": "Made in America", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107161740710043776884/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-06T16:18:26.466082649Z", "text": "Dr. Ivan Rubel provided exceptional care during a very challenging time for me and our family.\n\nHe performed my third, fourth, and fifth surgeries, and from the beginning, he was thorough and thoughtful—making sure every important health concern was carefully addressed before moving forward.\n\nAlthough I was in and out of the hospital for four months and we worked with many doctors during that time, Dr. Rubel truly stands out.\n\nHis professionalism, skill, and genuine care made a meaningful difference in our journey.\n\nHe was attentive, clear in his communication, and deeply committed to my well-being.\n\nHaving a doctor me and my wife could trust during such a difficult period brought us great peace of mind.\n\nHe is also supported by an outstanding team. Kevin and Jacquelyn his assistants were  consistently kind, professional, and supportive, reflecting the same high standard of care.\n\nWe are deeply grateful for Dr. Rubel’s dedication, expertise, and humanity.\n\nThank you Dr. Rubel and God Bless them all.\n\nWalter and Cecilia Angiolini.   :-  )", "author": "Walter Angiolini", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110016551994499968269/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-27T07:06:43.997694411Z", "text": "I truly love and respect all the people in the medical field but this place needs a change of management/operation. 1st off you get in and not really greeted politely and quickly asked what do you need or why you are here. Then they take you into triage where you are put in a IV to get blood drawn so they can run some basic tests. Then you are told to wait and you will be waiting 2-8 hours and that is literally not even exaggerating. I truly wish I was. There are people in there suffering. People crying from the pain they are in. Throwing up and peeing blood from what ever is causing it. Then once you get in the doctors and nurses are super nice and very knowledgeable but they take another 2-5 hours to fully talk and figure out what is wrong with you. That’s ig you ever get pass the waiting room. I am truly surprised no one has died in the waiting room it is a miracle of God. So if you are tired of waiting and want to leave now you have to wait for the front desk people to finally stop goofing off in the back which they do and take 30 minutes while the security just sit there looking at you not at least letting the front desk people know there is someone waiting and I needed them so they can take off the IV so I can leave and look for another hospital to go too. Please fix this place this is a Christian hospital it should be the best hospital in ATL", "author": "Nahum Gonzalez", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110705660818464504348/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.emoryhealthcare.org/locations/hospitals/emory-saint-josephs-hospital", "location": {"latitude": 33.9085976, "longitude": -84.34972839999999}, "services": ["Cancer (Oncology)", "Emergency Care", "Gamma Knife", "Heart & Vascular", "Orthopaedics", "Pulmonary Rehabilitation", "Radiology & Imaging", "Urology", "Visconti Center for Robotics"], "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Nationally Ranked Centers of Excellence", "detail": "Home to several nationally ranked Centers of Excellence, including Winship Cancer Institute (Georgia''s only NCI-designated cancer center) and a top heart hospital.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Seven Straight Magnet® Designations", "detail": "First community hospital in the world to earn seven straight Magnet® designations for nursing professionalism, teamwork and quality in patient care.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Top 25 for Hip & Knee Replacements", "detail": "Named a Top 25 hospital in the U.S. for hip and knee replacements by the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS).", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Minimally Invasive & Robotic Surgery", "detail": "Visconti Center for Robotics offers the latest in minimally invasive surgical approaches using the da Vinci surgical system for cardiac, thoracic, urological, gynecological and oncology procedures.", "category": "technology"}, {"title": "24/7 Emergency Care", "detail": "Emergency Department open 24/7, staffed with board-certified emergency medical physicians and nursing specialists, treating both major and minor conditions.", "category": "care"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://www.emoryhealthcare.org/locations/hospitals/emory-saint-josephs-hospital?&utm_campaign=brand_all_ra_gmb-locations&utm_source=google&utm_medium=gmb&utm_content=gmb_locations?&utm_campaign=brand_all_non&utm_source=google&utm_medium=gmb&utm_content=gmb-locations", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": null, "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": null, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": true, "scout_query": "Vietnamese speaking hospital in Atlanta, GA", "search_text": "hospital | english | vietnamese | tiếng việt | người việt | bác sĩ việt | cancer (oncology) | emergency care | gamma knife | heart & vascular | orthopaedics | pulmonary reh