lative treatment (omt) | stress reduction | jessica chan | doctor of osteopathic medicine (do)", "google_types": ["medical_clinic", "doctor", "health", "point_of_interest", "service", "establishment"], "open_weekend": false, "rating_count": 1, "team_members": [{"name": "Jessica Chan", "role": "Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO)", "bio_snippet": "Board-certified in family medicine. Earned her doctoral degree from the Chicago College of Osteopathic Medicine at Midwestern University and completed a family medicine residency at Ventura County Medical Center. Passionate about primary care, women''s health, obstetrics, OMT, and stress reduction.", "languages_spoken": []}], "open_saturday": false, "quality_score": 95, "working_hours": {"friday": "8:00 AM – 6:00 PM", "monday": "8:00 AM – 6:00 PM", "sunday": "Closed", "tuesday": "8:00 AM – 6:00 PM", "saturday": "Closed", "thursday": "8:00 AM – 6:00 PM", "wednesday": "8:00 AM – 6:00 PM"}, "gallery_images": ["https://provider-images.prod.1life.com/UserImage-650"], "review_profile": {"rating": 5, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Clinical Expertise", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Dr. Chan is described as thorough, caring, and attentive to patient concerns."}, {"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Urgent care doctors and nurses are uniformly excellent according to the review."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Dr. Chan listens carefully to patient concerns and maintains awareness of their progress."}, {"theme": "Availability", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Dr. Chan''s part-time schedule can make it difficult to see her for urgent issues."}, {"theme": "Treatment Outcomes", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "The reviewer reports only positive experiences with both Dr. Chan and One Medical."}], "summary": "Patients highly praise Dr. Jessica Chan for her kindness, thoroughness, and attentive care, though note her limited availability for urgent issues. The clinic''s urgent care staff also receives consistent positive feedback.", "review_count": 1, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2024-10-17T19:15:01.639649Z", "text": "Jessica Chan is a stellar doctor. She’s kind, thorough, and cares deeply about her patients. She will not rush through an exam and she really listens to a patient’s concerns. She does not work full time, so it’s not always easy to see her for an urgent medical problem. But the urgent care docs and nurses ay One Medical are uniformly excellent. And Dr. Chan is always aware of my situation, monitors my progress and handles follow up visits. I have had  only positive experiences at One Medical.", "author": "Wendy Miller", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107399958909875910602/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients highly praise Dr. Jessica Chan for her kindness, thoroughness, and attentive care, though note her limited availability for urgent issues. The clinic''s urgent care staff also receives consistent positive feedback.", "about_highlight": "Jessica Chan, DO is an osteopathic family medicine doctor at One Medical''s Noe Valley - 24th St office in San Francisco. She emphasizes a whole-person approach to care, focusing on body, mind, and spirit, and is passionate about primary care, women''s health, obstetrics, osteopathic manipulative treatment (OMT), and stress reduction. She earned her doctoral degree from Midwestern University and is board-certified in family medicine. Outside of work, she enjoys hiking, yoga, cooking, and spending time with family and friends.", "appointment_url": "https://app.onemedical.com/registration/signup?service_area_id=all&source=omdc-top_nav-signup", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=3036510416234516466&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJITqkwaZ_j4AR8o9urCLaIyo", "quality_missing": ["insurance"], "search_keywords": ["family medicine", "family practice", "primary care", "bác sĩ gia đình", "가정의학과", "家庭医学", "english", "korean", "한국어", "한인", "한국말", "women''s health", "obstetrics", "osteopathic manipulative treatment (omt)", "stress reduction", "jessica chan", "doctor of osteopathic medicine (do)"], "services_offered": [{"name": "Primary Care", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Comprehensive primary care for patients ages 14 and up.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Adults and teens ages 14+"}, {"name": "Women''s Health", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Dr. Chan is passionate about women''s health and provides related care.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Women"}, {"name": "Obstetrics", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Dr. Chan provides obstetrics care.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Pregnant patients"}, {"name": "Osteopathic Manipulative Treatment (OMT)", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "A hands-on treatment focusing on the musculoskeletal system. OMT appointments must be booked by the admin team.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients needing musculoskeletal treatment"}, {"name": "Stress Reduction", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Dr. Chan works with patients on stress reduction.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": "Patients seeking stress management"}], "short_description": "Jessica Chan, DO is an osteopathic family medicine doctor at One Medical''s Noe Valley - 24th St office in San Francisco, providing whole-person primary care for patients ages 14 and up.", "google_website_url": "https://www.onemedical.com/providers/jessica-chan/?utm_source=google&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=localseo", "google_primary_type": "Doctor", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": ["Jessica Chan"], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "3885 24th St, San Francisco, CA 94114, USA"}'::jsonb, '2026-06-26T11:24:37.60116+00:00', 'one-medical-jessica-chan-do', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.clinics ("id", "org_id", "name", "description", "address", "city", "state", "zip_code", "phone", "languages", "specialty", "is_telehealth_available", "metadata", "created_at", "slug", "claimed_by", "is_claimed") VALUES ('8bb36c46-9dac-4911-a2c5-2305682a210e', NULL, 'NYC Health + Hospitals/Elmhurst', 'NYC Health + Hospitals/Elmhurst is the second oldest municipal hospital in New York City. It has been named a ''Best Regional Hospital'' and nationally ranked by U.S. News & World Report in eight key areas, including Heart Failure, Heart Attack, Stroke, Hip Fracture, Kidney Failure, Orthopedics, Pneumonia, and COPD. The hospital operates 545 beds, handles over 717,000 clinic visits and 136,000 emergency room visits annually, and supports 2,359 births. It is also recognized as an LGBTQ+ Healthcare Equality Leader by the Human Rights Campaign and holds a Designated Adult Level 1 Trauma Center designation. Elmhurst offers a comprehensive range of services, from primary care and cardiology to women''s health and orthopedics, with a commitment to serving the diverse Queens community.', '79-01 Broadway', 'Elmhurst', 'NY', '11373', '1-718-334-4000', ARRAY['English']::text[], 'Hospital', TRUE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/nyc-health-hospitalselmhurst-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/nyc-health-hospitalselmhurst-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/nyc-health-hospitalselmhurst-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/nyc-health-hospitalselmhurst-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/nyc-health-hospitalselmhurst-google-5.webp", "https://captcha.perfdrive.com/captcha-public/images/ss_captcha.png"], "rating": 3.6, "reviews": [{"date": "2025-09-28T05:20:20.136948705Z", "text": "I want to sincerely thank Elmhurst Hospital—all the surgeons, doctors, nurses, and every team member of this incredible institution.\n\nOn May 19th, 2024, you saved my husband’s life. He went through four cranial surgeries, and thanks to your expertise and dedication, today he is recovering, feeling better, and preparing to return to everyday life.\n\nIt took me a year and a half to write this review, because I didn’t know how his story would unfold. Now, with hope and gratitude, I can finally say thank you.\n\nA special thanks to Dr. Zachary Hickman, Dr. Rappaport, Dr. Carr, and the entire surgical team.\nOur deepest gratitude to Valeriya Bokova, who became our guardian angel throughout these 1.5 years, supporting both me and my husband with care and compassion.\n\nWe are also grateful to the emergency team who brought us safely to Elmhurst, the reception staff, the surgery and ICU teams, the aftercare and rehab staff, and truly everyone who helped us on this difficult journey.\n\nFrom the bottom of our hearts—thank you very much.\nWe wish you all strong health and happiness.", "author": "Gri Shi", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116458966731253147563/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-11-11T12:11:57.176925836Z", "text": "🌸 I just want to take a moment to say a big thank you to everyone at Elmhurst Hospital\n\nI stayed in the hospital for two days, and before that, I was in the ER for another two days. During that time, every nurse and doctor I met was so kind, patient, and caring. They made a difficult time so much easier and really treated me with warmth and respect. 🙏\n\nElmhurst Hospital is definitely a good hospital — the staff truly care about their patients and go above and beyond to help.\n\nA special thank you to Nurse Karma, who helped me on my last day. I went back to look for her because I had some questions about my prescription, and she kindly helped me out with patience and understanding. 💕\n\nI’m truly grateful for all the staff at Elmhurst Hospital — thank you for your care, professionalism, and compassion. You’re all amazing!", "author": "Mei,Yee Chan", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114888289267499626507/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-21T07:34:03.307577097Z", "text": "Hello, my name is Barsha. I have been living near Elmhurst Hospital for the past nine years, and unfortunately, my experiences there have consistently been disappointing. Over the years, I have visited this facility multiple times seeking medical care for my parents, siblings, and occasionally myself. However, due to repeated negative encounters with the front desk, medical staff, excessive wait times, and an overall lack of empathy and urgency, I have often avoided coming here for my own care.\n\nMost recently, I arrived at the emergency department at 3:00 PM with right lower quadrant abdominal pain, concerned about a possible appendix-related issue—something that should not be ignored. The check-in process took an excessive amount of time, seemingly complicated by my TRICARE (military) insurance.\n\nAfter approximately an hour, I was initially seen in fast track, where my vitals were taken and a urine sample was collected. However, after briefly hearing my symptoms, I was told they could not proceed with my care and was sent back to the waiting room. I then waited an additional two hours before being called again.\n\nDuring the second evaluation, a nurse asked a few questions and directed me to another waiting area. A newly assigned nurse repeatedly asked me the same set of questions I had already answered multiple times, which reflected a lack of coordination and training.\n\nEventually, I was seen by a physician assistant who conducted a thorough evaluation. I appreciate his professionalism, as he asked appropriate questions and addressed my concerns effectively under the supervision of two physicians. Following the examination, I was informed that I would likely need blood work and a CT scan, and I was instructed to return to the waiting area.\n\nAfter being called back again for the physicians to verify my symptoms before ordering the CT scan, I experienced the most difficult part of my visit. From approximately 8:17 PM to 1:58 AM, I waited for the CT scan. During this time, I remained seated in a chair with an IV line, experiencing ongoing abdominal pain, without being offered a bed, water, or food. The CT scan results did not come back in hours. The conditions were extremely uncomfortable and distressing.\n\nIt is concerning that patients are expected to endure 12–18 hours in the emergency department without adequate comfort or timely care. The facility consistently appears overcrowded, with insufficient space, poor cleanliness, and visible trash. Additionally, many staff interactions came across as dismissive and lacking compassion.\n\nI hope this feedback highlights areas that require immediate attention, particularly regarding patient flow, staff training, adequate staffing,\ncommunication, and overall patient care experience.", "author": "JANNATUL BARSHA", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107102248769746633997/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-04T13:50:38.135607609Z", "text": "Good morning,\n\nI want to express my sincere gratitude for the care and kindness I received during a very difficult experience. When my knee suddenly popped and I was unable to walk, I had to hop to my desk and was scared and overwhelmed. My wonderful work family immediately stepped in, helping me get to the ER and making sure I was cared for.\n\nFrom the moment I arrived, I was treated with compassion, professionalism, and genuine concern. The ER staff registered me promptly and provided exceptional care, making me feel comfortable, supported, and at ease throughout my stay. Every member of the team showed kindness and understanding, and I am truly grateful for the love and care I received.\n\nI was also touched by the visits and support from my work family. Their concern reminded me how much we value and appreciate one another, and it meant more to me than words can express.\n\nPlease extend my heartfelt thanks to the Patient Experience Team and the entire ER staff for making a frightening situation much easier to navigate. Your compassion, dedication, and outstanding care did not go unnoticed and will always be remembered. Thank you again.", "author": "maris Love", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110955015990867060968/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-11-13T17:54:00.005848580Z", "text": "So grateful to all the doctors, nurses, radiologists, transporters and the amazing GI team that took care of my mom not once but twice! Forever grateful and put a candle in your honor.", "author": "H Landaverde", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115798710172837164312/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.nychealthandhospitals.org/elmhurst/", "location": {"latitude": 40.7450814, "longitude": -73.8857797}, "services": ["Cardiology", "Women''s Health", "Elmhurst Hip & Knee Center (Orthopedics)", "Primary Care", "Labor & Delivery", "Stroke Care"], "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Best Regional Hospital", "detail": "Nationally ranked by U.S. News & World Report in 8 key areas including Heart Failure, Heart Attack, Stroke, and Orthopedics.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "LGBTQ+ Healthcare Equality Leader", "detail": "Recognized by the Human Rights Campaign for LGBTQ+ inclusive care.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Level 1 Trauma Center", "detail": "Designated Adult Level 1 Trauma Center for comprehensive emergency care.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "High-Volume Care", "detail": "Over 717,000 clinic visits and 136,000 ER visits annually.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Maternity Excellence", "detail": "U.S. News & World Report 2025 Best Hospitals for Maternity.", "category": "care"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://www.nychealthandhospitals.org/elmhurst/", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": "https://www.nychealthandhospitals.org/make-an-appointment/", "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": true, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": true, "scout_query": "hospitals in new york that speak asian languages", "search_text": "hospital | english | cardiology | women''s health | elmhurst hip & knee center (orthopedics) | primary care | labor & delivery | stroke care | obstetrics & gynecology | orthopedics | neurology", "google_types": ["general_hospital", "hospital", "doctor", "consultant", "health", "point_of_interest", "service", "establishment"], "open_weekend": true, "rating_count": 3542, "open_saturday": true, "quality_score": 87, "working_hours": {"friday": "Open 24 hours", "monday": "Open 24 hours", "sunday": "Open 24 hours", "tuesday": "Open 24 hours", "saturday": "Open 24 hours", "thursday": "Open 24 hours", "wednesday": "Open 24 hours"}, "iframe_sources": ["https://newassets.hcaptcha.com/captcha/v1/caa502ef4d2063b68a3b48defc6ff368e0012d5d/static/hcaptcha.html#frame=checkbox&id=0mzhbr4hfjui&host=validate.perfdrive.com&sentry=true&reportapi=https%3A%2F%2Faccounts.hcaptcha.com&recaptchacompat=off&custom=false&hl=en&tplinks=on&andint=off&pstissuer=https%3A%2F%2Fpst-issuer.hcaptcha.com&sitekey=ae73173b-7003-44e0-bc87-654d0dab8b75&theme=light&origin=https%3A%2F%2Fvalidate.perfdrive.com&clientOptions=%7B%22sentry%22%3Atrue%2C%22reportapi%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Faccounts.hcaptcha.com%22%2C%22recaptchacompat%22%3A%22off%22%2C%22custom%22%3Afalse%2C%22hl%22%3A%22en-US%40posix%22%2C%22tplinks%22%3A%22on%22%2C%22andint%22%3A%22off%22%2C%22pat%22%3A%22on%22%2C%22pstissuer%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fpst-issuer.hcaptcha.com%22%2C%22endpoint%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fapi.hcaptcha.com%22%2C%22theme%22%3A%22light%22%2C%22size%22%3A%22normal%22%2C%22confirm-nav%22%3Afalse%7D", "https://newassets.hcaptcha.com/captcha/v1/caa502ef4d2063b68a3b48defc6ff368e0012d5d/static/hcaptcha.html#frame=challenge&id=0mzhbr4hfjui&host=validate.perfdrive.com&sentry=true&reportapi=https%3A%2F%2Faccounts.hcaptcha.com&recaptchacompat=off&custom=false&hl=en&tplinks=on&andint=off&pstissuer=https%3A%2F%2Fpst-issuer.hcaptcha.com&sitekey=ae73173b-7003-44e0-bc87-654d0dab8b75&theme=light&origin=https%3A%2F%2Fvalidate.perfdrive.com&clientOptions=%7B%22sentry%22%3Atrue%2C%22reportapi%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Faccounts.hcaptcha.com%22%2C%22recaptchacompat%22%3A%22off%22%2C%22custom%22%3Afalse%2C%22hl%22%3A%22en-US%40posix%22%2C%22tplinks%22%3A%22on%22%2C%22andint%22%3A%22off%22%2C%22pat%22%3A%22on%22%2C%22pstissuer%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fpst-issuer.hcaptcha.com%22%2C%22endpoint%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fapi.hcaptcha.com%22%2C%22theme%22%3A%22light%22%2C%22size%22%3A%22normal%22%2C%22confirm-nav%22%3Afalse%7D"], "review_profile": {"rating": 3.6, "source": "google", "summary": "Patients express deep gratitude for life-saving care and compassionate staff, though some report long wait times and administrative frustrations.", "review_count": 3542, "concern_themes": ["Long wait times", "Front desk issues", "Insurance complications", "Lack of urgency", "Inconsistent experiences"], "positive_themes": ["Life-saving care", "Compassionate staff", "Professional expertise", "Emergency responsiveness", "Team dedication"], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2025-09-28T05:20:20.136948705Z", "text": "I want to sincerely thank Elmhurst Hospital—all the surgeons, doctors, nurses, and every team member of this incredible institution.\n\nOn May 19th, 2024, you saved my husband’s life. He went through four cranial surgeries, and thanks to your expertise and dedication, today he is recovering, feeling better, and preparing to return to everyday life.\n\nIt took me a year and a half to write this review, because I didn’t know how his story would unfold. Now, with hope and gratitude, I can finally say thank you.\n\nA special thanks to Dr. Zachary Hickman, Dr. Rappaport, Dr. Carr, and the entire surgical team.\nOur deepest gratitude to Valeriya Bokova, who became our guardian angel throughout these 1.5 years, supporting both me and my husband with care and compassion.\n\nWe are also grateful to the emergency team who brought us safely to Elmhurst, the reception staff, the surgery and ICU teams, the aftercare and rehab staff, and truly everyone who helped us on this difficult journey.\n\nFrom the bottom of our hearts—thank you very much.\nWe wish you all strong health and happiness.", "author": "Gri Shi", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116458966731253147563/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-11-11T12:11:57.176925836Z", "text": "🌸 I just want to take a moment to say a big thank you to everyone at Elmhurst Hospital\n\nI stayed in the hospital for two days, and before that, I was in the ER for another two days. During that time, every nurse and doctor I met was so kind, patient, and caring. They made a difficult time so much easier and really treated me with warmth and respect. 🙏\n\nElmhurst Hospital is definitely a good hospital — the staff truly care about their patients and go above and beyond to help.\n\nA special thank you to Nurse Karma, who helped me on my last day. I went back to look for her because I had some questions about my prescription, and she kindly helped me out with patience and understanding. 💕\n\nI’m truly grateful for all the staff at Elmhurst Hospital — thank you for your care, professionalism, and compassion. You’re all amazing!", "author": "Mei,Yee Chan", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114888289267499626507/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-21T07:34:03.307577097Z", "text": "Hello, my name is Barsha. I have been living near Elmhurst Hospital for the past nine years, and unfortunately, my experiences there have consistently been disappointing. Over the years, I have visited this facility multiple times seeking medical care for my parents, siblings, and occasionally myself. However, due to repeated negative encounters with the front desk, medical staff, excessive wait times, and an overall lack of empathy and urgency, I have often avoided coming here for my own care.\n\nMost recently, I arrived at the emergency department at 3:00 PM with right lower quadrant abdominal pain, concerned about a possible appendix-related issue—something that should not be ignored. The check-in process took an excessive amount of time, seemingly complicated by my TRICARE (military) insurance.\n\nAfter approximately an hour, I was initially seen in fast track, where my vitals were taken and a urine sample was collected. However, after briefly hearing my symptoms, I was told they could not proceed with my care and was sent back to the waiting room. I then waited an additional two hours before being called again.\n\nDuring the second evaluation, a nurse asked a few questions and directed me to another waiting area. A newly assigned nurse repeatedly asked me the same set of questions I had already answered multiple times, which reflected a lack of coordination and training.\n\nEventually, I was seen by a physician assistant who conducted a thorough evaluation. I appreciate his professionalism, as he asked appropriate questions and addressed my concerns effectively under the supervision of two physicians. Following the examination, I was informed that I would likely need blood work and a CT scan, and I was instructed to return to the waiting area.\n\nAfter being called back again for the physicians to verify my symptoms before ordering the CT scan, I experienced the most difficult part of my visit. From approximately 8:17 PM to 1:58 AM, I waited for the CT scan. During this time, I remained seated in a chair with an IV line, experiencing ongoing abdominal pain, without being offered a bed, water, or food. The CT scan results did not come back in hours. The conditions were extremely uncomfortable and distressing.\n\nIt is concerning that patients are expected to endure 12–18 hours in the emergency department without adequate comfort or timely care. The facility consistently appears overcrowded, with insufficient space, poor cleanliness, and visible trash. Additionally, many staff interactions came across as dismissive and lacking compassion.\n\nI hope this feedback highlights areas that require immediate attention, particularly regarding patient flow, staff training, adequate staffing,\ncommunication, and overall patient care experience.", "author": "JANNATUL BARSHA", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107102248769746633997/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-04T13:50:38.135607609Z", "text": "Good morning,\n\nI want to express my sincere gratitude for the care and kindness I received during a very difficult experience. When my knee suddenly popped and I was unable to walk, I had to hop to my desk and was scared and overwhelmed. My wonderful work family immediately stepped in, helping me get to the ER and making sure I was cared for.\n\nFrom the moment I arrived, I was treated with compassion, professionalism, and genuine concern. The ER staff registered me promptly and provided exceptional care, making me feel comfortable, supported, and at ease throughout my stay. Every member of the team showed kindness and understanding, and I am truly grateful for the love and care I received.\n\nI was also touched by the visits and support from my work family. Their concern reminded me how much we value and appreciate one another, and it meant more to me than words can express.\n\nPlease extend my heartfelt thanks to the Patient Experience Team and the entire ER staff for making a frightening situation much easier to navigate. Your compassion, dedication, and outstanding care did not go unnoticed and will always be remembered. Thank you again.", "author": "maris Love", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110955015990867060968/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-11-13T17:54:00.005848580Z", "text": "So grateful to all the doctors, nurses, radiologists, transporters and the amazing GI team that took care of my mom not once but twice! Forever grateful and put a candle in your honor.", "author": "H Landaverde", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115798710172837164312/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients express deep gratitude for life-saving care and compassionate staff, though some report long wait times and administrative frustrations.", "about_highlight": "NYC Health + Hospitals/Elmhurst is the second oldest municipal hospital in New York City. It has been named a ''Best Regional Hospital'' and nationally ranked by U.S. News & World Report in eight key areas, including Heart Failure, Heart Attack, Stroke, Hip Fracture, Kidney Failure, Orthopedics, Pneumonia, and COPD. The hospital operates 545 beds, handles over 717,000 clinic visits and 136,000 emergency room visits annually, and supports 2,359 births. It is also recognized as an LGBTQ+ Healthcare Equality Leader by the Human Rights Campaign and holds a Designated Adult Level 1 Trauma Center designation. Elmhurst offers a comprehensive range of services, from primary care and cardiology to women''s health and orthopedics, with a commitment to serving the diverse Queens community.", "appointment_url": "https://www.nychealthandhospitals.org/make-an-appointment/", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=16818405044916477525&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJi2Z3IpVfwokRVV7i1kf6Zuk", "quality_missing": ["languages (non-default)", "insurance", "team_members"], "search_keywords": ["hospital", "english", "cardiology", "women''s health", "elmhurst hip & knee center (orthopedics)", "primary care", "labor & delivery", "stroke care", "obstetrics & gynecology", "orthopedics", "neurology"], "services_offered": [{"name": "Cardiology", "category": "Cardiology", "description": null, "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Women''s Health", "category": "Obstetrics & Gynecology", "description": null, "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Elmhurst Hip & Knee Center (Orthopedics)", "category": "Orthopedics", "description": null, "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Primary Care", "category": "Primary Care", "description": null, "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Labor & Delivery", "category": "Obstetrics & Gynecology", "description": null, "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Stroke Care", "category": "Neurology", "description": null, "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}], "google_website_url": "https://www.nychealthandhospitals.org/elmhurst/", "google_primary_type": "General Hospital", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "79-01 Broadway, Elmhurst, NY 11373, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/110016633381143193664", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXB5kGnYdlX8bl8VMTkxX734oKgTlW_pW0TkzkW6hGJCYDGl3WGZQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Faisal Mobarak"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/116857930449756512623", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocImRg4VuuqilqnRIg0iiC7yVKdD2InYYq4dvUpREo8jjYAvOA=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Mario Delucca"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/106909210065237971665", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWAMhDNLPBt8ldPPj7f96M2nxrro57wBh6_Wecf7rOQsdx_GWrC7w=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jaison George"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/102394465086443190135", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVihfK4_u4Qf-PGRke4MabAHO3iGjObBv4aZICYJ8peq_LLheww=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Chelsea Lee"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/112998676252315999163", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKiaosnE2Pm_4mgJ9nyjXmjPyYvM-9iuS5pqbuAFnnlWZEqYQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Sofia Huerta"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-25T09:59:38.37786+00:00', 'nyc-health-hospitalselmhurst', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
