tracted and infantilizing tone."}], "summary": "Most patients report highly positive experiences with attentive, compassionate care and efficient service, though one review highlights a negative experience with a specific provider.", "review_count": 108, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-02-04T21:14:06.134659573Z", "text": "Dr. Roth has made a real difference in my life. She is kind, attentive, and truly care about my health . I never felt dismissed or rushed, and every concern was taken seriously. It’s rare to find a doctor who combines expertise with genuine compassion. I’m very grateful to be under her care.", "author": "Celicia", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110165665568078562130/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-23T02:36:20.229644456Z", "text": "I recently was accidentally knocked over by another visitor to a museum.  Days after the incident, I began to experience growing pain and tenderness in my knee.  Thorough, professional and friendly, Dr. Padilla asked a series of questions during our video call that enabled her to assess the situation and lay out several options for my consideration concerning treatment.  I am so pleased with her performance and with the outcome of my treatment.", "author": "Dan Mozena", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118420759176381924621/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-12T20:01:54.773353750Z", "text": "My appointment with One Medical was right on time. Waiting area is spacious with only one other patient. Lab work done on site - quick and easy. Love Dr. Buchwalter. She spends time with me, listens to my concerns and discusses options.", "author": "Carla Luggiero", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112948014098116582145/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-29T22:08:28.343678828Z", "text": "Visited this location for my annual physical yesterday and it was a great experience. I saw Rebecca Roth, NP, who had excellent bedside manner and was thorough. I never felt rushed throughout my visit. The receptionists were super nice as well! The office is modern and beautifully designed. It is also a super convenient location from the Metro Center station.\n\nThe best part is is I was done with my visit, flu shot, AND labs in under 30 minutes. This morning, I got my lab results and a message from my provider. Very quick turnaround time! They have always started on time here and are highly efficient. Thank you OM Metro Center!", "author": "Jay Lee", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113758456343582125650/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-31T14:23:35.319838616Z", "text": "I have had a few disappointing visit with Dr. Garfinkel. Last time, during a video session, he seemed quite distracted by a broken nail or cuticle. He eventually picked a nail clipper to trim whatever it was, on the camera.\nLast session, again he failed active listening and he talked to me with an infantilizing tone like my symptoms were excuses.\nI definitely won’t see Dr. Garfinkel again. I may actually move away from One Medical.", "author": "Shideh", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107603145567084564846/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Most patients report highly positive experiences with attentive, compassionate care and efficient service, though one review highlights a negative experience with a specific provider.", "about_highlight": "Our Metro Center office offers exceptional primary care for adults of all ages, including seniors on Medicare. We focus on building real relationships with patients and using technology to simplify every aspect of getting care. And we’re not just here for when you’re sick or injured. We can also help you meet physical and mental health goals, manage chronic illnesses, and live a happier, healthier life. Plus, you can expect improved coordination of specialty care through our affiliation with MedStar Health. Think of us as your home for healthcare.", "appointment_url": "https://health.amazon.com/onemedical/service-areas/dc?cta=omdc_office_gs_hl_dc_kst", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=17221255779361877481&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJR9pqP5G3t4kR6e0Bo-Mw_u4", "quality_missing": [], "search_keywords": ["primary care", "family doctor", "general practitioner", "annual physical", "checkup", "bác sĩ gia đình", "khám tổng quát", "nội khoa", "내과", "가정의학과", "家庭医生", "全科医生", "内科", "english", "korean", "한국어", "한인", "한국말", "everyday and preventative care", "physical exams (live well visits)", "women''s health", "mental health (mindset by one medical)", "lab work", "preventive", "mental health", "diagnostic", "most commercial plans", "medicare", "rachel barr", "pa-c", "jean-luc doan", "carolyn cabrey", "maren ketcham", "md", "rebecca roth", "np", "patricia evans", "kelly thelin", "alicia buchwalter", "daniel garfinkel", "deborah grorud"], "services_offered": [{"name": "Everyday and preventative care", "category": "Preventive", "description": "State-of-the art screening, disease prevention, and lifestyle advice. We diagnose and treat a wide spectrum of illnesses.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Physical exams (Live Well visits)", "category": "Preventive", "description": "Personalized physicals guided by questions in the app about your health priorities, from mental health to diet and sexual health.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Women''s health", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Birth control, sexual health, cancer screenings, menopause, preventive care, aging, gynecological problems, and more.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Women"}, {"name": "Mental health (Mindset by One Medical)", "category": "Mental Health", "description": "Services for depression, anxiety, insomnia, and more complex concerns through our suite of mental health services.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Lab work", "category": "Diagnostic", "description": "Drop-in lab services in all offices for labs ordered by One Medical providers and also outside labs on a drop-in basis.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}], "short_description": "One Medical Metro Center provides primary care for adults of all ages, including seniors on Medicare, with same/next-day appointments available and a focus on building real relationships and using technology to simplify care.", "google_website_url": "https://onemedical.com/locations/dc/1001g?y_source=1_MTA1Mzk0OTM4NS03MTUtbG9jYXRpb24ud2Vic2l0ZQ%3D%3D", "insurance_accepted": ["Most commercial plans", "Medicare"], "google_primary_type": "Medical Clinic", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": ["Rachel Barr", "Jean-Luc Doan", "Carolyn Cabrey", "Maren Ketcham", "Rebecca Roth", "Patricia Evans", "Kelly Thelin", "Alicia Buchwalter", "Daniel Garfinkel", "Deborah Grorud"], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "1001 G St NW Ste 200 East, Washington, DC 20001, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/101803381285790389453", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUo6EeMR7awtc0NWIHNLb6_lciEg4J8AG1ZgPdvRoxd_MExlEk=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "One Medical Primary Care Clinic - Metro Center"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/118372222166609939873", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUaC7012R_inqzRHpyb-TuOGvb9oqSqaDX2w5yFIZKhpQj8fbSOqg=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Tony Sheh"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/105833860239304340208", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVlX8n1mdvsESPEToOsEManVgJOxy2gC_mWXedTvoaIsHIPMto=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "ADDee"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/101803381285790389453", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUo6EeMR7awtc0NWIHNLb6_lciEg4J8AG1ZgPdvRoxd_MExlEk=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "One Medical Primary Care Clinic - Metro Center"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/101803381285790389453", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUo6EeMR7awtc0NWIHNLb6_lciEg4J8AG1ZgPdvRoxd_MExlEk=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "One Medical Primary Care Clinic - Metro Center"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-26T11:45:03.419069+00:00', 'one-medical-primary-care-clinic-metro-center', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.clinics ("id", "org_id", "name", "description", "address", "city", "state", "zip_code", "phone", "languages", "specialty", "is_telehealth_available", "metadata", "created_at", "slug", "claimed_by", "is_claimed") VALUES ('81d658fa-0727-4b2e-8059-1f3ed712af60', NULL, 'GW Primary Care - McPherson Square', 'Located in the heart of downtown DC at the intersection of 15th and L Streets Northwest, GW Primary Care - McPherson Square delivers quality primary care services. The office is part of the GW Medical Faculty Associates network, offering convenient hours including weekday appointments from 7:00 am to 7:00 pm and select Saturday hours. Patients can manage prescription refills through MyChart and schedule appointments online or by phone.', '1101 15th St NW, Washington, DC 20005', 'Washington', 'DC', '20005', '202-798-0100', ARRAY['English', 'Korean']::text[], 'Primary Care', FALSE, '{"fax": "202-379-3570", "images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/gw-primary-care-mcpherson-square-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/gw-primary-care-mcpherson-square-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/gw-primary-care-mcpherson-square-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/gw-primary-care-mcpherson-square-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/gw-primary-care-mcpherson-square-google-5.webp"], "rating": 2.5, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-18T22:20:48.031607049Z", "text": "Garrett Kneese was polite and friendly, and the nursing staff were pleasant, though the physical I received and the tests orders didn''t seem comprehensive, leaving me confused.  The experience getting to that appointment, was yet more frustrating, though.\nBooking was confusing from the start:  the online system showed availability that the scheduling staff said hadn''t been released, with no guidance on when it would be. I was told to check back online, which I did, eventually securing an appointment months out. When a staff member called mere days before the appointment to tell me it was a ''new patient visit'' rather than the annual physical I''d indicated, she suggested that the confusion could have been avoided had I booked by phone apparently unaware, or unconcerned, that a previous staff member had directed me to book online.  There was no clarity on whether labs would be done or whether I should fast. I took the gamble and fasted.  Labs were drawn, thankfully, though I was left with a nasty bruise for upwards of a week and no indication of what tests I was getting.  I expected a comprehensive metabolic panel and only a lipid panel was done.\n\nAfter the appointment, Dr. Kneese recommended a follow-up within a couple of weeks. I was told at checkout that scheduling wasn''t yet possible but that I''d hear from someone. I did not. Two MyChart messages over the course of two weeks went unanswered beyond an identical stock response. This included a message about abnormal lab results, which no one has addressed.\n\nUpdate:  After asking via an email to patient care for follow-up to the unanswered messages, I received a bunch of messages at once, none that responded to an issue with a specialist referral.\n\nAfter the scheduling/administrative failures, I had so hoped that the appointment itself and follow-up would be smooth sailing, but no dice.", "author": "Carl Budd", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103910726993319768364/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-10T19:11:29.639909905Z", "text": "I have been a patient of Khalil Nader for 9 years. Thanks to him and the all team there,  I feel better and healthy. Always good to talk  and listen to him. Best primary care doc I’ve ever had!!", "author": "ismail elabe", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105861382100965670746/reviews"}, {"date": "2024-12-31T15:20:54.323917Z", "text": "I''ve been a patient of this Primary Care for about 5 years now, and I have never written a review until my spectacular visit today. Whenever I walked in, I was well greeted by the front desk staff. They checked me in efficiently, and I waited less that 10 minutes to be seen. The next man that I saw look my weight and vital information and brought me back to the room while I waited for NP Khalil Nadar. He is an excellent doctor! I am a younger man, and the first time that I saw him a few years ago he sat me down and was extremely serious with me about monitoring and taking care of my blood pressure efficiently. Because of his dedication to me being as healthy as I can be, I took his advice seriously and I took the medication and monitored it per his directive. I was able to bring my blood pressure down to a normal/balanced level. And even when I stray away from his directives, it''s as if every visit I''ve had with him stays with me as a wise guide on my shoulder about what I should do to stay healthy. At our visit today, I was just overjoyed to see him again because I hadn''t seen him since leaving the country. I had some issues and concern and he addressed them with such warmth and genuine care. I feel so much better now that I have a course of action and steps I can take to feel so much healthier moving into 2025! The lady that took my blood was such a joy, and the entire process of this visit was extremely seamless, professional, and giving me such hope and strength for the best days ahead!!!!", "author": "Shanti Baba Ganesha", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103153758079258470631/reviews"}, {"date": "2024-09-13T16:26:26.879879Z", "text": "Absolutely awful service. The online appointment system doesn''t work, and when I called the phone number, I had to wait an hour to receive a callback. The doctor was available exactly one time within a two month period to do an annual physical, and they wouldn''t let me book a physical with any other healthcare provider until I kept pushing for another 15 minutes. They also denied a prescription refill with no notice until I had scheduled a new appointment. The receptionist put me on hold several times and clearly had no interest in helping patients. I cannot wait to be on new insurance so I never have to deal with these people again.", "author": "Bo Carlson", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100132644808330104706/reviews"}, {"date": "2023-11-29T17:18:17.061517Z", "text": "I would not recommend this facility.\n\nThe clinic was not responsive before my appointment. For example, they did not detail how I would have to go about picking up a prescription needed at my appointment, even though I contacted them many times. I found myself leaving the office in the midst of my appointment to visit the CVS around the corner. No details beforehand, I was left to troubleshoot as my appointment was occurring -- at my own expense it turns out.\n\nThe bill process is absurd. I left the appointment with a relatively low payment required, only to have that amount shoot up hundreds of dollars a week later.\n\nDon''t bother asking for an explanation for the increased cost; they won''t provide it. Truly a shameful way of providing \"care\".\n\nI will not be returning.", "author": "Claudia Butler", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112030394031127336477/reviews"}], "website": "https://gwdocs.com/locations/gw-primary-care-mcpherson-square", "location": {"latitude": 38.904025, "longitude": -77.03421329999999}, "services": ["Primary Care"], "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Downtown DC Location", "detail": "Located at 15th and L Streets NW, near McPherson Square metro.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Extended Hours", "detail": "Open Monday–Thursday 7:00 am–7:00 pm and select Saturdays 8:00 am–4:00 pm.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Online Appointment Booking", "detail": "Book an appointment with a primary care provider through the GW MFA website.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "MyChart Access", "detail": "Request prescription refills and manage health records via MyChart patient portal.", "category": "technology"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://gwdocs.com/locations/gw-primary-care-mcpherson-square", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": "https://gwdocs.com/profile?tid=178000326&field_gender_value=All&title=&tid_1=99000000", "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": true, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": false, "scout_query": "Korean speaking medical clinic in Washington, D.C.", "search_text": "primary care | family doctor | general practitioner | annual physical | checkup | bác sĩ gia đình | khám tổng quát | nội khoa | 내과 | 가정의학과 | 家庭医生 | 全科医生 | 内科 | english | korean | 한국어 | 한인 | 한국말", "google_types": ["medical_clinic", "health", "point_of_interest", "establishment"], "open_weekend": false, "rating_count": 217, "open_saturday": false, "quality_score": 92, "working_hours": {"friday": "7:00 AM – 6:00 PM", "monday": "7:00 AM – 7:00 PM", "sunday": "Closed", "tuesday": "7:00 AM – 7:00 PM", "saturday": "Closed", "thursday": "7:00 AM – 7:00 PM", "wednesday": "7:00 AM – 7:00 PM"}, "gallery_images": ["https://gwdocs.com/sites/g/files/zaskib551/files/styles/1920_x_variable/public/2023-08/mcphersonsq_exterior_16_2000x702.jpg?itok=sP-Vchm8"], "review_profile": {"rating": 2.5, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Mixed", "summary_quote": "Some staff are polite and friendly, while others are described as unhelpful or disinterested."}, {"theme": "Appointment Scheduling", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Patients frequently cite confusion and frustration with the online booking system and scheduling process."}, {"theme": "Clinical Expertise", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Providers like Khalil Nader are praised for their dedication and effectiveness in patient care."}, {"theme": "Billing Process", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Patients express dissatisfaction with unclear billing practices and unexpected cost increases."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Lack of clear communication about prescriptions and appointment details leads to frustration."}], "summary": "Patients report mixed experiences at GW Primary Care - McPherson Square, with praise for some providers like Khalil Nader but frustration over administrative issues, billing, and appointment scheduling.", "review_count": 217, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-18T22:20:48.031607049Z", "text": "Garrett Kneese was polite and friendly, and the nursing staff were pleasant, though the physical I received and the tests orders didn''t seem comprehensive, leaving me confused.  The experience getting to that appointment, was yet more frustrating, though.\nBooking was confusing from the start:  the online system showed availability that the scheduling staff said hadn''t been released, with no guidance on when it would be. I was told to check back online, which I did, eventually securing an appointment months out. When a staff member called mere days before the appointment to tell me it was a ''new patient visit'' rather than the annual physical I''d indicated, she suggested that the confusion could have been avoided had I booked by phone apparently unaware, or unconcerned, that a previous staff member had directed me to book online.  There was no clarity on whether labs would be done or whether I should fast. I took the gamble and fasted.  Labs were drawn, thankfully, though I was left with a nasty bruise for upwards of a week and no indication of what tests I was getting.  I expected a comprehensive metabolic panel and only a lipid panel was done.\n\nAfter the appointment, Dr. Kneese recommended a follow-up within a couple of weeks. I was told at checkout that scheduling wasn''t yet possible but that I''d hear from someone. I did not. Two MyChart messages over the course of two weeks went unanswered beyond an identical stock response. This included a message about abnormal lab results, which no one has addressed.\n\nUpdate:  After asking via an email to patient care for follow-up to the unanswered messages, I received a bunch of messages at once, none that responded to an issue with a specialist referral.\n\nAfter the scheduling/administrative failures, I had so hoped that the appointment itself and follow-up would be smooth sailing, but no dice.", "author": "Carl Budd", "rating": 2, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103910726993319768364/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-10T19:11:29.639909905Z", "text": "I have been a patient of Khalil Nader for 9 years. Thanks to him and the all team there,  I feel better and healthy. Always good to talk  and listen to him. Best primary care doc I’ve ever had!!", "author": "ismail elabe", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105861382100965670746/reviews"}, {"date": "2024-12-31T15:20:54.323917Z", "text": "I''ve been a patient of this Primary Care for about 5 years now, and I have never written a review until my spectacular visit today. Whenever I walked in, I was well greeted by the front desk staff. They checked me in efficiently, and I waited less that 10 minutes to be seen. The next man that I saw look my weight and vital information and brought me back to the room while I waited for NP Khalil Nadar. He is an excellent doctor! I am a younger man, and the first time that I saw him a few years ago he sat me down and was extremely serious with me about monitoring and taking care of my blood pressure efficiently. Because of his dedication to me being as healthy as I can be, I took his advice seriously and I took the medication and monitored it per his directive. I was able to bring my blood pressure down to a normal/balanced level. And even when I stray away from his directives, it''s as if every visit I''ve had with him stays with me as a wise guide on my shoulder about what I should do to stay healthy. At our visit today, I was just overjoyed to see him again because I hadn''t seen him since leaving the country. I had some issues and concern and he addressed them with such warmth and genuine care. I feel so much better now that I have a course of action and steps I can take to feel so much healthier moving into 2025! The lady that took my blood was such a joy, and the entire process of this visit was extremely seamless, professional, and giving me such hope and strength for the best days ahead!!!!", "author": "Shanti Baba Ganesha", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103153758079258470631/reviews"}, {"date": "2024-09-13T16:26:26.879879Z", "text": "Absolutely awful service. The online appointment system doesn''t work, and when I called the phone number, I had to wait an hour to receive a callback. The doctor was available exactly one time within a two month period to do an annual physical, and they wouldn''t let me book a physical with any other healthcare provider until I kept pushing for another 15 minutes. They also denied a prescription refill with no notice until I had scheduled a new appointment. The receptionist put me on hold several times and clearly had no interest in helping patients. I cannot wait to be on new insurance so I never have to deal with these people again.", "author": "Bo Carlson", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100132644808330104706/reviews"}, {"date": "2023-11-29T17:18:17.061517Z", "text": "I would not recommend this facility.\n\nThe clinic was not responsive before my appointment. For example, they did not detail how I would have to go about picking up a prescription needed at my appointment, even though I contacted them many times. I found myself leaving the office in the midst of my appointment to visit the CVS around the corner. No details beforehand, I was left to troubleshoot as my appointment was occurring -- at my own expense it turns out.\n\nThe bill process is absurd. I left the appointment with a relatively low payment required, only to have that amount shoot up hundreds of dollars a week later.\n\nDon''t bother asking for an explanation for the increased cost; they won''t provide it. Truly a shameful way of providing \"care\".\n\nI will not be returning.", "author": "Claudia Butler", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112030394031127336477/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients report mixed experiences at GW Primary Care - McPherson Square, with praise for some providers like Khalil Nader but frustration over administrative issues, billing, and appointment scheduling.", "about_highlight": "Located in the heart of downtown DC at the intersection of 15th and L Streets Northwest, GW Primary Care - McPherson Square delivers quality primary care services. The office is part of the GW Medical Faculty Associates network, offering convenient hours including weekday appointments from 7:00 am to 7:00 pm and select Saturday hours. Patients can manage prescription refills through MyChart and schedule appointments online or by phone.", "appointment_url": "https://gwdocs.com/profile?tid=178000326&field_gender_value=All&title=&tid_1=99000000", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=12252674510752810822&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJ3fEV0L-3t4kRRofn0Yw-Cqo", "quality_missing": ["insurance", "team_members"], "search_keywords": ["primary care", "family doctor", "general practitioner", "annual physical", "checkup", "bác sĩ gia đình", "khám tổng quát", "nội khoa", "내과", "가정의학과", "家庭医生", "全科医生", "内科", "english", "korean", "한국어", "한인", "한국말"], "services_offered": [{"name": "Primary Care", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "Quality primary care services for adults and families.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}], "short_description": "GW Primary Care - McPherson Square offers quality primary care in downtown DC with convenient hours and easy access.", "google_website_url": "https://gwdocs.com/locations/gw-primary-care-mcpherson-square", "google_primary_type": "Medical Clinic", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "1101 15th St NW, Washington, DC 20005, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/108980284740580063383", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWF-GziTREwrnOSEUZhREw7sXnscPb9E0kvVIYN2U9qTJCabDYj=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Nils Hünerfürst"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/113323220797459772594", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIwF-66X0_xtosPsbAQvTLjjkXAFoJ_1EFpCK2rzZmzyG8ERQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "GW Primary Care - McPherson Square"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/103744238119947294596", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUYPdLqcd-LTmYcd-3YaQ2rd4-bdCK9vmaI0uOcWJtFF7qQOqaj=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Brendan Collins"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/107608633802272777818", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJhNsIL3mBRTtiWpVbM851QbAHvpFUM3W3h-a7ZoBzWsNPV4g=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jessica Pickney"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/108514088843488433198", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWJlOzJTtBB5N19SeuUK1UCzU4PIvc4oCC_X1ditrA-yyEEyjan=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Marni Barnard"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-26T11:46:47.134029+00:00', 'gw-primary-care-mcpherson-square', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.clinics ("id", "org_id", "name", "description", "address", "city", "state", "zip_code", "phone", "languages", "specialty", "is_telehealth_available", "metadata", "created_at", "slug", "claimed_by", "is_claimed") VALUES ('c69892fd-a25a-4c07-8e40-e3372cce0baf', NULL, 'Paul Hom Asian Clinic', 'Founded in 1971, the Paul Hom Asian Clinic is a 501(c)(3) non-profit, student-run clinic committed to providing free, high-quality primary and specialty healthcare to underserved individuals — regardless of insurance status or background. We strive to create a welcoming environment where patients feel safe, respected, and connected to medical care that honors their identity and experiences. Through the generosity and kindness of our undergraduate volunteers, health professional students, and healthcare professionals from UC Davis, Kaiser, and Sutter Health, and more, we are able to offer high-quality, culturally and linguistically sensitive healthcare in English, Cantonese, Mandarin, Korean, Taishanese, Vietnamese, Hmong, Spanish, Mongolian, and Hindi. Together, we continue to strive to make healthcare accessible for all — and to carry forward our passion to serve. We are three student-run clinics -- PHAC, VN CARES, and HLUB, working together under the Paul Hom Asian Clinic to provide quality healthcare for all.', '6341 Folsom Blvd Sacramento, CA, 95819', 'Sacramento', 'CA', '95819', '916-318-8302', ARRAY['Hmong', 'Vietnamese', 'Spanish', 'Hindi', 'English', 'Korean', 'Mongolian', 'Cantonese', 'Taishanese', 'Mandarin']::text[], 'Primary Care', FALSE, '{"fax": "916-453-9725", "email": "triorg-leadership@paulhomclinic.org", "images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/paul-hom-asian-clinic-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/paul-hom-asian-clinic-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/paul-hom-asian-clinic-google-3.webp"], "rating": 5, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-01-31T20:31:21.372943281Z", "text": "I can’t say enough good things about the staff. Everyone is so polite, professional and patient. My parents were treated better than they have ever been treated at any other medical facility. They have been uninsured for two years and today they were able to receive full physical exams, blood work, EKGs and referral to specialists based on their health concerns. This clinic is a life saver for people who are unable to afford insurance, and I’m forever grateful for the students and doctors who are running the clinic.", "author": "Marwa Aljoher", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118006497404603157090/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-09-12T16:00:41.022755958Z", "text": "They''ve taken great care of my parents by providing them with excellent doctors and kind translators.", "author": "ThienVinh Nguyen", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115200648485479539801/reviews"}, {"date": "2020-02-13T05:48:51.260839Z", "text": "Amazing clinic! Everyone is super friendly with great doctors too! They provide a wide range of primary care services and even cancer screenings on sundays if needed! They have many translators that can help you even if you don''t speak english like Hmong, Vietnamese, or Chinese. Don''t hesitate to come in :D 10/10 I would highly recommend!", "author": "Matthew Tan", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101283167697104504337/reviews"}, {"date": "2018-01-26T08:03:51.340Z", "text": "There are many Chinese translators here, and the doctors are very patient in listening to your symptoms. Although there are many students who haven''t graduated yet studying there, and they also need to consult with the doctors, which takes a bit longer, it''s really a great place!", "author": "Jiaxin Pan", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115112645895133608464/reviews"}, {"date": "2022-01-21T18:59:25.357857Z", "text": "Excellent service.\nThe doctor was very professional.\nThe student intern had a very good service attitude.", "author": "Xiuya Zhao", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104375814434070550670/reviews"}], "website": "http://paulhomasianclinic.org/", "location": {"latitude": 38.5553746, "longitude": -121.42907149999998}, "services": ["Primary Care", "Cancer Screenings", "Cardiopulmonary", "Covered California", "Diabetes", "Hepatitis", "Neurology", "Ophthalmology", "Patient Assistance Program", "Psychiatry", "Women''s Health"], "insurance": {"notes": "The clinic provides free healthcare regardless of insurance status. No specific insurance networks are mentioned.", "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Free Quality Medical Service", "detail": "Provides free, high-quality primary and specialty healthcare to underserved individuals regardless of insurance status or background.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Culturally and Linguistically Sensitive Care", "detail": "Offers services in English, Cantonese, Mandarin, Korean, Taishanese, Vietnamese, Hmong, Spanish, Mongolian, and Hindi.", "category": "culture"}, {"title": "Student-Run Clinic", "detail": "Operated by dedicated undergraduate volunteers, health professional students, and healthcare professionals from UC Davis, Kaiser, and Sutter Health.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Saturday Clinic Hours", "detail": "Open every Saturday from 8:00 AM to 12:00 PM at 6341 Folsom Blvd, Sacramento.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Multiple Specialty Clinics", "detail": "Offers primary care, cancer screenings, cardiopulmonary, diabetes, hepatitis, neurology, ophthalmology, psychiatry, women''s health, and more.", "category": "care"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "http://paulhomasianclinic.org/", "appointment": {"booking_note": "To schedule an appointment, please call one of the numbers listed below, or contact us via email. Please leave a message with your name, phone number, reason for appointment, preferred times and dates (if applicable), and preferred language. A member of our team will reach out to you to confirm an appointment as soon as we can.", "appointment_url": null, "new_patient_note": "Bring to your appointment (if applicable): A list of ALL your current medications (including any traditional herbal medications or supplements) and any relevant medical records (e.g. X-rays, lab results, etc.).", "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": false, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": false, "scout_query": "Vietnamese speaking medical clinic in Sacramento, CA", "search_text": "primary care | family doctor | general practitioner | annual physical | checkup | bác sĩ gia đình | khám tổng quát | nội khoa | 내과 | 가정의학과 | 家庭医生 | 全科医生 | 内科 | hmong | vietnamese | tiếng việt | người việt | bác sĩ việt | spanish | hindi | english | korean | 한국어 | 한인 | 한국말 | mongolian | cantonese | chinese | 粤语 | 广东话 | tiếng quảng đông | taishanese | mandarin | 中文 | 普通话 | 国语 | tiếng trung | tiếng phổ thông | cancer screenings | cardiopulmonary | covered california | diabetes | hepatitis | neurology | ophthalmology | patient assistance program | psychiatry | women''s health | preventive | specialty | other", "google_types": ["medical_clinic", "health", "point_of_interest", "establishment"], "open_weekend": true, "rating_count": 9, "language_note": "Founded in 1971, the clinic is deeply rooted in serving the Asian community. It offers culturally and linguistically sensitive healthcare in English, Cantonese, Mandarin, Korean, Taishanese, Vietnamese, Hmong, Spanish, Mongolian, and Hindi. The clinic is named after Paul Hom and operates three student-run clinics (PHAC, VN CARES, HLUB) to meet the needs of diverse Asian and immigrant populations.", "open_saturday": true, "quality_score": 90, "working_hours": {"friday": "Closed", "monday": "Closed", "sunday": "Closed", "tuesday": "Closed", "saturday": "8:30 AM – 1:00 PM", "thursday": "Closed", "wednesday": "Closed"}, "gallery_images": ["https://static.wixstatic.com/media/50acdd_195cc89074324f6ea51baae111373ec1~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1280,h_730,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/50acdd_195cc89074324f6ea51baae111373ec1~mv2.jpg", "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/5929e9_32110e00f51540b6b1f895bef60fa756~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_639,h_700,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/5929e9_32110e00f51540b6b1f895bef60fa756~mv2.jpg", "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/5929e9_bc0236a32b5b49da9b0a7f860fe6457e~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_641,h_700,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/5929e9_bc0236a32b5b49da9b0a7f860fe6457e~mv2.jpg"], "review_profile": {"rating": 5, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 5, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Every reviewer highlights the polite, professional, and patient staff, with special mentions of doctors and student interns."}, {"theme": "Facility Environment", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Reviewers appreciate the clinic''s welcoming atmosphere and the availability of translators for non-English speakers."}, {"theme": "Treatment Outcomes", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients report receiving comprehensive care, including physical exams, blood work, and specialist referrals."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 4, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Many reviews commend the doctors for being patient listeners and the availability of translators in multiple languages."}, {"theme": "Clinical Expertise", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Reviewers consistently mention the high quality of medical care provided by both doctors and student interns."}], "summary": "Patients consistently praise the clinic for its professional and caring staff, excellent medical services, and support for uninsured individuals, with many highlighting the availability of translators and comprehensive care.", "review_count": 9, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-01-31T20:31:21.372943281Z", "text": "I can’t say enough good things about the staff. Everyone is so polite, professional and patient. My parents were treated better than they have ever been treated at any other medical facility. They have been uninsured for two years and today they were able to receive full physical exams, blood work, EKGs and referral to specialists based on their health concerns. This clinic is a life saver for people who are unable to afford insurance, and I’m forever grateful for the students and doctors who are running the clinic.", "author": "Marwa Aljoher", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118006497404603157090/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-09-12T16:00:41.022755958Z", "text": "They''ve taken great care of my parents by providing them with excellent doctors and kind translators.", "author": "ThienVinh Nguyen", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115200648485479539801/reviews"}, {"date": "2020-02-13T05:48:51.260839Z", "text": "Amazing clinic! Everyone is super friendly with great doctors too! They provide a wide range of primary care services and even cancer screenings on sundays if needed! They have many translators that can help you even if you don''t speak english like Hmong, Vietnamese, or Chinese. Don''t hesitate to come in :D 10/10 I would highly recommend!", "author": "Matthew Tan", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101283167697104504337/reviews"}, {"date": "2018-01-26T08:03:51.340Z", "text": "There are many Chinese translators here, and the doctors are very patient in listening to your symptoms. Although there are many students who haven''t graduated yet studying there, and they also need to consult with the doctors, which takes a bit longer, it''s really a great place!", "author": "Jiaxin Pan", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115112645895133608464/reviews"}, {"date": "2022-01-21T18:59:25.357857Z", "text": "Excellent service.\nThe doctor was very professional.\nThe student intern had a very good service attitude.", "author": "Xiuya Zhao", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104375814434070550670/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients consistently praise the clinic for its professional and caring staff, excellent medical services, and support for uninsured individuals, with many highlighting the availability of translators and comprehensive care.", "about_highlight": "Founded in 1971, the Paul Hom Asian Clinic is a 501(c)(3) non-profit, student-run clinic committed to providing free, high-quality primary and specialty healthcare to underserved individuals — regardless of insurance status or background. We strive to create a welcoming environment where patients feel safe, respected, and connected to medical care that honors their identity and experiences. Through the generosity and kindness of our undergraduate volunteers, health professional students, and healthcare professionals from UC Davis, Kaiser, and Sutter Health, and more, we are able to offer high-quality, culturally and linguistically sensitive healthcare in English, Cantonese, Mandarin, Korean, Taishanese, Vietnamese, Hmong, Spanish, Mongolian, and Hindi. Together, we continue to strive to make healthcare accessible for all — and to carry forward our passion to serve. We are three student-run clinics -- PHAC, VN CARES, and HLUB, working together under the Paul Hom Asian Clinic to provide quality healthcare for all.", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=1624089589698574635&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJYSwYjpHamoARK7lkheDsiRY", "quality_missing": ["insurance", "team_members", "appointment_url"], "search_keywords": ["primary care", "family doctor", "general practitioner", "annual physical", "checkup", "bác sĩ gia đình", "khám tổng quát", "nội khoa", "내과", "가정의학과", "家庭医生", "全科医生", "内科", "hmong", "vietnamese", "tiếng việt", "người việt", "bác sĩ việt", "spanish", "hindi", "english", "korean", "한국어", "한인", "한국말", "mongolian", "cantonese", "chinese", "粤语", "广东话", "tiếng quảng đông", "taishanese", "mandarin", "中文", "普通话", "国语", "tiếng trung", "tiếng phổ thông", "cancer screenings", "cardiopulmonary", "covered california", "diabetes", "hepatitis", "neurology", "ophthalmology", "patient assistance program", "psychiatry", "women''s health", "preventive", "specialty", "other"], "cultural_context": "Founded in 1971, the clinic is deeply rooted in serving the Asian community. It offers culturally and linguistically sensitive healthcare in English, Cantonese, Mandarin, Korean, Taishanese, Vietnamese, Hmong, Spanish, Mongolian, and Hindi. The clinic is named after Paul Hom and operates three student-run clinics (PHAC, VN CARES, HLUB) to meet the needs of diverse Asian and immigrant populations.", "services_offered": [{"name": "Primary Care", "category": "Primary Care", "description": "General medical care provided every Saturday.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": "Underserved individuals regardless of insurance status or background."}, {"name": "Cancer Screenings", "category": "Preventive", "description": "Specialty clinic for cancer screenings.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Cardiopulmonary", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Specialty clinic for heart and lung conditions.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Covered California", "category": "Other", "description": "Assistance with Covered California enrollment.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Diabetes", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Diabetes education and management.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Hepatitis", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Hepatitis screening and care.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Neurology", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Neurology consultations.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Ophthalmology", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Eye care services.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Patient Assistance Program", "category": "Other", "description": "Helps patients access medications and other assistance.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Psychiatry", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Mental health and psychiatric care.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Women''s Health", "category": "Specialty", "description": "Obstetric and gynecological care.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}], "short_description": "Free quality medical service for our community. A student-run clinic at UC Davis providing primary and specialty care every Saturday.", "google_website_url": "http://paulhomasianclinic.org/", "google_primary_type": "Medical Clinic", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "6341 Folsom Blvd, Sacramento, CA 95819, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/100144066784119489209", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW1CTycPllncU90GEI-VMoXU1t4Fd-5-9MGl19H46UgwfCiXWc=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Paul Hom Asian Clinic"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/100144066784119489209", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW1CTycPllncU90GEI-VMoXU1t4Fd-5-9MGl19H46UgwfCiXWc=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Paul Hom Asian Clinic"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/100144066784119489209", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW1CTycPllncU90GEI-VMoXU1t4Fd-5-9MGl19H46UgwfCiXWc=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Paul Hom Asian Clinic"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-26T09:51:07.990472+00:00', 'paul-hom-asian-clinic', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.clinics ("id", "org_id", "name", "description", "address", "city", "state", "zip_code", "phone", "languages", "specialty", "is_telehealth_available", "metadata", "created_at", "slug", "claimed_by", "is_claimed") VALUES ('820de2b5-52a8-4a23-9aa3-21be2e60eebf', NULL, 'Mongtinh M. Tran-Liu, Physician', 'No specific information about this physician is available from the provided source. The page is a generic VA San Diego maintenance page with no clinic or provider details.', '3350 La Jolla Village Dr, San Diego, CA 92161', 'San Diego', 'CA', '92161', '(858) 552-8585', ARRAY['English', 'Vietnamese']::text[], 'Hospital', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/mongtinh-m.-tran-liu-physician-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/mongtinh-m.-tran-liu-physician-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/mongtinh-m.-tran-liu-physician-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/mongtinh-m.-tran-liu-physician-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/mongtinh-m.-tran-liu-physician-google-5.webp"], "rating": 3.4, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-30T00:18:50.502872509Z", "text": "Minus some process frustration, I''ve had an overall good experience with this hospital and its staff in the many times I''ve been here, for either the ER or simple appointments. Obviously when something goes wrong the effects on the patient experience can snowball into something terrible really quickly, though, so I wish they had more real time admin support to be reviewing cases as they occur so the medical staff can catch issues in advance of them happening. Like when they forgot to assign post surgery pain management meds when I was inpatient and left me screaming in pain while they waited for the surgery team to respond to messages.  Or an ER attending forgot to put in a time sensitive referral when doing the discharge. You''d think those would be check boxes somewhere that admin could catch.", "author": "Sai Tamayo", "rating": 4, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106286219772518565568/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-10T06:18:42.030834916Z", "text": "I have been a social worker for 10 years and have accompanied many clients to hospital settings. This was by far the worse ER experience I have ever encountered at a hospital in San Diego County.\n\nWe were told escort services would assist us, but after waiting with no help while the patient was in severe pain, we had to locate staff ourselves. A security guard named Trey was helpful, but otherwise support was minimal.\n\nDespite visible distress including labored breathing, constant repositioning, and shaking, care was delayed, and communication was limited. The check-in area offered little privacy, and personal information could be easily overheard, raising serious concerns about how patient information is protected.\n\nAbout 90% of the staff were rude and dismissive. My professional experience and knowledge of patient advocacy were necessary to ensure our needs were addressed. Paperwork corrections required repeated follow-up.\n\nAt final discharge, staff handed over paperwork and said absolutely nothing, which felt unprofessional and impersonal. Improvements in communication, privacy, and professionalism are needed to ensure patients receive safe and respectful care.", "author": "Nicole", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115504200497938231469/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-06T05:02:01.264606446Z", "text": "The wait wasn''t bad. 2 hours from entering to being discharged. Staff was respectful. I do question the differences in care for females versus males that have the exact same reasoning for coming in. Please please protect patient confidentiality by lowering your voices when u discuss patient care. This is how I know I was treated differently (to include with medications) for the same exact reason the other patient came in for. Smh", "author": "P Family", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116835338894101329956/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-20T21:00:46.050336069Z", "text": "I had to go to the VA ER.\nFull disclosure- I am not an easy patient. I have taken out my IV and left the hospital more than a few times.  Yesterday was no exception. I''ve been a medical mystery for a very long time. I''m frustrated and I want answers.\nYesterday was no exception. I  said alot of things, that I regret. The staff was professional, but I knew that they would glad to be rid of me.\nThen, too my surprise, the doctor came back and approached me with a totally different attitude. I apologized for my combative attitude. He showed me grace that I''m not sure I deserved. He had heard me. He tested me for things that I had never considered. He pointed out things that I had never considered. Unfortunately, I''m still a medical mystery. I\n. But I will be forever grateful for the hope that they all gave me.\nIt was remarkable and a great reminder that I don''t have to fight everyone.", "author": "Kimberley Siple", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108907535720626734620/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-20T21:08:05.545141961Z", "text": "I went to the ER because I cut my finger with hedge trimmers. I was bottom of the triage list, but the nurse stitches me up very well. So well in fact, that I barely have a scar. It was a Saturday evening and I was out in about 2 hours. I wish I could remember my nurses name, but he was the bees knees and kept me chill.", "author": "aimee winstead", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113106009723264586323/reviews"}], "website": "http://www.sandiego.va.gov/", "location": {"latitude": 32.8757681, "longitude": -117.23266379999998}, "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "http://www.sandiego.va.gov/", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": null, "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": null, "online_booking_available": null, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": false, "scout_query": "Vietnamese speaking medical clinic in San Diego, CA", "search_text": "hospital | english | vietnamese | tiếng việt | người việt | bác sĩ việt", "google_types": ["hospital", "health", "point_of_interest", "association_or_organization", "service", "establishment"], "open_weekend": false, "rating_count": 136, "open_saturday": false, "quality_score": 75, "review_profile": {"rating": 3.4, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Several reviewers commend the staff for their professionalism and care, even in challenging situations."}, {"theme": "Administrative Processes", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Multiple reviews criticize administrative inefficiencies, such as delayed pain management and missed referrals."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Patients express dissatisfaction with communication, noting dismissive attitudes and lack of privacy during discussions."}, {"theme": "Patient Confidentiality", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Concerns about patient confidentiality were raised, with reviewers noting overheard conversations and lack of privacy."}, {"theme": "Treatment Outcomes", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "One reviewer praised the quality of care received, highlighting excellent stitching and minimal scarring."}], "summary": "Patients report mixed experiences, with some praising the professionalism and care of staff, while others highlight significant frustrations with administrative processes and communication.", "review_count": 136, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-30T00:18:50.502872509Z", "text": "Minus some process frustration, I''ve had an overall good experience with this hospital and its staff in the many times I''ve been here, for either the ER or simple appointments. Obviously when something goes wrong the effects on the patient experience can snowball into something terrible really quickly, though, so I wish they had more real time admin support to be reviewing cases as they occur so the medical staff can catch issues in advance of them happening. Like when they forgot to assign post surgery pain management meds when I was inpatient and left me screaming in pain while they waited for the surgery team to respond to messages.  Or an ER attending forgot to put in a time sensitive referral when doing the discharge. You''d think those would be check boxes somewhere that admin could catch.", "author": "Sai Tamayo", "rating": 4, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106286219772518565568/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-10T06:18:42.030834916Z", "text": "I have been a social worker for 10 years and have accompanied many clients to hospital settings. This was by far the worse ER experience I have ever encountered at a hospital in San Diego County.\n\nWe were told escort services would assist us, but after waiting with no help while the patient was in severe pain, we had to locate staff ourselves. A security guard named Trey was helpful, but otherwise support was minimal.\n\nDespite visible distress including labored breathing, constant repositioning, and shaking, care was delayed, and communication was limited. The check-in area offered little privacy, and personal information could be easily overheard, raising serious concerns about how patient information is protected.\n\nAbout 90% of the staff were rude and dismissive. My professional experience and knowledge of patient advocacy were necessary to ensure our needs were addressed. Paperwork corrections required repeated follow-up.\n\nAt final discharge, staff handed over paperwork and said absolutely nothing, which felt unprofessional and impersonal. Improvements in communication, privacy, and professionalism are needed to ensure patients receive safe and respectful care.", "author": "Nicole", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115504200497938231469/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-06T05:02:01.264606446Z", "text": "The wait wasn''t bad. 2 hours from entering to being discharged. Staff was respectful. I do question the differences in care for females versus males that have the exact same reasoning for coming in. Please please protect patient confidentiality by lowering your voices when u discuss patient care. This is how I know I was treated differently (to include with medications) for the same exact reason the other patient came in for. Smh", "author": "P Family", "rating": 3, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116835338894101329956/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-05-20T21:00:46.050336069Z", "text": "I had to go to the VA ER.\nFull disclosure- I am not an easy patient. I have taken out my IV and left the hospital more than a few times.  Yesterday was no exception. I''ve been a medical mystery for a very long time. I''m frustrated and I want answers.\nYesterday was no exception. I  said alot of things, that I regret. The staff was professional, but I knew that they would glad to be rid of me.\nThen, too my surprise, the doctor came back and approached me with a totally different attitude. I apologized for my combative attitude. He showed me grace that I''m not sure I deserved. He had heard me. He tested me for things that I had never considered. He pointed out things that I had never considered. Unfortunately, I''m still a medical mystery. I\n. But I will be forever grateful for the hope that they all gave me.\nIt was remarkable and a great reminder that I don''t have to fight everyone.", "author": "Kimberley Siple", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108907535720626734620/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-20T21:08:05.545141961Z", "text": "I went to the ER because I cut my finger with hedge trimmers. I was bottom of the triage list, but the nurse stitches me up very well. So well in fact, that I barely have a scar. It was a Saturday evening and I was out in about 2 hours. I wish I could remember my nurses name, but he was the bees knees and kept me chill.", "author": "aimee winstead", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113106009723264586323/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients report mixed experiences, with some praising the professionalism and care of staff, while others highlight significant frustrations with administrative processes and communication.", "about_highlight": "No specific information about this physician is available from the provided source. The page is a generic VA San Diego maintenance page with no clinic or provider details.", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=5675799254880074743&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJy6yiHdAG3IAR97uNw1l9xE4", "quality_missing": ["services", "working_hours", "insurance", "team_members", "appointment_url"], "search_keywords": ["hospital", "english", "vietnamese", "tiếng việt", "người việt", "bác sĩ việt"], "google_website_url": "https://www.va.gov/san-diego-health-care/", "google_primary_type": "Hospital", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "3350 La Jolla Village Dr, San Diego, CA 92161, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/107906513463056831060", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVhSStbi-TpwVsT9_kNBODDbjWpieHnh6w_MSMhEHiw9b7uDSE=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Eva Pataki"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/107906513463056831060", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVhSStbi-TpwVsT9_kNBODDbjWpieHnh6w_MSMhEHiw9b7uDSE=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Eva Pataki"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/107906513463056831060", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVhSStbi-TpwVsT9_kNBODDbjWpieHnh6w_MSMhEHiw9b7uDSE=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Eva Pataki"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/114357261623894493481", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUu0EasvkFXdXLzxO5EYrAc1TMs9NwmDVSiw5QGukjnIis6gCw9=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Miguel AP (UAP.Photography)"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/100717559531681516121", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUTEXWfoR5jw0KI3ngjNbftA3nUDXVuyWkoXBcelhzAx-GKgcDAcw=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Jonnee Johnson"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-26T11:56:49.61969+00:00', 'mongtinh-m-tran-liu-physician', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.clinics ("id", "org_id", "name", "description", "address", "city", "state", "zip_code", "phone", "languages", "specialty", "is_telehealth_available", "metadata", "created_at", "slug", "claimed_by", "is_claimed") VALUES ('5db9a440-7ee0-4bc3-b830-ce1757d813f1', NULL, 'Dao Medical Clinic', 'Viet T. Dao, MD, is a family medicine physician practicing as part of Sharp Community Medical Group in San Diego. With over a decade of experience since 2012, Dr. Dao provides comprehensive primary care services at his office located at 2363 Ulric St, Suite B. He is dedicated to serving the local community and accepts a wide range of insurance plans, including Medicare and self-pay options. Dr. Dao is recognized by grateful patients through Sharp''s Guardian Angel program.', '2363 Ulric St, Suite B, San Diego, CA 92111', 'San Diego', 'CA', '92111', '858-268-1747', ARRAY['Vietnamese']::text[], 'Family Medicine', FALSE, '{"fax": "858-268-4172", "images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/dao-medical-clinic-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/dao-medical-clinic-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/dao-medical-clinic-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/dao-medical-clinic-google-4.webp"], "rating": 1.5, "pricing": [{"name": "Self-Pay", "notes": "Self-pay option listed as accepted, no specific pricing mentioned.", "price": null, "category": "Self-Pay", "price_range": null}], "reviews": [{"date": "2026-03-24T18:06:34.270722316Z", "text": "Worst doctor’s office in San Diego – unprofessional, dismissive, and poorly managed!\n\nI had an appointment at Dao Medical Clinic and waited nearly an hour past my scheduled time — despite being the only patient there. The visit lasted less than 10 minutes and felt rushed. I did not feel heard, and my concerns were not properly addressed. I was referred to a specialist, but the referral was incomplete.\n\nFor over 2 weeks, I called multiple times and left messages but never received a callback. When I finally reached a staff member, I was told to contact my insurance myself — which my insurance confirmed was the clinic’s responsibility. I ended up going to the office multiple times in person because there was no follow-up, and the office was frequently closed during posted business hours.\n\nThe most concerning issue is the conduct of the front desk, managed by the doctor’s wife. Communication was consistently dismissive and unhelpful. At times, her tone was raised and came across as condescending. I also observed similar interactions with other patients, particularly Vietnamese and elderly individuals, where they were spoken to impatiently or left waiting unnecessarily. Meanwhile, staff appeared engaged in unrelated conversations rather than assisting patients.\n\nWhen I tried to resolve my situation, I was repeatedly told: “That’s all we can do.” When I asked for further clarification or help, I was told to “choose a different PCP” if I was not satisfied.\n\nIt has now been over a month, and I still have not been able to complete the referral process while my symptoms continued to worsen.\n\nOverall, the lack of communication, accountability, and basic patient care is deeply concerning. I would strongly recommend considering other providers if you value timely and respectful medical care.", "author": "kitkatishere", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100356355728990898125/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-01T18:01:44.742441176Z", "text": "They have the rudest staff, you would never believe. They have the worst customer service I have ever had an experienced in my entire life. I called to ask for the Medical Records Department fax number and the Lady would not give me the number correctly, she rushes the numbers down for me not to be able to write it down, instead she sent me to the medical records department without saying a word to me, when the phone call came back to her after medical records did not answer the system  transferred call back to the same employee. I told the same lady that answer my first call she was not very nice and professional she should not treat customers like that. she simply hung up on me... I could not go without advising you find another place to go we are all patients are treated with respect, dignity, as valuable clients. I was trying to help my sister out with this matter because she said she is never able to get a hold of anybody in the office to schedule an appointment, and when they do not answer her calls, they are not very polite. now I understand!", "author": "Dilva Casillas", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111873192985318608567/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-14T10:19:33.346066566Z", "text": "I am writing this review after a very serious and frightening experience involving my father. We sought care from this physician, but his condition was not properly recognized or managed. Shortly afterward, we had to rush to the emergency room, where doctors informed us that his condition had already become severe.\n\nThis situation could have led to much more serious consequences. As a family member, it was devastating to learn that earlier intervention might have made a difference.\n\nI take full responsibility for what I am saying here. I will be filing formal complaints with the appropriate medical boards and insurance providers to ensure this situation is reviewed thoroughly.\n\nFor anyone considering this physician, I strongly encourage you to carefully evaluate your options and advocate firmly for your health. Patient safety should always come first.", "author": "Sophia", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111521590803681103285/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-08-13T18:41:26.324012111Z", "text": "The worst medical experience of my life. The doctor is completely indifferent to patients — no examination, no tests, ignoring all listed health problems. Assistants are rude, unprofessional, and incompetent. It’s been 15 days and I still haven’t received my referrals. Terrible service and total disregard. SHARP Insurance shows the same irresponsibility. How can such a ‘medical’ facility be allowed to operate? I strongly advise everyone to stay away.", "author": "Elkhan Sarkhnov", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115475316517501362094/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-11-04T20:35:55.282025521Z", "text": "This review is a warning!!!!!Learn from my mistake and avoid this place. I made appointment for my mom. Upon arrival, the staff claimed they could not find their insurance information—a recurring issue I''ve since noticed in other reviews.When my mom tried to fix it, the staff was unhelpful and a female employee actually yelled at co worker \"Just let them go!\".\nShe was rude to all the patients, not just my parents. No one deserves this kind of treatment. The environment was hostile and unprofessional, leaving my mother scared. I''m just relieved my mother never ended up getting treated here. They have zero respect for patients. Do not waste your time or risk your peace of mind here.", "author": "Crystal Zhang", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105681656157987355793/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.sharp.com/doctors/viet-dao", "location": {"latitude": 32.7865659, "longitude": -117.1691874}, "services": ["Family Medicine"], "insurance": {"notes": "Sharp accepts most health insurance. Contact your insurance company to verify your specific plan. Self-pay option is listed.", "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": true, "accepted_networks": ["Aetna", "Blue Cross Blue Shield", "Cigna", "Health Net", "UnitedHealthcare", "Medicare", "Sharp Health Plan HMO", "Sharp Health Plan Covered California", "Sharp Health Plan POS"], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": true}, "highlights": [{"title": "Accepts Medicare", "detail": "Accepts Medicare Parts A and B, Medicare Advantage HMO plans, and Medigap plans.", "category": "insurance"}, {"title": "Self-Pay Accepted", "detail": "Self-pay option is available for patients without insurance.", "category": "insurance"}, {"title": "Vietnamese Speaking", "detail": "Dr. Dao speaks Vietnamese, providing language-concordant care.", "category": "culture"}, {"title": "Accepting New Patients", "detail": "Currently accepting new patients.", "category": "access"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://www.sharp.com/doctors/viet-dao", "appointment": {"booking_note": "Call to schedule an appointment.", "appointment_url": "tel:1-8582681747", "new_patient_note": "Accepting new patients.", "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": null, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": false, "scout_query": "Vietnamese speaking medical clinic in San Diego, CA", "search_text": "family medicine | family practice | primary care | bác sĩ gia đình | 가정의학과 | 家庭医学 | vietnamese | tiếng việt | người việt | bác sĩ việt | aetna | blue cross blue shield | cigna | health net | unitedhealthcare | medicare | sharp health plan hmo | sharp health plan covered california | sharp health plan pos | viet t. dao, md | family medicine physician", "google_types": ["doctor", "health", "point_of_interest", "establishment"], "open_weekend": false, "rating_count": 65, "team_members": [{"name": "Viet T. Dao, MD", "role": "Family Medicine Physician", "bio_snippet": "In practice since 2012. Male, age 64. Medical School: St. George''s University. Internship and Residency at Arrowhead Regional Medical Center. Received Guardian Angel recognitions from grateful patients.", "languages_spoken": ["Vietnamese"]}], "language_note": "Dr. Dao speaks Vietnamese, making him accessible to Vietnamese-speaking patients in the San Diego area.", "open_saturday": false, "quality_score": 95, "gallery_images": ["https://www.sharp.com/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fimages.ctfassets.net%2Fpxcfulgsd9e2%2F7uqLHkvVYYz0iNFMIX06XT%2Fbeff474d6839a678e55143f7bdd32d47%2Fdao_viet_79016_2022.jpg%3Fq%3D85%26f%3Dface%26fit%3Dfill%26fm%3Dwebp&w=1536&q=75"], "review_profile": {"rating": 1.5, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Compassionate care", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight compassionate care in their feedback."}, {"theme": "Friendly staff", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight friendly staff in their feedback."}, {"theme": "Clear explanations", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight clear explanations in their feedback."}, {"theme": "Strong results", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight strong results in their feedback."}], "summary": "Dao Medical Clinic has a 1.5 star Google rating from 65 Google reviews. Patients commonly mention compassionate care, friendly staff, clear explanations, strong results.", "review_count": 65, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-03-24T18:06:34.270722316Z", "text": "Worst doctor’s office in San Diego – unprofessional, dismissive, and poorly managed!\n\nI had an appointment at Dao Medical Clinic and waited nearly an hour past my scheduled time — despite being the only patient there. The visit lasted less than 10 minutes and felt rushed. I did not feel heard, and my concerns were not properly addressed. I was referred to a specialist, but the referral was incomplete.\n\nFor over 2 weeks, I called multiple times and left messages but never received a callback. When I finally reached a staff member, I was told to contact my insurance myself — which my insurance confirmed was the clinic’s responsibility. I ended up going to the office multiple times in person because there was no follow-up, and the office was frequently closed during posted business hours.\n\nThe most concerning issue is the conduct of the front desk, managed by the doctor’s wife. Communication was consistently dismissive and unhelpful. At times, her tone was raised and came across as condescending. I also observed similar interactions with other patients, particularly Vietnamese and elderly individuals, where they were spoken to impatiently or left waiting unnecessarily. Meanwhile, staff appeared engaged in unrelated conversations rather than assisting patients.\n\nWhen I tried to resolve my situation, I was repeatedly told: “That’s all we can do.” When I asked for further clarification or help, I was told to “choose a different PCP” if I was not satisfied.\n\nIt has now been over a month, and I still have not been able to complete the referral process while my symptoms continued to worsen.\n\nOverall, the lack of communication, accountability, and basic patient care is deeply concerning. I would strongly recommend considering other providers if you value timely and respectful medical care.", "author": "kitkatishere", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100356355728990898125/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-01T18:01:44.742441176Z", "text": "They have the rudest staff, you would never believe. They have the worst customer service I have ever had an experienced in my entire life. I called to ask for the Medical Records Department fax number and the Lady would not give me the number correctly, she rushes the numbers down for me not to be able to write it down, instead she sent me to the medical records department without saying a word to me, when the phone call came back to her after medical records did not answer the system  transferred call back to the same employee. I told the same lady that answer my first call she was not very nice and professional she should not treat customers like that. she simply hung up on me... I could not go without advising you find another place to go we are all patients are treated with respect, dignity, as valuable clients. I was trying to help my sister out with this matter because she said she is never able to get a hold of anybody in the office to schedule an appointment, and when they do not answer her calls, they are not very polite. now I understand!", "author": "Dilva Casillas", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111873192985318608567/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-14T10:19:33.346066566Z", "text": "I am writing this review after a very serious and frightening experience involving my father. We sought care from this physician, but his condition was not properly recognized or managed. Shortly afterward, we had to rush to the emergency room, where doctors informed us that his condition had already become severe.\n\nThis situation could have led to much more serious consequences. As a family member, it was devastating to learn that earlier intervention might have made a difference.\n\nI take full responsibility for what I am saying here. I will be filing formal complaints with the appropriate medical boards and insurance providers to ensure this situation is reviewed thoroughly.\n\nFor anyone considering this physician, I strongly encourage you to carefully evaluate your options and advocate firmly for your health. Patient safety should always come first.", "author": "Sophia", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111521590803681103285/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-08-13T18:41:26.324012111Z", "text": "The worst medical experience of my life. The doctor is completely indifferent to patients — no examination, no tests, ignoring all listed health problems. Assistants a