rdering lab tests and lack of helpfulness during appointments."}, {"theme": "Facility Environment", "mentions": 0, "sentiment": "Neutral", "summary_quote": "No specific mentions of the facility environment in the provided reviews."}], "summary": "Patients have mixed experiences at Pacific Women''s OB/GYN Medical Group, with some praising Dr. Chan''s compassionate care during procedures, while others express frustration with billing practices and poor communication.", "review_count": 43, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-05-28T01:56:31.030590620Z", "text": "Dr. Fung Yee Chan is truly the greatest doctor. I was incredibly nervous about an IUD replacement, after my first insertion was the most painful experience I’ve ever had. As soon as she learned that I was nervous, Dr. Chan was incredibly kind - explaining every step of the process as she went through the procedure so I knew exactly what to expect, allowing me to play music, and having ALL the right pain relief options prepped for me. The experience was infinitely better than my first insertion. Highly highly recommend seeing Dr. Chan!! I never thought I’d say this, but I’d happily get another IUD as long as she’s my doctor.", "author": "Michelle Park", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108737110881843981379/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-04-20T22:57:14.579048821Z", "text": "If I could give less than 1 star, I would. I should have never gone after reading the reviews. I went for an annual exam in January, which would''ve been fully covered by insurance, but due to their shady billing practices I ended up with an insane bill that my insurance didn''t even cover all of it. I have emailed 4 times and called their billing twice with ZERO response. Do not go here unless you want mediocre care, pay the highest possible price, and then get ghosted.", "author": "Julia Parry", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://w