lthy over the past three years.\n\nAnd English is not my strongest language. While I’m used to describing symptoms in English, I often find it more comfortable to explain in detail or ask deeper questions in Korean. That’s why I especially recommend Dr. Kim to other Korean-speaking parents in the area. She is warm, compassionate, and will take the time to explain things clearly.\n\nSometimes the wait time can be a bit long when there are many patients, even with an appointment. But aside from that, everything else has been excellent. The Providence app makes it easy to check records and send messages, and every single staff member we’ve encountered has been kind, caring, and professional.\nOur family is now moving out of state, so we unfortunately won’t be able to continue visiting this pediatrics. We’re truly sad to leave, because our experience here has been so positive. Thank you so much for everything over the years — I wholeheartedly recommend this pediatrics to others.", "author": "Ahyoung Cho", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116253336477199401514/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Patients consistently praise Dr. Hannah Kim and the staff at Providence Pediatrics - Redondo Beach for their friendly, professional, and responsive care, particularly highlighting the convenience for Korean-speaking families.", "about_highlight": "Providence Pediatrics - Redondo Beach, part of Providence Medical Institute, provides specialized pediatric care for children from birth to adolescence. Using the latest medical advances, the team offers comprehensive services including well-child visits, sick and urgent care, immunizations, developmental consultations, sport physicals, vision and hearing screenings, prenatal consults, and in-hospital newborn care. Additional areas of focus include nutritional counseling, integrative medicine, weight management, diabetes care, and behavioral health issues like ADHD.", "google_maps_url": "ht