es/doctors/debbie_lieu_od.jpg?v=1", "https://sceyes.org/images/doctors/mark_cheung_od.jpg?v=5"], "review_profile": {"rating": 4.8, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Compassionate care", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight compassionate care in their feedback."}, {"theme": "Friendly staff", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight friendly staff in their feedback."}, {"theme": "Clear explanations", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight clear explanations in their feedback."}, {"theme": "Comfortable visits", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight comfortable visits in their feedback."}], "summary": "Southern California Eye Institute (SCEI) has a 4.8 star Google rating from 353 Google reviews. Patients commonly mention compassionate care, friendly staff, clear explanations, comfortable visits.", "review_count": 353, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-06-04T21:52:33.574909669Z", "text": "They are great. Very friendly and kind behavior. I like their service Definitely recommend", "author": "Zakia Sultana", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107358476073695333010/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-05T22:13:28.150761228Z", "text": "Dr Popat didn''t just go through the routine but also educated me difference of glaucoma and cataract and other informative facts related to the checkup.\nShe is also not rushing.  She established a calm and professional atmosphere.  Front desk girl is very pleasant and helpful ☺️", "author": "M DeeDee De Leon", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102310239139553501650/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-14T03:54:27.068916614Z", "text": "The visit was easy in and out, Both the Dr. and Receptionist/Assistant were very helpful and pleasant to talk to, My Husband was the Patient and is a bit difficult to deal with, He was Happy with the glasses I chose for Him, I really appreciate both the Dr. and Assistant very much.", "author": "Elie Zindros", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114863745697229707549/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-16T18:59:26.197925541Z", "text": "I want to say a huge thank you to the medical staff. This was my first time here, and if I ever need help, I''ll definitely return to this clinic. They''re highly qualified, attentive, and knowledgeable.", "author": "Karine Oganisyan", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107989970288858807000/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-10-27T20:46:59.069584247Z", "text": "Dr. Nicole Fuerst (Ophthalmologist ) and her entire team are tops! I am Always treated so warmly by all. They have an optometry Department that is connected to them, with a super nice young lady named “Q” running the front, and she really goes above and beyond for patients and is very knowledgeable about your Health insurance and coverages. They would’ve gotten five stars but my last visit end of October I had to wait an unusually long time to see my ophthalmologist. I’m not sure, but they might’ve been understaffed that day.\nDr. Nicole is there only once per month, on Wednesday, so book well in advance if you want An appointment with her.", "author": "Jeanette St. John", "rating": 4, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100377896776655479641/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Southern California Eye Institute (SCEI) has a 4.8 star Google rating from 353 Google reviews. Patients commonly mention compassionate care, friendly staff, clear explanations, comfortable visits.", "about_highlight": "The Southern California Eye Institute (SCEI) is a leading ophthalmology center dedicated to ending blindness through advanced medical and surgical eye care, innovative research, and education. Under the leadership of Founding Director Dr. Rohit Varma, MD, MPH, SCEI provides compassionate, personalized care using state-of-the-art technologies including lasers, novel imaging devices, minimally invasive and complex surgical techniques. The institute''s team of board-certified ophthalmologists, glaucoma specialists, optometrists, and researchers are committed to restoring vision and transforming hope into reality for every patient. SCEI also houses the SCEI Vision Van, a mobile clinic bringing eye care to underserved communities, and offers specialized services across multiple locations in Los Angeles, Pasadena, and Bakersfield.", "appointment_url": "https://sceyes.org/appointment", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=16329520478326273669&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJJWbPS8THwoARhbYah1scnuI", "quality_missing": ["insurance"], "search_keywords": ["ophthalmology", "optometry", "optometrist", "eye doctor", "eye exam", "cataract", "lasik", "glasses", "nhãn khoa", "khám mắt", "bác sĩ mắt", "안과", "검안", "眼科", "配镜", "english", "russian", "korean", "한국어", "한인", "한국말", "cataract & refractive surgery", "cornea & external diseases", "glaucoma", "neuro-ophthalmology & strabismus", "ocular oncology", "oculo-facial plastics & reconstructive surgery", "pediatric ophthalmology", "retinal diseases", "rohit varma, md, mph", "founding director and glaucoma expert", "alena reznik, md", "glaucoma specialist", "david j. fuerst, md", "board certified ophthalmologist", "nicole m. fuerst, md", "jing wang, md", "umangi popat, od", "director of optometric services", "michael savetsky, md", "debbie lieu, od", "mark cheung, o.d.", "doctor of optometry"], "cultural_context": "SCEI emphasizes serving diverse communities and provides a Russian language version of its website (РУССКИЙ). The institute''s team includes providers with Asian surnames (Jing Wang, MD; Umangi Popat, OD; Debbie Lieu, OD; Mark Cheung, O.D.) suggesting multilingual and culturally responsive care. The SCEI Vision Van mobile clinic extends access to underserved populations.", "services_offered": [{"name": "Cataract & Refractive Surgery", "category": "Ophthalmology", "description": "Surgical removal of cataracts and correction of refractive errors using advanced techniques.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Cornea & External Diseases", "category": "Ophthalmology", "description": "Diagnosis and treatment of corneal conditions and diseases affecting the outer eye.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Glaucoma", "category": "Ophthalmology", "description": "Comprehensive glaucoma care including medical, laser, and surgical treatments such as ClearPath glaucoma surgery.", "is_featured": true, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Neuro-ophthalmology & Strabismus", "category": "Ophthalmology", "description": "Management of visual disturbances related to neurological conditions and eye misalignment.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Ocular Oncology", "category": "Ophthalmology", "description": "Diagnosis and treatment of eye tumors and cancers.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Oculo-facial Plastics & Reconstructive Surgery", "category": "Ophthalmology", "description": "Surgical repair and reconstruction of the eyelids, orbit, and facial structures around the eyes.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Pediatric Ophthalmology", "category": "Ophthalmology", "description": "Eye care for children including diagnosis and treatment of pediatric eye conditions.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}, {"name": "Retinal Diseases", "category": "Ophthalmology", "description": "Advanced diagnosis and treatment of retinal conditions such as macular degeneration, diabetic retinopathy, and retinal detachments.", "is_featured": false, "patient_fit": null}], "short_description": "Where hope is visible: Southern California Eye Institute is a premier ophthalmology center offering advanced, compassionate eye care from routine exams to complex surgeries, with locations in Los Angeles, Pasadena, and Bakersfield.", "google_website_url": "https://sceyes.org/", "google_primary_type": "Medical Clinic", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": ["Rohit Varma, MD, MPH", "Alena Reznik, MD", "David J. Fuerst, MD", "Nicole M. Fuerst, MD", "Jing Wang, MD", "Umangi Popat, OD", "Michael Savetsky, MD", "Debbie Lieu, OD", "Mark Cheung, O.D."], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "1300 North Vermont Avenue, Doctors Tower, Ste 101, Los Angeles, CA 90027, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/109903851568072779343", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVGiLoznYknXoifvZDtxW6FYNuzB09sHtC7XH2rU81y5hhHiUs=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA EYE INSTITUTE (SCEI)"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/109903851568072779343", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVGiLoznYknXoifvZDtxW6FYNuzB09sHtC7XH2rU81y5hhHiUs=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA EYE INSTITUTE (SCEI)"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/103678517493147229584", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXcLMPQaTl6mHycEN3TXIBcYO9XeKjGicXC9KH-RtIavENQIMJR=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Fernando Parker"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/109903851568072779343", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVGiLoznYknXoifvZDtxW6FYNuzB09sHtC7XH2rU81y5hhHiUs=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA EYE INSTITUTE (SCEI)"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/109903851568072779343", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVGiLoznYknXoifvZDtxW6FYNuzB09sHtC7XH2rU81y5hhHiUs=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA EYE INSTITUTE (SCEI)"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-26T13:25:55.751681+00:00', 'southern-california-eye-institute-scei', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.clinics ("id", "org_id", "name", "description", "address", "city", "state", "zip_code", "phone", "languages", "specialty", "is_telehealth_available", "metadata", "created_at", "slug", "claimed_by", "is_claimed") VALUES ('d5177c40-c3de-43e0-9589-ff7392f64b0e', NULL, 'UAMS Medical Center', 'UAMS Medical Center is a comprehensive academic medical center located in Little Rock, Arkansas, offering a full spectrum of inpatient and outpatient services across virtually all medical and surgical specialties. The facility is open 24/7 and serves as the primary teaching hospital for the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences, providing advanced care in areas such as emergency medicine, orthopedics, neurology, cardiology, oncology, maternal-fetal medicine, neonatology, pathology, anesthesiology, pulmonology, nephrology, infectious disease, and many others. Patients benefit from an integrated care environment that includes a robust patient portal (UAMS Health MyChart) for secure access to health information, appointment scheduling, prescription refills, and bill payment, as well as a price estimator tool to help understand potential costs. The medical center also has a clear respiratory virus protocol to ensure safety for all patients and staff, with options for phone or video visits when appropriate.', '4301 W. Markham St., Little Rock, AR 72205', 'Little Rock', 'AR', '72205', '501-686-8000', ARRAY['English']::text[], 'Hospital', FALSE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/uams-medical-center-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/uams-medical-center-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/uams-medical-center-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/uams-medical-center-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/uams-medical-center-google-5.webp"], "rating": 3.1, "reviews": [{"date": "2025-12-16T17:01:09.858580456Z", "text": "I have Meige syndrome and I had gotten to the point where I couldn''t swallow. The Urgent care I went to evaluated me and sent me to UAMS after calling my specialist in the movement disorder clinic. Upon arrival, the ER took me straight back with no waiting. After forming a team just for me and my condition, they began explaining how they would proceed. I was made comfortable to wait for a room. Within 36 hours I had a surgical procedure to place a feeding tube. All went well and came home the following Wednesday. I only have good things to say about this hospital and every staff member, doctor, and even the chaplain. At times it seems that they were slow to respond, but I realized the hospital is under staffed and were all working above and beyond. Thank you, UAMS. I would encourage all those who can to  make regular contributions to this place. It will help so many people in so many ways. This includes the doctors, nurses, students, and the patients who go to UAMS. The outpatients, inpatients, and the ER patients. Everyone gains when we all give together", "author": "Martha Hardin", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101762687083495218931/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-01T22:18:25.695296691Z", "text": "If I could give this place zero stars I would. The place isn’t very clean to start off with. They don’t even look at my husband’s chart all the way before making decisions. They keep giving him meds that I have told them he is no longer on. They don’t communicate with him at all, the only way we know what’s going on is by checking MyChart. He has been dealing with condition since he was born and knows what he needs. They refuse to listen. They put him through constant pain giving him multiple IV’s knowing that his veins will blow. He needs a port and they’re trying to midline’s. They have put him through so much pain and refuse to give pain meds, treating him like a druggy. They left an alcohol pad under the cotton ball and caused his arm to break out we guess from a chemical burn. They aren’t giving him the right amount of enzymes he’s supposed to take or all of his meds he’s supposed to take and not even giving them on time. If we could find another doctor for his condition we would. He shouldn’t be put through all this when he has to go there at least every 2 months. They should know what to do by now. Honestly this place should be shut down. The lack of care is ridiculous.", "author": "Breanna Ezell", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118264365502894443778/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-02T07:35:08.433845062Z", "text": "i waited in that damn waiting room for 9 whole hours!!!! The triage nurses had the damn audacity to have an attitude because i’m needing to see a dr!! how many staff do yall have in the back working 2? yall are neglecting patients!!!   St vincent’s wld never!! Do Not come here!!! Ever they will let u die in the waiting room!! i’m a nurse trust i’ve seen it!! rating 0.00001", "author": "DATRAP Queen", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100256533718201437229/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-22T17:10:51.485317001Z", "text": "1st to 2nd worse hospital experience of my life. Had a bullet wound and they did surgery a day or two before and expected me to walk and do pt with a 5mg hydrocodone in my body and a Tylenol. Do not go here what ever u do go to Baptist. And my mother is a nurse so I tried to be the sweetest as possible but them not listening to me 4-5 days straight I couldn’t even talk to the doctor or nurse I said just get me outta here I walked so far in  crutches and in pain. No one communicates so when you say there’s a problem you gotta explain to 5 different people not including the nurse the same thing over and over again.", "author": "Bigge Smells", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115418358364985390827/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-31T16:51:50.564106610Z", "text": "Dr Dana abulez delivered our baby Noah James Waid December 5th. Everything and everyone leading to delivery was great. The doctor had my wife pushing and doing great. Once the head was out she then ripped my boy out of my wife in an instant. I was not happy because she had a 3rd degree laceration that wasn’t necessary. I would also like to note the people who filed paperwork said I was an absent parent even though I was there the whole time. I understand being busy but this is not acceptable in any form or fashion and needs serious attention.", "author": "Nick Waid", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111506191886548640461/reviews"}], "website": "https://uamshealth.com/location/uams-medical-center/?utm_source=google&utm_medium=gmb&utm_campaign=clinical&utm_term=location&utm_content=profile&utm_specs=uams-medical-center", "location": {"latitude": 34.749314500000004, "longitude": -92.3205392}, "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Open 24/7", "detail": "The medical center is accessible around the clock for patient care.", "category": "access"}, {"title": "Comprehensive Specialty Care", "detail": "Offers a wide range of medical and surgical specialties including orthopedics, neurology, oncology, cardiology, and more.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Patient Portal & Online Tools", "detail": "UAMS Health MyChart provides secure 24-hour access to health information, appointment scheduling, and bill payment.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Price Estimator Tool", "detail": "Patients can use an online tool to estimate the cost of care.", "category": "technology"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://uamshealth.com/location/uams-medical-center/?utm_source=google&utm_medium=gmb&utm_campaign=clinical&utm_term=location&utm_content=profile&utm_specs=uams-medical-center", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": "https://uamshealth.com/make-an-appointment/", "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": true, "online_booking_available": true, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": true, "scout_query": "UAMS Medical Center in the United States", "search_text": "hospital | english", "google_types": ["medical_center", "hospital", "health", "point_of_interest", "service", "establishment"], "open_weekend": true, "rating_count": 606, "open_saturday": true, "quality_score": 77, "working_hours": {"friday": "Open 24 hours", "monday": "Open 24 hours", "sunday": "Open 24 hours", "tuesday": "Open 24 hours", "saturday": "Open 24 hours", "thursday": "Open 24 hours", "wednesday": "Open 24 hours"}, "gallery_images": ["https://uamshealth.com/wp-content/uploads/bis-images/55214/Bruce-fountain-630x473-cc.jpg"], "review_profile": {"rating": 3.1, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Staff Professionalism", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients appreciate the dedicated and compassionate care from doctors, nurses, and even the chaplain."}, {"theme": "Communication", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Multiple reviews highlight poor communication between staff and patients, with updates often only available through MyChart."}, {"theme": "Facility Environment", "mentions": 1, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Some patients report cleanliness issues and dissatisfaction with the hospital''s environment."}, {"theme": "Wait Times", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Long wait times, including one instance of a 9-hour wait, are a recurring complaint among patients."}, {"theme": "Pain Management", "mentions": 2, "sentiment": "Negative", "summary_quote": "Patients express frustration with inadequate pain management and perceived disregard for their discomfort."}], "summary": "Reviews for UAMS Medical Center are mixed, with some patients praising the specialized care and professionalism of staff, while others express frustration with communication issues, long wait times, and perceived neglect.", "review_count": 606, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2025-12-16T17:01:09.858580456Z", "text": "I have Meige syndrome and I had gotten to the point where I couldn''t swallow. The Urgent care I went to evaluated me and sent me to UAMS after calling my specialist in the movement disorder clinic. Upon arrival, the ER took me straight back with no waiting. After forming a team just for me and my condition, they began explaining how they would proceed. I was made comfortable to wait for a room. Within 36 hours I had a surgical procedure to place a feeding tube. All went well and came home the following Wednesday. I only have good things to say about this hospital and every staff member, doctor, and even the chaplain. At times it seems that they were slow to respond, but I realized the hospital is under staffed and were all working above and beyond. Thank you, UAMS. I would encourage all those who can to  make regular contributions to this place. It will help so many people in so many ways. This includes the doctors, nurses, students, and the patients who go to UAMS. The outpatients, inpatients, and the ER patients. Everyone gains when we all give together", "author": "Martha Hardin", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101762687083495218931/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-06-01T22:18:25.695296691Z", "text": "If I could give this place zero stars I would. The place isn’t very clean to start off with. They don’t even look at my husband’s chart all the way before making decisions. They keep giving him meds that I have told them he is no longer on. They don’t communicate with him at all, the only way we know what’s going on is by checking MyChart. He has been dealing with condition since he was born and knows what he needs. They refuse to listen. They put him through constant pain giving him multiple IV’s knowing that his veins will blow. He needs a port and they’re trying to midline’s. They have put him through so much pain and refuse to give pain meds, treating him like a druggy. They left an alcohol pad under the cotton ball and caused his arm to break out we guess from a chemical burn. They aren’t giving him the right amount of enzymes he’s supposed to take or all of his meds he’s supposed to take and not even giving them on time. If we could find another doctor for his condition we would. He shouldn’t be put through all this when he has to go there at least every 2 months. They should know what to do by now. Honestly this place should be shut down. The lack of care is ridiculous.", "author": "Breanna Ezell", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118264365502894443778/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-02T07:35:08.433845062Z", "text": "i waited in that damn waiting room for 9 whole hours!!!! The triage nurses had the damn audacity to have an attitude because i’m needing to see a dr!! how many staff do yall have in the back working 2? yall are neglecting patients!!!   St vincent’s wld never!! Do Not come here!!! Ever they will let u die in the waiting room!! i’m a nurse trust i’ve seen it!! rating 0.00001", "author": "DATRAP Queen", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100256533718201437229/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-22T17:10:51.485317001Z", "text": "1st to 2nd worse hospital experience of my life. Had a bullet wound and they did surgery a day or two before and expected me to walk and do pt with a 5mg hydrocodone in my body and a Tylenol. Do not go here what ever u do go to Baptist. And my mother is a nurse so I tried to be the sweetest as possible but them not listening to me 4-5 days straight I couldn’t even talk to the doctor or nurse I said just get me outta here I walked so far in  crutches and in pain. No one communicates so when you say there’s a problem you gotta explain to 5 different people not including the nurse the same thing over and over again.", "author": "Bigge Smells", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115418358364985390827/reviews"}, {"date": "2025-12-31T16:51:50.564106610Z", "text": "Dr Dana abulez delivered our baby Noah James Waid December 5th. Everything and everyone leading to delivery was great. The doctor had my wife pushing and doing great. Once the head was out she then ripped my boy out of my wife in an instant. I was not happy because she had a 3rd degree laceration that wasn’t necessary. I would also like to note the people who filed paperwork said I was an absent parent even though I was there the whole time. I understand being busy but this is not acceptable in any form or fashion and needs serious attention.", "author": "Nick Waid", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111506191886548640461/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "Reviews for UAMS Medical Center are mixed, with some patients praising the specialized care and professionalism of staff, while others express frustration with communication issues, long wait times, and perceived neglect.", "about_highlight": "UAMS Medical Center is a comprehensive academic medical center located in Little Rock, Arkansas, offering a full spectrum of inpatient and outpatient services across virtually all medical and surgical specialties. The facility is open 24/7 and serves as the primary teaching hospital for the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences, providing advanced care in areas such as emergency medicine, orthopedics, neurology, cardiology, oncology, maternal-fetal medicine, neonatology, pathology, anesthesiology, pulmonology, nephrology, infectious disease, and many others. Patients benefit from an integrated care environment that includes a robust patient portal (UAMS Health MyChart) for secure access to health information, appointment scheduling, prescription refills, and bill payment, as well as a price estimator tool to help understand potential costs. The medical center also has a clear respiratory virus protocol to ensure safety for all patients and staff, with options for phone or video visits when appropriate.", "appointment_url": "https://uamshealth.com/make-an-appointment/", "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=980427499144927317&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA", "google_place_id": "ChIJJz5GH8ql0ocRVdiOrp0tmw0", "quality_missing": ["services", "languages (non-default)", "insurance", "team_members"], "search_keywords": ["hospital", "english"], "short_description": "UAMS Medical Center is a 24/7 academic medical center in Little Rock, Arkansas, providing comprehensive specialty and primary care through a large, multidisciplinary team of providers.", "google_website_url": "https://uamshealth.com/location/uams-medical-center/?utm_source=google&utm_medium=gmb&utm_campaign=clinical&utm_term=location&utm_content=profile&utm_specs=uams-medical-center", "google_primary_type": "Medical Center", "provider_credentials": {"education": [], "providers": [], "residency": [], "years_in_practice": null, "board_certifications": [], "hospital_affiliations": [], "professional_memberships": []}, "google_business_status": "OPERATIONAL", "google_formatted_address": "4301 W Markham St, Little Rock, AR 72205, USA", "google_photo_attributions": [[{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/110442654651815910687", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUeWxiFuM1mRVw4DJFsYqLhA9jx42bE0rJXUjTLXXxo92tnRNI=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "UAMS Medical Center"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/105890743414491571457", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVCsZWVbAK_iNi9Qxi_iGpDCBa12nZpPHgvmM0aZAqLCFyFZg0vJQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Mason Mason"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/111131212365154471728", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV97vWfDSDPeslU7YMB_PTRzTZ1iB3UHHMcgFglVemmCrdXHB3RXw=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Moon Light"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/117561604641796296619", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUmq5xzSUrDHfR9SumOuG0MNWhiapgqaFUFUZEbBlhGJROwkys=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Hershel Thompson"}], [{"uri": "https://maps.google.com/maps/contrib/113757755772505088319", "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI8T5IDmbNwKRWBBlKkLo-k7cuNml0Yj1bHIuKVaR46fDupyQ=s100-p-k-no-mo", "displayName": "Yas Yas"}]]}'::jsonb, '2026-06-25T17:26:37.287235+00:00', 'uams-medical-center', NULL, FALSE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.clinics ("id", "org_id", "name", "description", "address", "city", "state", "zip_code", "phone", "languages", "specialty", "is_telehealth_available", "metadata", "created_at", "slug", "claimed_by", "is_claimed") VALUES ('0188dfdb-ff6e-4ff3-a393-690de79e58f7', NULL, 'UCSF Medical Center', 'UCSF Health is a leading academic medical center offering advanced specialty care, clinical trials, second opinions, and research innovation. We provide award-winning care across many regions in Northern California, with highly specialized experts delivering the very best treatments and promising new therapies. Our doctors are among the top in their field, and we offer access to new treatments through clinical trials not available elsewhere.', '505 Parnassus Ave, San Francisco, CA 94143', 'San Francisco', 'CA', '94143', '(415) 476-1000', ARRAY['Romanian', 'German', 'Italian', 'Korean', 'Chinese - Cantonese', 'Vietnamese', 'Telugu', 'Turkish', 'Portuguese', 'Chinese', 'Arabic', 'Hindi', 'Japanese', 'Chinese - Mandarin', 'Hokkien', 'Farsi', 'Hebrew', 'Assyrian', 'Nepali', 'Urdu', 'French', 'Russian', 'Taiwanese', 'Spanish', 'Burmese']::text[], 'Hospital', TRUE, '{"images": ["https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/ucsf-medical-center-google-1.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/ucsf-medical-center-google-2.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/ucsf-medical-center-google-3.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/ucsf-medical-center-google-4.webp", "https://smkyqdkuablxlexyuhgs.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/generated-images/generated-clinics/google-places/ucsf-medical-center-google-5.webp", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/live/ucsf/large-hero/homepage-1.jpg?h=1426&iar=0&w=2424", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/live/ucsf/large-hero/homepage-1.jpg?h=1426&iar=0&w=2424", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/shared/base/logos/ucsf-logo-small.svg?iar=0", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/live/ucsf/large-hero/homepage-1.jpg?h=1426&iar=0&w=2424&f=webp", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/live/ucsf/large-hero/mobile/homepage-1-mobile.jpg?h=1952&iar=0&w=1476&f=webp", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/live/ucsf/link-lists/homepage-linklist-1.jpg?h=1692&iar=0&w=1065&f=webp", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/live/ucsf/link-lists/i-need-to-explore-care.jpg?h=1692&iar=0&w=1065&f=webp", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/live/ucsf/link-lists/homepage-linklist-3.jpg?h=1692&iar=0&w=1065&f=webp", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/live/ucsf/large-hero/pritzker-adolescent-waiting-room-1200x800.jpg?h=800&iar=0&w=1200&f=webp", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/live/ucsf/video/871613367.jpg?h=810&iar=0&w=1440&f=webp", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/live/ucsf/video/928826600.jpg?h=810&iar=0&w=1440&f=webp", "https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/ucsfhealth1487c-ucsfplatfor7e11-prod0cc0-65a9/media/project/valcore/live/ucsf/video/987289369.jpg?h=810&iar=0&w=1440&f=webp"], "rating": 3.5, "reviews": [{"date": "2026-04-25T16:36:37.048611219Z", "text": "My husband and I wish to express the greatest appreciation to UCSF Medical Center members!!! They completed incredible work saving my husband'' life!!! The Medical Center has modern equipment and advanced methods for patients'' treatment. These methods jumped even over science fiction! The 21 st century neurological procedures allow to restore the functions of human brains!!! I was impressed by professionalism, kindness, and compassion of the Medical Center team members!!! Special thanks to Dr. Moreno, Dr. Ullal; Nurses Hannah, Kristin, and Michelle!!! These members of the team have such professional qualities as deep professional knowledge, ability to persuade patients, multicultural awareness, and the highest level of communication skills!!! Dear members of the UCSF Medical Center, thank you for completion the important mission: saving lives of people!!!", "author": "Tatiana Saengkeo", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114872109892837026083/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-24T14:32:01.655060100Z", "text": "Pioneering treatments and technology in a compassionate setting. Notable for neurology, transplantation, and women''s health. The Mission Bay hospital feels more like a luxury hotel, designed for patient and family comfort. Staff are collaborative and explain complex information clearly. Parking is challenging; use shuttles.", "author": "Henry", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105935242741699410821/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-19T17:39:05.864497225Z", "text": "Worst doctors and nurses.\nDoctor comes only once day.\nNurses don''t know anything when you ask questions.\nWill be ringing bell to use restroom. They won''t answer for an hour.\nLunch and dinner tray sitting  in room for over 2 hours.\nNow I know why they sid even know that someone  was dead on stairs for weeks . Because nurses don''t even check on patients", "author": "rita prasad", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112463501045222637710/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-27T09:39:06.351467699Z", "text": "If you can go to an other emergency room go there. My grandma fell and hit her head on the edge of a table, with a 8cm lacerations and alot of blood lost. We requested to the ambulance to bring us to kaiser but they brought us here. Right of the bat the waiting is overfilled and people sitting in the hallways and even in areas going to the bathroom.\n\nHour 1 just to do paper\nHour 2 no update\nHour 3 does xray\nHour 4 ekg\nHour 5 no update\nHour 6 told there is not eta for getting stitches or for the ct\nHour 7 still no update\nHour 8 asked for a doctor note for work, was told they need to hold off cause they need to see my grandma first.\n\nLong story short, no compassion, no update, no care for the patiences or their families.", "author": "PC D.", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100925582999172312200/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-03T17:02:36.168864345Z", "text": "World class doctors taking care of my dear friend.  The neurosurgeon is the top rated in the world.   The nursing staff and support staff were all so friendly and patient with answering all our questions as best they could.  Couldn’t be in better hands.  Very quiet, peaceful, and stress free environment in even the hardest of times.  Side benefit, the views, especially in the upper floors are absolutely stunning.", "author": "Diane Olsen", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103502832238357142002/reviews"}], "website": "https://www.ucsfhealth.org/", "location": {"latitude": 37.763104399999996, "longitude": -122.4578806}, "services": ["Emergency Department", "Urgent Care", "Express Care Video Visit", "Primary Care", "Specialty Care", "Second Opinions", "Clinical Trials"], "insurance": {"notes": null, "accepts_medicaid": null, "accepts_medicare": null, "accepted_networks": [], "out_of_network_available": null, "accepts_private_insurance": false}, "highlights": [{"title": "Ranked #1 Hospital in California", "detail": "UCSF Health is the No. 1 hospital in California (tied) and best in the state for cancer, geriatrics, neurology & neurosurgery, pulmonology and rheumatology.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Advanced Specialty Care", "detail": "Our doctors are among the top in their field and have highly specialized expertise and experience in managing complex care.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Clinical Trials Access", "detail": "We help patients get into research studies that allow access to new treatments not available anywhere else.", "category": "technology"}, {"title": "Second Opinions Available", "detail": "For help with a complex medical issue or difficult treatment decision, discuss your case with a leading expert from UCSF Health.", "category": "care"}, {"title": "Virtual Care (Telehealth)", "detail": "Express care video visits and virtual consultations are available for convenient access to care.", "category": "convenience"}, {"title": "Multiple Languages Available", "detail": "Providers are available who speak a wide range of languages including Spanish, Chinese-Mandarin, Cantonese, Vietnamese, and many more.", "category": "access"}, {"title": "Excellent Care Everywhere", "detail": "Award-winning care is offered in many regions of Northern California, so you can access the best of UCSF Health close to home.", "category": "access"}], "price_tier": "$$", "source_url": "https://www.ucsfhealth.org/", "appointment": {"booking_note": null, "appointment_url": "https://www.ucsfhealth.org/patients-visitors/appointments", "new_patient_note": null, "phone_booking_available": null, "online_booking_available": true, "free_consultation_available": null}, "open_sunday": true, "scout_query": "Korean speaking hospital in the United States", "search_text": "hospital | romanian | german | italian | korean | 한국어 | 한인 | 한국말 | chinese - cantonese | vietnamese | tiếng việt | người việt | bác sĩ việt | telugu | turkish | portuguese | chinese | mandarin | cantonese | 中文 | 普通话 | 国语 | 粤语 | 广东话 | 华人 | arabic | hindi | japanese | chinese - mandarin | hokkien | farsi | hebrew | assyrian | nepali | urdu | french | russian | taiwanese | spanish | burmese | emergency department | urgent care | express care video visit | primary care | specialty care | second opinions | clinical trials | emergency | telehealth | research", "google_types": ["hospital", "health", "point_of_interest", "service", "establishment"], "open_weekend": true, "rating_count": 360, "open_saturday": true, "quality_score": 92, "working_hours": {"friday": "Open 24 hours", "monday": "Open 24 hours", "sunday": "Open 24 hours", "tuesday": "Open 24 hours", "saturday": "Open 24 hours", "thursday": "Open 24 hours", "wednesday": "Open 24 hours"}, "review_profile": {"rating": 3.5, "source": "google", "themes": [{"theme": "Compassionate care", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight compassionate care in their feedback."}, {"theme": "Friendly staff", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight friendly staff in their feedback."}, {"theme": "Clear explanations", "mentions": 3, "sentiment": "Positive", "summary_quote": "Patients highlight clear explanations in their feedback."}], "summary": "UCSF Medical Center has a 3.5 star Google rating from 360 Google reviews. Patients commonly mention compassionate care, friendly staff, clear explanations.", "review_count": 360, "concern_themes": [], "positive_themes": [], "featured_reviews": [{"date": "2026-04-25T16:36:37.048611219Z", "text": "My husband and I wish to express the greatest appreciation to UCSF Medical Center members!!! They completed incredible work saving my husband'' life!!! The Medical Center has modern equipment and advanced methods for patients'' treatment. These methods jumped even over science fiction! The 21 st century neurological procedures allow to restore the functions of human brains!!! I was impressed by professionalism, kindness, and compassion of the Medical Center team members!!! Special thanks to Dr. Moreno, Dr. Ullal; Nurses Hannah, Kristin, and Michelle!!! These members of the team have such professional qualities as deep professional knowledge, ability to persuade patients, multicultural awareness, and the highest level of communication skills!!! Dear members of the UCSF Medical Center, thank you for completion the important mission: saving lives of people!!!", "author": "Tatiana Saengkeo", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114872109892837026083/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-24T14:32:01.655060100Z", "text": "Pioneering treatments and technology in a compassionate setting. Notable for neurology, transplantation, and women''s health. The Mission Bay hospital feels more like a luxury hotel, designed for patient and family comfort. Staff are collaborative and explain complex information clearly. Parking is challenging; use shuttles.", "author": "Henry", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105935242741699410821/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-19T17:39:05.864497225Z", "text": "Worst doctors and nurses.\nDoctor comes only once day.\nNurses don''t know anything when you ask questions.\nWill be ringing bell to use restroom. They won''t answer for an hour.\nLunch and dinner tray sitting  in room for over 2 hours.\nNow I know why they sid even know that someone  was dead on stairs for weeks . Because nurses don''t even check on patients", "author": "rita prasad", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112463501045222637710/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-01-27T09:39:06.351467699Z", "text": "If you can go to an other emergency room go there. My grandma fell and hit her head on the edge of a table, with a 8cm lacerations and alot of blood lost. We requested to the ambulance to bring us to kaiser but they brought us here. Right of the bat the waiting is overfilled and people sitting in the hallways and even in areas going to the bathroom.\n\nHour 1 just to do paper\nHour 2 no update\nHour 3 does xray\nHour 4 ekg\nHour 5 no update\nHour 6 told there is not eta for getting stitches or for the ct\nHour 7 still no update\nHour 8 asked for a doctor note for work, was told they need to hold off cause they need to see my grandma first.\n\nLong story short, no compassion, no update, no care for the patiences or their families.", "author": "PC D.", "rating": 1, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100925582999172312200/reviews"}, {"date": "2026-02-03T17:02:36.168864345Z", "text": "World class doctors taking care of my dear friend.  The neurosurgeon is the top rated in the world.   The nursing staff and support staff were all so friendly and patient with answering all our questions as best they could.  Couldn’t be in better hands.  Very quiet, peaceful, and stress free environment in even the hardest of times.  Side benefit, the views, especially in the upper floors are absolutely stunning.", "author": "Diane Olsen", "rating": 5, "source": "google", "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103502832238357142002/reviews"}]}, "review_summary": "UCSF Medical Center has a 3.5 star Google rating from 360 Google reviews. Patients commonly mention compassionate care, friendly staff, clear explanations.", "about_highlight": "UCSF Health is a leading academic medical center offering advanced specialty care, clinical trials, second opinions, and research innovation. We provide award-winning care across many regions in Northern California, with highly specialized experts delivering the very best treatments and promising new therapies. Our doctors are among the top in their field, and we offer access to new treatments through clinical trials not available elsewhere.", "a